erse_NFT_plagiarism_scandal\" title=\"Voiceverse NFT plagiarism scandal\">Voiceverse NFT plagiarism scandal</a></li></ul></div></div></td>\\n</tr><tr><td class=\"sidebar-below\">\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Glossary of artificial intelligence\">Glossary</a></td></tr><tr><td class=\"sidebar-navbar\"><span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333133064\" about=\"#mwt10\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Hlist/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1239400231\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" about=\"#mwt11\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Navbar/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'>.mw-parser-output .navbar{display:inline;font-size:88%;font-weight:normal}.mw-parser-output .navbar-collapse{float:left;text-align:left}.mw-parser-output .navbar-boxtext{word-spacing:0}.mw-parser-output .navbar ul{display:inline-block;white-space:nowrap;line-height:inherit}.mw-parser-output .navbar-brackets::before{margin-right:-0.125em;content:\"[ \"}.mw-parser-output .navbar-brackets::after{margin-left:-0.125em;content:\" ]\"}.mw-parser-output .navbar li{word-spacing:-0.125em}.mw-parser-output .navbar a>span,.mw-parser-output .navbar a>abbr{text-decoration:inherit}.mw-parser-output .navbar-mini abbr{font-variant:small-caps;border-bottom:none;text-decoration:none;cursor:inherit}.mw-parser-output .navbar-ct-full{font-size:114%;margin:0 7em}.mw-parser-output .navbar-ct-mini{font-size:114%;margin:0 4em}html.skin-theme-clientpref-night .mw-parser-output .navbar li a abbr{color:var(--color-base)!important}@media(prefers-color-scheme:dark){html.skin-theme-clientpref-os .mw-parser-output .navbar li a abbr{color:var(--color-base)!important}}@media print{.mw-parser-output .navbar{display:none!important}}</style></span><div class=\"navbar plainlinks hlist navbar-mini\"><ul><li class=\"nv-view\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template:Artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Template:Artificial intelligence\"><abbr title=\"View this template\">v</abbr></a></li><li class=\"nv-talk\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Template_talk:Artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Template talk:Artificial intelligence\"><abbr title=\"Discuss this template\">t</abbr></a></li><li class=\"nv-edit\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:EditPage/Template:Artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Special:EditPage/Template:Artificial intelligence\"><abbr title=\"Edit this template\">e</abbr></a></li></ul></div></td></tr></tbody></table>\\n\\n<!-- The lead section &#x26; other large sections are demarcated by comments to try and keep it a bit organised when edits are rapid. -->\\n<!-- DEFINITIONS -->\\n<p id=\"mwDQ\"><b id=\"mwDg\">Artificial intelligence</b> (<b id=\"mwDw\">AI</b>) is the capability of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer\" title=\"Computer\" id=\"mwEA\">computational systems</a> to perform tasks typically associated with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_intelligence\" title=\"Human intelligence\" id=\"mwEQ\">human intelligence</a>, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Learning\" title=\"Learning\" id=\"mwEg\">learning</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reason\" title=\"Reason\" id=\"mwEw\">reasoning</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Problem-solving\" title=\"Problem-solving\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwFA\">problem-solving</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perception\" title=\"Perception\" id=\"mwFQ\">perception</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision-making\" title=\"Decision-making\" id=\"mwFg\">decision-making</a>. It is a field of research in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Engineering\" title=\"Engineering\" id=\"mwFw\">engineering</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematics\" title=\"Mathematics\" id=\"mwGA\">mathematics</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_science\" title=\"Computer science\" id=\"mwGQ\">computer science</a> that develops and studies methods and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software\" title=\"Software\" id=\"mwGg\">software</a> that enable machines to perceive their environment and use <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mwGw\">learning</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligence\" title=\"Intelligence\" id=\"mwHA\">intelligence</a> to take actions that maximise their chances of achieving defined goals.<sup about=\"#mwt12\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4_1-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"1–4\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\" id=\"mwHQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwHg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwHw\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwIA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- APPLICATIONS -->\\n<p id=\"mwIQ\">High-profile <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Applications_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Applications of artificial intelligence\" id=\"mwIg\">applications of AI</a> include advanced <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Web_search_engine\" title=\"Web search engine\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwIw\">web search engines</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatbot\" title=\"Chatbot\" id=\"mwJA\">chatbots</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_assistant\" title=\"Virtual assistant\" id=\"mwJQ\">virtual assistants</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomous_vehicles\" title=\"Autonomous vehicles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwJg\">autonomous vehicles</a>, play and analysis in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strategy_game\" title=\"Strategy game\" id=\"mwJw\">strategy games</a> (e.g., <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chess\" title=\"Chess\" id=\"mwKA\">chess</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Go_(game)\" title=\"Go (game)\" id=\"mwKQ\">Go</a>), and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\" id=\"mwKg\">content generation</a> (e.g. images, audio, and videos).</p>\\n\\n<!-- GOALS AND TOOLS: SCOPE OF AI -->\\n<p id=\"mwKw\">The traditional goals of AI research include learning, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_reasoning\" title=\"Automated reasoning\" id=\"mwLA\">reasoning</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_representation\" title=\"Knowledge representation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwLQ\">knowledge representation</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_planning_and_scheduling\" title=\"Automated planning and scheduling\" id=\"mwLg\">planning</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_language_processing\" title=\"Natural language processing\" id=\"mwLw\">natural language processing</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_perception\" title=\"Machine perception\" id=\"mwMA\">perception</a>, as well as support for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotics\" title=\"Robotics\" id=\"mwMQ\">robotics</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt15\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Problems_of_AI_2-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Problems of AI\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Problems_of_AI-2\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"name\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"Problems of AI\\\\\"\"},\"1\":{\"wt\":\"This list of intelligent traits is based on the topics covered by the major AI textbooks, including: {{Harvtxt|Russell|Norvig|2021}}, {{Harvtxt|Luger|Stubblefield|2004}}, {{Harvtxt|Poole|Mackworth|Goebel|1998}} and {{Harvtxt|Nilsson|1998}}.\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Problems_of_AI-2\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwMg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwMw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwNA\">[</span>a<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwNQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> To reach these goals, AI researchers use techniques including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_space_search\" title=\"State space search\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwNg\">state space search</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_optimization\" title=\"Mathematical optimization\" id=\"mwNw\">mathematical optimisation</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Formal_logic\" title=\"Formal logic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwOA\">formal logic</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_network\" title=\"Artificial neural network\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwOQ\">artificial neural networks</a>, and methods based on <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statistics\" title=\"Statistics\" id=\"mwOg\">statistics</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Operations_research\" title=\"Operations research\" id=\"mwOw\">operations research</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economics\" title=\"Economics\" id=\"mwPA\">economics</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt18\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Tools_of_AI_3-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Tools of AI\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"html\":\"\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"name\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"Tools of AI\\\\\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Tools_of_AI-3\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwPQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwPg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwPw\">[</span>b<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwQA\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI also draws upon <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Psychology\" title=\"Psychology\" id=\"mwQQ\">psychology</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linguistics\" title=\"Linguistics\" id=\"mwQg\">linguistics</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophy_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Philosophy of artificial intelligence\" id=\"mwQw\">philosophy</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuroscience\" title=\"Neuroscience\" id=\"mwRA\">neuroscience</a>, and other fields.<sup about=\"#mwt22\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-4\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-4\" id=\"mwRQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwRg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwRw\">[</span>2<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwSA\">]</span></span></a></sup> Some companies, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI\" title=\"OpenAI\" id=\"mwSQ\">OpenAI</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_DeepMind\" title=\"Google DeepMind\" id=\"mwSg\">Google DeepMind</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms\" title=\"Meta Platforms\" id=\"mwSw\">Meta</a>, aim to create <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_general_intelligence\" title=\"Artificial general intelligence\" id=\"mwTA\">artificial general intelligence</a> (AGI)—AI that can complete nearly any <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cognition\" title=\"Cognition\" id=\"mwTQ\">cognitive</a> task at least as well as a human.<sup about=\"#mwt25\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-5\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-5\" id=\"mwTg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwTw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwUA\">[</span>3<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwUQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- HISTORY AND ETHICS -->\\n<p id=\"mwUg\">Artificial intelligence was founded as an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academic_discipline\" title=\"Academic discipline\" id=\"mwUw\">academic discipline</a> in 1956.<sup about=\"#mwt29\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dartmouth_workshop_6-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Dartmouth workshop\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Dartmouth_workshop-6\" id=\"mwVA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwVQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwVg\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwVw\">]</span></span></a></sup> The field went through multiple cycles of optimism throughout <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"History of artificial intelligence\" id=\"mwWA\">its history</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt30\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Succ1_7-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Succ1\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Succ1-7\" id=\"mwWQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwWg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwWw\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwXA\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt31\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Fund01_8-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Fund01\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Fund01-8\" id=\"mwXQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwXg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwXw\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwYA\">]</span></span></a></sup> followed by periods of disappointment and loss of funding, known as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_winter\" title=\"AI winter\" id=\"mwYQ\">AI winters</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt32\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-First_AI_Winter_9-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"First AI Winter\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-First_AI_Winter-9\" id=\"mwYg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwYw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwZA\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwZQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt33\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Second_AI_Winter_10-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Second AI Winter\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Second_AI_Winter-10\" id=\"mwZg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwZw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwaA\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwaQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> Funding and interest increased substantially after 2012, when <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphics_processing_unit\" title=\"Graphics processing unit\" id=\"mwag\">graphics processing units</a> (GPUs) started being used to accelerate neural networks, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_learning\" title=\"Deep learning\" id=\"mwaw\">deep learning</a> outperformed previous AI techniques.<sup about=\"#mwt34\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Deep_learning_revolution_11-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Deep learning revolution\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Deep_learning_revolution-11\" id=\"mwbA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwbQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwbg\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwbw\">]</span></span></a></sup> This growth accelerated further after 2017 with the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transformer_architecture\" title=\"Transformer architecture\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwcA\">transformer architecture</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt26\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEToews2023_12-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEToews2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEToews2023-12\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Toews\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEToews2023-12\" id=\"mwcQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwcg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwcw\">[</span>10<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwdA\">]</span></span></a></sup> In the 2020s, an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_boom\" title=\"AI boom\" id=\"mwdQ\">AI boom</a> coincided with advances in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\" id=\"mwdg\">generative AI</a>, which became widespread and allowed for the creation and modification of media. In addition to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_safety\" title=\"AI safety\" id=\"mwdw\">AI safety</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI#Concerns\" title=\"Generative AI\" id=\"mweA\">unintended consequences and harms</a> from the use of AI, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethics_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Ethics of artificial intelligence\" id=\"mweQ\">ethical concerns</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_aftermath_scenarios\" title=\"AI aftermath scenarios\" id=\"mweg\">AI\\'s long-term effects</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_impacts_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Environmental impacts of artificial intelligence\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwew\">environmental effects</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt35\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UN_13-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"UN\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-UN-13\" id=\"mwfA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwfQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwfg\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwfw\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existential_risk_from_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Existential risk from artificial intelligence\" id=\"mwgA\">potential existential risks</a> have prompted discussions of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regulation_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Regulation of artificial intelligence\" id=\"mwgQ\">AI regulation</a>.</p>\\n\\n<meta property=\"mw:PageProp/toc\" id=\"mwgg\" data-mw=\\'{\"autoGenerated\":true}\\'/></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"1\" id=\"mwgw\" aria-labelledby=\"Goals\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Goals\">Goals</h2></div>\\n<p id=\"mwhA\">The general problem of simulating (or creating) intelligence has been broken down into subproblems. These consist of specific traits or capabilities that researchers expect an intelligent system to display. The traits described below have received the most attention and cover the scope of AI research.<sup about=\"#mwt36\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Problems_of_AI_2-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Problems of AI\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"html\":\"\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"name\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"Problems of AI\\\\\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Problems_of_AI-2\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwhQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwhg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwhw\">[</span>a<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwiA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"2\" id=\"mwiQ\" aria-labelledby=\"Reasoning_and_problem-solving\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Reasoning_and_problem-solving\">Reasoning and problem-solving</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwig\">Early researchers developed algorithms that imitated step-by-step reasoning that humans use when solving puzzles or making logical <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deductive_reasoning\" title=\"Deductive reasoning\" id=\"mwiw\">deductions</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt44\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-14\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-14\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-14\" id=\"mwjA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwjQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwjg\">[</span>12<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwjw\">]</span></span></a></sup> By the late 1980s and 1990s, methods were developed for dealing with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Uncertainty\" title=\"Uncertainty\" id=\"mwkA\">uncertain</a> or incomplete information, employing concepts from <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Probability\" title=\"Probability\" id=\"mwkQ\">probability</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economics\" title=\"Economics\" id=\"mwkg\">economics</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt49\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-15\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-15\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-15\" id=\"mwkw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwlA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwlQ\">[</span>13<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwlg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwlw\">Many of these <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithm\" title=\"Algorithm\" id=\"mwmA\">algorithms</a> were insufficient for solving large reasoning problems because they experienced a \"combinatorial explosion\", meaning they become exponentially slower as the problems grow.<sup about=\"#mwt51\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Intractability_and_efficiency_and_the_combinatorial_explosion_16-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Intractability and efficiency and the combinatorial explosion\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Intractability_and_efficiency_and_the_combinatorial_explosion-16\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Intractability_and_efficiency_and_the_combinatorial_explosion-16\" id=\"mwmQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwmg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwmw\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwnA\">]</span></span></a></sup> Even humans rarely use the step-by-step deduction that early AI research could model. Humans solve most of their problems using fast, intuitive judgments.<sup about=\"#mwt56\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Psychological_evidence_of_the_prevalence_of_sub_17-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Psychological evidence of the prevalence of sub\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Psychological_evidence_of_the_prevalence_of_sub-17\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Psychological_evidence_of_the_prevalence_of_sub-17\" id=\"mwnQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwng\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwnw\">[</span>15<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwoA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwoQ\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reasoning_model\" title=\"Reasoning model\" id=\"mwog\">Reasoning models</a>, a type of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model\" title=\"Large language model\" id=\"mwow\">large language model</a> (LLM) trained to generate intermediate chains-of-thought, emerged in 2024 and allowed improved performance on complex problems in mathematics and coding.<sup about=\"#mwt59\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-18\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-18\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-18\" id=\"mwpA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwpQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwpg\">[</span>16<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwpw\">]</span></span></a></sup> These models can produce incorrect outputs or \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallucination_(artificial_intelligence)\" title=\"Hallucination (artificial intelligence)\" id=\"mwqA\">hallucinations</a>,\" unlike symbolic <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reasoning_system\" title=\"Reasoning system\" id=\"mwqQ\">reasoning systems</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt62\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Garcez_19-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Garcez\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Garcez-19\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Garcez-19\" id=\"mwqg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwqw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwrA\">[</span>17<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwrQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"3\" id=\"mwrg\" aria-labelledby=\"Knowledge_representation\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Knowledge_representation\">Knowledge representation</h3></div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwrw\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:General_Formal_Ontology.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwsA\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:General_Formal_Ontology.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/General_Formal_Ontology.svg/330px-General_Formal_Ontology.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e8/General_Formal_Ontology.svg/960px-General_Formal_Ontology.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"512\" data-file-height=\"512\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"300\" width=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.2\" id=\"mwsQ\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwsg\">An ontology represents knowledge as a set of concepts within a domain and the relationships between those concepts.</figcaption></figure>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwsw\">AI programs use knowledge to answer questions intelligently and make deductions about real-world facts.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwtA\">Formal <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_representation\" title=\"Knowledge representation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwtQ\">knowledge representation</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_engineering\" title=\"Knowledge engineering\" id=\"mwtg\">knowledge engineering</a> use <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_AI\" title=\"Symbolic AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwtw\">symbols</a> to represent words, concepts and things in the world.<sup about=\"#mwt120\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-20\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-20\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-20\" id=\"mwuA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwuQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwug\">[</span>18<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwuw\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt63\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-26\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Formal knowledge representations are used in content-based indexing and retrieval,{{Sfnp|Smoliar|Zhang|1994}} scene interpretation,{{Sfnp|Neumann|Möller|2008}} clinical decision support,{{Sfnp|Kuperman|Reichley|Bailey|2006}} knowledge discovery (mining \\\\\"interesting\\\\\" and actionable inferences from large [[database]]s),{{Sfnp|McGarry|2005}} and other areas.{{Sfnp|Bertini|Del Bimbo|Torniai|2006}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-26\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwvA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwvQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwvg\">[</span>c<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwvw\">]</span></span></a></sup> A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_base\" title=\"Knowledge base\" id=\"mwwA\">knowledge base</a> is a body of knowledge represented in a form that can be used by a program. An <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ontology_(information_science)\" title=\"Ontology (information science)\" id=\"mwwQ\">ontology</a> is the set of objects, relations, concepts, and properties used by a particular domain of knowledge.<sup about=\"#mwt81\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021272_27-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021272\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021272-27\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"272\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021272-27\" id=\"mwwg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwww\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwxA\">[</span>24<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwxQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> Formal knowledge has been studied extensively since the 1970s and researchers have developed formalisms for a wide variety of difficult domains.<sup about=\"#mwt84\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-33\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-33\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"A complete formal knowledge base needs to represent things such as objects, properties, categories, and relations between objects;&lt;ref>Representing categories and relations: [[Semantic network]]s, [[description logic]]s, [[Inheritance (object-oriented programming)|inheritance]] (including [[Frame (artificial intelligence)|frames]], and [[Scripts (artificial intelligence)|scripts]]): {{Harvtxt|Russell|Norvig|2021|loc=§10.2 &amp; 10.5}}, {{Harvtxt|Poole|Mackworth|Goebel|1998|pp=174–177}}, {{Harvtxt|Luger|Stubblefield|2004|pp=248–258}}, {{Harvtxt|Nilsson|1998|loc=chpt. 18.3}}&lt;/ref> situations, events, states, and time;&lt;ref>Representing events and time:[[Situation calculus]], [[event calculus]], [[fluent calculus]] (including solving the [[frame problem]]): {{Harvtxt|Russell|Norvig|2021|loc=§10.3}}, {{Harvtxt|Poole|Mackworth|Goebel|1998|pp=281–298}}, {{Harvtxt|Nilsson|1998|loc=chpt. 18.2}}&lt;/ref> causes and effects;&lt;ref>[[Causality#Causal calculus|Causal calculus]]: {{Harvtxt|Poole|Mackworth|Goebel|1998|pp=335–337}}&lt;/ref> knowledge about knowledge (what we know about what other people know);&lt;ref>Representing knowledge about knowledge: Belief calculus, [[modal logic]]s: {{Harvtxt|Russell|Norvig|2021|loc=§10.4}}, {{Harvtxt|Poole|Mackworth|Goebel|1998|pp=275–277}}&lt;/ref> [[default reasoning]] (things humans assume are true until they are told differently and will remain true even when other facts are changing);&lt;ref name=\\\\\"Default reasoning\\\\\">[[Default reasoning]], [[Frame problem]], [[default logic]], [[non-monotonic logic]]s, [[circumscription (logic)|circumscription]], [[closed world assumption]], [[abductive reasoning|abduction]]: {{Harvtxt|Russell|Norvig|2021|loc=§10.6}}, {{Harvtxt|Poole|Mackworth|Goebel|1998|pp=248–256, 323–335}}, {{Harvtxt|Luger|Stubblefield|2004|pp=335–363}}, {{Harvtxt|Nilsson|1998|loc=~18.3.3}}\\\\n(Poole &apos;&apos;et al.&apos;&apos; places abduction under \\\\\"default reasoning\\\\\". Luger &apos;&apos;et al.&apos;&apos; places this under \\\\\"uncertain reasoning\\\\\").&lt;/ref> and many other aspects and domains of knowledge.\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-33\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwxg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwxw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwyA\">[</span>d<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwyQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwyg\">The symbolic approach has difficulty with several problems: the breadth of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonsense_knowledge\" title=\"Commonsense knowledge\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwyw\">commonsense knowledge</a> (the set of atomic facts the average person knows is enormous),<sup about=\"#mwt134\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Breadth_of_commonsense_knowledge_34-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Breadth of commonsense knowledge\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Breadth_of_commonsense_knowledge-34\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Breadth_of_commonsense_knowledge-34\" id=\"mwzA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwzQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwzg\">[</span>30<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwzw\">]</span></span></a></sup> the sub-symbolic form of most commonsense knowledge (much of what people know is not represented as \"facts\" or \"statements\" they can express verbally),<sup about=\"#mwt135\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Psychological_evidence_of_the_prevalence_of_sub_17-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Psychological evidence of the prevalence of sub\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Psychological_evidence_of_the_prevalence_of_sub-17\" id=\"mw0A\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw0Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw0g\">[</span>15<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw0w\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_acquisition\" title=\"Knowledge acquisition\" id=\"mw1A\">knowledge acquisition</a> (the problem of obtaining knowledge for AI applications).<sup about=\"#mwt121\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-37\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-37\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Knowledge acquistion is among the reasons that [[expert system]]s proved to be inefficient for capturing knowledge.{{Sfnp|Newquist|1994|p=296}}{{Sfnp|Crevier|1993|pp=204–208}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-37\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mw1Q\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw1g\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw1w\">[</span>e<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw2A\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mw2Q\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_models\" title=\"Large language models\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mw2g\">Large language models</a> (and some other AI programs developed since 2012) do not require explicit, symbolic knowledge. They acquire knowledge by being trained on the combined text of millions of books and billions of websites. Modern AI can also learn about a domain by running experiments (as when <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaZero\" title=\"AlphaZero\" id=\"mw2w\">AlphaZero</a> learns game strategy by playing against itself). <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mw3A\">Machine learning</a> solves the problems of general knowledge, commonsense knowledge and knowledge acquisition, however this approach has struggled with accurate recall and valid reasoning.<link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:All_articles_with_unsourced_statements\" about=\"#mwt136\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mw3Q\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"citation needed\",\"href\":\"./Template:Citation_needed\"},\"params\":{\"date\":{\"wt\":\"August 2026\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'/><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:Articles_with_unsourced_statements_from_August_2026\" about=\"#mwt136\"/><sup class=\"noprint Inline-Template Template-Fact\" style=\"white-space:nowrap;\" about=\"#mwt136\" id=\"mw3g\"><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">[</span><i><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wikipedia:Citation_needed\" title=\"Wikipedia:Citation needed\"><span title=\"This claim needs references to reliable sources. (August 2026)\">citation needed</span></a></i><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">]</span></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"4\" id=\"mw3w\" aria-labelledby=\"Planning_and_decision-making\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Planning_and_decision-making\">Planning and decision-making</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mw4A\">An \"agent\" is any entity (artificial or not) that perceives and takes actions in the world. A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rational_agent\" title=\"Rational agent\" id=\"mw4Q\">rational agent</a> has goals or preferences and takes actions to make them happen.<sup about=\"#mwt137\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-38\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"Rational agent\\\\\" is general term used in [[economics]], [[philosophy]] and theoretical artificial intelligence. It can refer to anything that directs its behaviour to accomplish goals, such as a person, an animal, a corporation, a nation, or in the case of AI, a computer program.\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-38\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mw4g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw4w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw5A\">[</span>f<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw5Q\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt140\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021528_39-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021528\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021528-39\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"528\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021528-39\" id=\"mw5g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw5w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw6A\">[</span>33<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw6Q\">]</span></span></a></sup> In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_planning\" title=\"Automated planning\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mw6g\">automated planning</a>, the agent has a specific goal.<sup about=\"#mwt144\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-40\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-40\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-40\" id=\"mw6w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw7A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw7Q\">[</span>34<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw7g\">]</span></span></a></sup> In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_decision-making\" title=\"Automated decision-making\" id=\"mw7w\">automated decision-making</a>, the agent has preferences—there are some situations it would prefer to be in, and some situations it is trying to avoid. The decision-making agent assigns a number to each situation (called its \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Utility\" title=\"Utility\" id=\"mw8A\">utility</a>\") that measures how much the agent prefers it. For each possible action, it can calculate the \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expected_utility\" title=\"Expected utility\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mw8Q\">expected utility</a>\": the utility of all possible outcomes of the action, weighted by the probability that the outcome will occur. It can then choose the action with the maximum expected utility.<sup about=\"#mwt146\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-41\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-41\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-41\" id=\"mw8g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw8w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw9A\">[</span>35<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw9Q\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mw9g\">In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_planning_and_scheduling#classical_planning\" title=\"Automated planning and scheduling\" id=\"mw9w\">classical planning</a>, the agent knows exactly what the effect of any action will be.<sup about=\"#mwt148\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-42\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-42\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-42\" id=\"mw-A\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw-Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw-g\">[</span>36<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw-w\">]</span></span></a></sup> In most real-world problems, however, the agent may not be certain about the situation it is in (it is \"unknown\" or \"unobservable\") and it may not know for certain what will happen after each possible action (it is not \"deterministic\"). It must choose an action by making a probabilistic guess and then reassess the situation to see if the action worked.<sup about=\"#mwt150\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-43\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-43\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-43\" id=\"mw_A\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mw_Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw_g\">[</span>37<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mw_w\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \\n\\n<p id=\"mwAQA\">Alongside thorough testing and improvement based on previous decisions, having an explanation for why the agent took certain decisions is a way to build trust, especially when the decisions have to be relied upon.<sup about=\"#mwt152\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-44\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-44\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-44\" id=\"mwAQE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAQI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAQM\">[</span>38<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAQQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAQU\">In some problems, the agent\\'s preferences may be uncertain, especially if there are other agents or humans involved. These preferences may be learned (e.g., with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inverse_reinforcement_learning\" title=\"Inverse reinforcement learning\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAQY\">inverse reinforcement learning</a>), or the agent can seek information to improve them.<sup about=\"#mwt155\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-45\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-45\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-45\" id=\"mwAQc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAQg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAQk\">[</span>39<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAQo\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_value_theory\" title=\"Information value theory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAQs\">Information value theory</a> can be used to weigh the value of exploratory or experimental actions.<sup about=\"#mwt157\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-46\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-46\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-46\" id=\"mwAQw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAQ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAQ4\">[</span>40<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAQ8\">]</span></span></a></sup> The space of possible future actions and situations is typically <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intractably\" title=\"Intractably\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwARA\">intractably</a> large, so the agents must take actions and evaluate situations while being uncertain of the outcome.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwARE\">A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markov_decision_process\" title=\"Markov decision process\" id=\"mwARI\">Markov decision process</a> has a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Finite-state_machine\" title=\"Finite-state machine\" id=\"mwARM\">transition model</a> that describes the probability that a particular action will change the state in a particular way and a reward function that supplies the utility of each state and the cost of each action. A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reinforcement_learning#Policy\" title=\"Reinforcement learning\" id=\"mwARQ\">policy</a> associates a decision with each possible state. The policy could be calculated (e.g., by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Policy_iteration\" title=\"Policy iteration\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwARU\">policy iteration</a>), determined by a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heuristic\" title=\"Heuristic\" id=\"mwARY\">heuristic</a>, or learned.<sup about=\"#mwt159\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-47\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-47\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-47\" id=\"mwARc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwARg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwARk\">[</span>41<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwARo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwARs\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_theory\" title=\"Game theory\" id=\"mwARw\">Game theory</a> describes the rational behaviour of multiple interacting agents and is used in AI programs that make decisions involving other agents.<sup about=\"#mwt161\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-48\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-48\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-48\" id=\"mwAR0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAR4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAR8\">[</span>42<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwASA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"5\" id=\"mwASE\" aria-labelledby=\"Learning\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Learning\">Learning</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwASI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mwASM\">Machine learning</a> is the study of programs that can improve their performance on a given task automatically.<sup about=\"#mwt175\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-49\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-49\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-49\" id=\"mwASQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwASU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwASY\">[</span>43<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwASc\">]</span></span></a></sup> It has been a part of AI from the beginning.<sup about=\"#mwt162\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-52\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-52\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Alan Turing]] discussed the centrality of learning as early as 1950, in his classic paper \\\\\"[[Computing Machinery and Intelligence]]\\\\\".{{Sfnp|Turing|1950}} In 1956, at the original Dartmouth AI summer conference, [[Ray Solomonoff]] wrote a report on unsupervised probabilistic machine learning: \\\\\"An Inductive Inference Machine\\\\\".{{Sfnp|Solomonoff|1956}}\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-52\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwASg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwASk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwASo\">[</span>g<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwASs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwASw\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwAS0\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4d/Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png/500px-Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/4/4d/Supervised_and_unsupervised_learning.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x\" data-file-width=\"681\" data-file-height=\"308\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"158\" width=\"350\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.4\" id=\"mwAS4\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwAS8\">In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supervised_learning\" title=\"Supervised learning\" id=\"mwATA\">supervised learning</a>, the training data is labelled with the expected answers, while in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unsupervised_learning\" title=\"Unsupervised learning\" id=\"mwATE\">unsupervised learning</a>, the model identifies patterns or structures in unlabelled data.</figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwATI\">There are several kinds of machine learning: </p>\\n\\n<ul id=\"mwATM\"><li id=\"mwATQ\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unsupervised_learning\" title=\"Unsupervised learning\" id=\"mwATU\">Unsupervised learning</a> analyses a stream of data, finds patterns, and makes predictions without any other guidance.<sup about=\"#mwt179\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-53\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-53\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-53\" id=\"mwATY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwATc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwATg\">[</span>46<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwATk\">]</span></span></a></sup></li>\\n<li id=\"mwATo\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supervised_learning\" title=\"Supervised learning\" id=\"mwATs\">Supervised learning</a> requires labelling the training data with the expected answers, and comes in two main varieties: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statistical_classification\" title=\"Statistical classification\" id=\"mwATw\">classification</a> (where the program must learn to predict what category the input belongs in) and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regression_analysis\" title=\"Regression analysis\" id=\"mwAT0\">regression</a> (where the program must deduce a numeric function based on numeric input).<sup about=\"#mwt182\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Supervised_learning_54-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Supervised learning\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Supervised_learning-54\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Supervised_learning-54\" id=\"mwAT4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAT8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAUA\">[</span>47<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAUE\">]</span></span></a></sup></li>\\n<li id=\"mwAUI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reinforcement_learning\" title=\"Reinforcement learning\" id=\"mwAUM\">Reinforcement learning</a> is when the agent is rewarded for good responses and punished for bad ones. The agent learns to choose responses that are classified as \"good\".<sup about=\"#mwt185\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-55\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-55\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-55\" id=\"mwAUQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAUU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAUY\">[</span>48<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAUc\">]</span></span></a></sup></li>\\n<li id=\"mwAUg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transfer_learning\" title=\"Transfer learning\" id=\"mwAUk\">Transfer learning</a> is when the knowledge gained from one problem is applied to a new problem.<sup about=\"#mwt188\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-56\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-56\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-56\" id=\"mwAUo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAUs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAUw\">[</span>49<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAU0\">]</span></span></a></sup></li>\\n<li id=\"mwAU4\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_learning\" title=\"Deep learning\" id=\"mwAU8\">Deep learning</a> is a type of machine learning that runs inputs through biologically inspired <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_networks\" title=\"Artificial neural networks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAVA\">artificial neural networks</a> for all of these types of learning.<sup about=\"#mwt191\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-57\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-57\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-57\" id=\"mwAVE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAVI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAVM\">[</span>50<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAVQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></li></ul>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAVU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_learning_theory\" title=\"Computational learning theory\" id=\"mwAVY\">Computational learning theory</a> can assess learners by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_complexity\" title=\"Computational complexity\" id=\"mwAVc\">computational complexity</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sample_complexity\" title=\"Sample complexity\" id=\"mwAVg\">sample complexity</a> (how much data is required), or other notions of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optimization\" title=\"Optimization\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAVk\">optimisation</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt194\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-58\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-58\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-58\" id=\"mwAVo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAVs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAVw\">[</span>51<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAV0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<div style=\"clear:both;\" class=\"\" about=\"#mwt195\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwAV4\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Clear\",\"href\":\"./Template:Clear\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}\\'></div>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"6\" id=\"mwAV8\" aria-labelledby=\"Natural_language_processing\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Natural_language_processing\">Natural language processing</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwAWA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_language_processing\" title=\"Natural language processing\" id=\"mwAWE\">Natural language processing</a> (NLP) allows programs to read, write, and communicate in human languages.<sup about=\"#mwt199\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-59\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-59\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-59\" id=\"mwAWI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAWM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAWQ\">[</span>52<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAWU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Specific problems include <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_recognition\" title=\"Speech recognition\" id=\"mwAWY\">speech recognition</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_synthesis\" title=\"Speech synthesis\" id=\"mwAWc\">speech synthesis</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_translation\" title=\"Machine translation\" id=\"mwAWg\">machine translation</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_extraction\" title=\"Information extraction\" id=\"mwAWk\">information extraction</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_retrieval\" title=\"Information retrieval\" id=\"mwAWo\">information retrieval</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Question_answering\" title=\"Question answering\" id=\"mwAWs\">question answering</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt201\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-60\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-60\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-60\" id=\"mwAWw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAW0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAW4\">[</span>53<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAW8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAXA\">Early work, based on <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noam_Chomsky\" title=\"Noam Chomsky\" id=\"mwAXE\">Noam Chomsky</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_grammar\" title=\"Generative grammar\" id=\"mwAXI\">generative grammar</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Semantic_network\" title=\"Semantic network\" id=\"mwAXM\">semantic networks</a>, had difficulty with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Word-sense_disambiguation\" title=\"Word-sense disambiguation\" id=\"mwAXQ\">word-sense disambiguation</a><sup about=\"#mwt202\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-61\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"See {{Section link|AI winter|Machine translation and the ALPAC report of 1966\\\\n}}.\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-61\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwAXU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAXY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAXc\">[</span>h<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAXg\">]</span></span></a></sup> unless restricted to small domains called \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blocks_world\" title=\"Blocks world\" id=\"mwAXk\">micro-worlds</a>\" (due to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonsense_knowledge_(artificial_intelligence)\" title=\"Commonsense knowledge (artificial intelligence)\" id=\"mwAXo\">common sense knowledge problem</a><sup about=\"#mwt205\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Breadth_of_commonsense_knowledge_34-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Breadth of commonsense knowledge\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Breadth_of_commonsense_knowledge-34\" id=\"mwAXs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAXw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAX0\">[</span>30<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAX4\">]</span></span></a></sup>). British <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linguist\" title=\"Linguist\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAX8\">linguist</a> and philosopher <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Margaret_Masterman\" title=\"Margaret Masterman\" id=\"mwAYA\">Margaret Masterman</a> believed it was meaning and not grammar that was the key to understanding languages,<sup about=\"#mwt208\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-62\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-62\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-62\" id=\"mwAYE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAYI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAYM\">[</span>54<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAYQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> and that dictionaries and especially <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thesauri\" title=\"Thesauri\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAYU\">thesauri</a> should be the basis of computational language structure.<sup about=\"#mwt211\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-63\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-63\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-63\" id=\"mwAYY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAYc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAYg\">[</span>55<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAYk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAYo\">Modern deep learning techniques for NLP include <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Word_embedding\" title=\"Word embedding\" id=\"mwAYs\">word embedding</a> (representing words, typically as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vector_space\" title=\"Vector space\" id=\"mwAYw\">vectors</a> encoding their meaning),<sup about=\"#mwt212\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021856–858_64-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021856–858\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021856–858-64\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"856–858\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021856–858-64\" id=\"mwAY0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAY4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAY8\">[</span>56<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAZA\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transformer_(machine_learning_model)\" title=\"Transformer (machine learning model)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAZE\">transformers</a> (a deep learning architecture using an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attention_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Attention (machine learning)\" id=\"mwAZI\">attention</a> mechanism),<sup about=\"#mwt215\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDickson2022_65-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEDickson2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDickson2022-65\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Dickson\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDickson2022-65\" id=\"mwAZM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAZQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAZU\">[</span>57<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAZY\">]</span></span></a></sup> and others.<sup about=\"#mwt229\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-66\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-66\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-66\" id=\"mwAZc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAZg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAZk\">[</span>58<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAZo\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2019, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_pre-trained_transformer\" title=\"Generative pre-trained transformer\" id=\"mwAZs\">generative pre-trained transformer</a> (or \"GPT\") language models began to generate coherent text.<sup about=\"#mwt218\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEVincent2019_67-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEVincent2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2019-67\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Vincent\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2019\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2019-67\" id=\"mwAZw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAZ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAZ4\">[</span>59<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAZ8\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt221\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021875–878_68-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021875–878\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021875–878-68\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"875–878\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021875–878-68\" id=\"mwAaA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAaE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAaI\">[</span>60<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAaM\">]</span></span></a></sup> By 2023, these models were able to get human-level scores on the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bar_exam\" title=\"Bar exam\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAaQ\">bar exam</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SAT\" title=\"SAT\" id=\"mwAaU\">SAT</a> (Scholastic Assessment Test), <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GRE\" title=\"GRE\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAaY\">GRE</a> (Graduate Record Examination), and many other real-world applications.<sup about=\"#mwt224\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBushwick2023_69-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEBushwick2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBushwick2023-69\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Bushwick\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBushwick2023-69\" id=\"mwAac\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAag\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAak\">[</span>61<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAao\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"7\" id=\"mwAas\" aria-labelledby=\"Perception\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Perception\">Perception</h3></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAaw\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_perception\" title=\"Machine perception\" id=\"mwAa0\">Machine perception</a> is the ability to use input from sensors (such as cameras, microphones, wireless signals, active <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lidar\" title=\"Lidar\" id=\"mwAa4\">lidar</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sonar\" title=\"Sonar\" id=\"mwAa8\">sonar</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Radar\" title=\"Radar\" id=\"mwAbA\">radar</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tactile_sensor\" title=\"Tactile sensor\" id=\"mwAbE\">tactile sensors</a>) to deduce aspects of the world. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_vision\" title=\"Computer vision\" id=\"mwAbI\">Computer vision</a> is the ability to analyse visual input.<sup about=\"#mwt232\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-70\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-70\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-70\" id=\"mwAbM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAbQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAbU\">[</span>62<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAbY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAbc\">The field includes <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_recognition\" title=\"Speech recognition\" id=\"mwAbg\">speech recognition</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt233\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021849–850_71-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021849–850\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021849–850-71\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"849–850\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021849–850-71\" id=\"mwAbk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAbo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAbs\">[</span>63<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAbw\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image_classification\" title=\"Image classification\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAb0\">image classification</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt236\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021895–899_72-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021895–899\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021895–899-72\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"895–899\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021895–899-72\" id=\"mwAb4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAb8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAcA\">[</span>64<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAcE\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facial_recognition_system\" title=\"Facial recognition system\" id=\"mwAcI\">facial recognition</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Object_recognition\" title=\"Object recognition\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAcM\">object recognition</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt239\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021899–901_73-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021899–901\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021899–901-73\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"899–901\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021899–901-73\" id=\"mwAcQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAcU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAcY\">[</span>65<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAcc\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Motion_capture\" title=\"Motion capture\" id=\"mwAcg\">object tracking</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt242\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChallaMorelandMušickiEvans2011_74-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChallaMorelandMušickiEvans2011\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChallaMorelandMušickiEvans2011-74\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Challa\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Moreland\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"Mušicki\"},\"4\":{\"wt\":\"Evans\"},\"5\":{\"wt\":\"2011\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChallaMorelandMušickiEvans2011-74\" id=\"mwAck\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAco\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAcs\">[</span>66<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAcw\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotic_perception\" title=\"Robotic perception\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAc0\">robotic perception</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt245\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021931–938_75-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021931–938\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021931–938-75\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"931–938\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021931–938-75\" id=\"mwAc4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAc8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAdA\">[</span>67<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAdE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"8\" id=\"mwAdI\" aria-labelledby=\"Social_intelligence\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Social_intelligence\">Social intelligence</h3></div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwAdM\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwAdQ\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg/250px-Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/2/27/Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg/500px-Kismet-IMG_6007-gradient.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"5500\" data-file-height=\"3667\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"167\" width=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" id=\"mwAdU\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwAdY\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kismet_(robot)\" title=\"Kismet (robot)\" id=\"mwAdc\">Kismet</a>, a robot head made in the 1990s, is a machine that can recognise and simulate emotions.<sup about=\"#mwt248\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMIT_AIL2014_76-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMIT AIL2014\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMIT_AIL2014-76\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"MIT AIL\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2014\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMIT_AIL2014-76\" id=\"mwAdg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAdk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAdo\">[</span>68<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAds\">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAdw\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Affective_computing\" title=\"Affective computing\" id=\"mwAd0\">Affective computing</a> is a field that comprises systems that recognise, interpret, process, or simulate human <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Affect_(psychology)\" title=\"Affect (psychology)\" id=\"mwAd4\">affect</a> (feeling, emotion, and mood).<sup about=\"#mwt255\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-77\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-77\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-77\" id=\"mwAd8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAeA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAeE\">[</span>69<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAeI\">]</span></span></a></sup> For example, some <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_assistant\" title=\"Virtual assistant\" id=\"mwAeM\">virtual assistants</a> are programmed to speak conversationally or even banter humorously; it makes them appear more sensitive to the emotional dynamics of human interaction, or to otherwise facilitate <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human–computer_interaction\" title=\"Human–computer interaction\" id=\"mwAeQ\">human–computer interaction</a>.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAeU\">However, this tends to give <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naïve\" title=\"Naïve\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAeY\">naïve</a> users an unrealistic conception of the intelligence of existing computer agents.<sup about=\"#mwt256\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWaddell2018_78-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEWaddell2018\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWaddell2018-78\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Waddell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2018\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWaddell2018-78\" id=\"mwAec\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAeg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAek\">[</span>70<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAeo\">]</span></span></a></sup> Moderate successes related to affective computing include textual <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentiment_analysis\" title=\"Sentiment analysis\" id=\"mwAes\">sentiment analysis</a> and, more recently, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multimodal_sentiment_analysis\" title=\"Multimodal sentiment analysis\" id=\"mwAew\">multimodal sentiment analysis</a>, wherein AI classifies the effects displayed by a videotaped subject.<sup about=\"#mwt259\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPoriaCambriaBajpaiHussain2017_79-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEPoriaCambriaBajpaiHussain2017\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPoriaCambriaBajpaiHussain2017-79\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Poria\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Cambria\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"Bajpai \"},\"4\":{\"wt\":\"Hussain\"},\"5\":{\"wt\":\"2017\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPoriaCambriaBajpaiHussain2017-79\" id=\"mwAe0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAe4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAe8\">[</span>71<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAfA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"9\" id=\"mwAfE\" aria-labelledby=\"General_intelligence\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"General_intelligence\">General intelligence</h3></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAfI\">A machine with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_general_intelligence\" title=\"Artificial general intelligence\" id=\"mwAfM\">artificial general intelligence</a> (AGI) would be able to solve a wide variety of problems with breadth and versatility similar to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_intelligence\" title=\"Human intelligence\" id=\"mwAfQ\">human intelligence</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt267\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Artificial_general_intelligence_80-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Artificial general intelligence\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Artificial_general_intelligence-80\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Artificial_general_intelligence-80\" id=\"mwAfU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAfY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAfc\">[</span>72<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAfg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"10\" id=\"mwAfk\" aria-labelledby=\"Techniques\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Techniques\">Techniques</h2></div>\\n<p id=\"mwAfo\">AI research uses a wide variety of techniques to accomplish the goals above.<sup about=\"#mwt268\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Tools_of_AI_3-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Tools of AI\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Tools_of_AI-3\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"name\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"Tools of AI\\\\\"\"},\"1\":{\"wt\":\"This list of tools is based on the topics covered by the major AI textbooks, including: {{Harvtxt|Russell|Norvig|2021}}, {{Harvtxt|Luger|Stubblefield|2004}}, {{Harvtxt|Poole|Mackworth|Goebel|1998}} and {{Harvtxt|Nilsson|1998}}.\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Tools_of_AI-3\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwAfs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAfw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAf0\">[</span>b<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAf4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"11\" id=\"mwAf8\" aria-labelledby=\"Search_and_optimisation\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Search_and_optimisation\">Search and optimisation</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwAgA\">There are two different kinds of search used in AI: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_space_search\" title=\"State space search\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAgE\">state space search</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Local_search_(optimization)\" title=\"Local search (optimization)\" id=\"mwAgI\">local search</a>:</p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"12\" id=\"mwAgM\" aria-labelledby=\"State_space_search\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"State_space_search\">State space search</h4></div>\\n<p id=\"mwAgQ\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/State_space_search\" title=\"State space search\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAgU\">State space search</a> searches through a tree of possible states to try to find a goal state.<sup about=\"#mwt275\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-81\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-81\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-81\" id=\"mwAgY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAgc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAgg\">[</span>73<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAgk\">]</span></span></a></sup> For example, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_planning_and_scheduling\" title=\"Automated planning and scheduling\" id=\"mwAgo\">planning</a> algorithms search through trees of goals and subgoals, attempting to find a path to a target goal, a process called <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Means-ends_analysis\" title=\"Means-ends analysis\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAgs\">means-ends analysis</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt271\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021sect._11.2_82-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021sect. 11.2\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021sect._11.2-82\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"loc\":{\"wt\":\"sect. 11.2\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021sect._11.2-82\" id=\"mwAgw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAg0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAg4\">[</span>74<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAg8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAhA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brute_force_search\" title=\"Brute force search\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAhE\">Simple exhaustive searches</a><sup about=\"#mwt280\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-83\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-83\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-83\" id=\"mwAhI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAhM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAhQ\">[</span>75<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAhU\">]</span></span></a></sup> are rarely sufficient for most real-world problems: the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Search_algorithm\" title=\"Search algorithm\" id=\"mwAhY\">search space</a> (the number of places to search) quickly grows to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Astronomically_large\" title=\"Astronomically large\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAhc\">astronomical numbers</a>. The result is a search that is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computation_time\" title=\"Computation time\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAhg\">too slow</a> or never completes.<sup about=\"#mwt281\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Intractability_and_efficiency_and_the_combinatorial_explosion_16-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Intractability and efficiency and the combinatorial explosion\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Intractability_and_efficiency_and_the_combinatorial_explosion-16\" id=\"mwAhk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAho\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAhs\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAhw\">]</span></span></a></sup> \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Heuristics\" title=\"Heuristics\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAh0\">Heuristics</a>\" or \"rules of thumb\" can help prioritise choices that are more likely to reach a goal.<sup about=\"#mwt286\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-84\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-84\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-84\" id=\"mwAh4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAh8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAiA\">[</span>76<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAiE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAiI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adversarial_search\" title=\"Adversarial search\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAiM\">Adversarial search</a> is used for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_AI\" title=\"Game AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAiQ\">game-playing</a> programs, such as chess or Go. It searches through a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_tree\" title=\"Game tree\" id=\"mwAiU\">tree</a> of possible moves and countermoves, looking for a winning position.<sup about=\"#mwt288\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-85\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-85\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-85\" id=\"mwAiY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAic\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAig\">[</span>77<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAik\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"13\" id=\"mwAio\" aria-labelledby=\"Local_search\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Local_search\">Local search</h4></div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size skin-invert-image\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwAis\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Gradient_descent.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwAiw\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Gradient_descent.gif\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/a3/Gradient_descent.gif/330px-Gradient_descent.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/a/a3/Gradient_descent.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x\" data-file-width=\"360\" data-file-height=\"292\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"243\" width=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.2\" id=\"mwAi0\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwAi4\">Illustration of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gradient_descent\" title=\"Gradient descent\" id=\"mwAi8\">gradient descent</a> for three different starting points; two parameters (represented by the plan coordinates) are adjusted in order to minimise the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loss_function\" title=\"Loss function\" id=\"mwAjA\">loss function</a> (the height).</figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwAjE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Local_search_(optimization)\" title=\"Local search (optimization)\" id=\"mwAjI\">Local search</a> uses <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_optimization\" title=\"Mathematical optimization\" id=\"mwAjM\">mathematical optimisation</a> to find a solution to a problem. It begins with some form of guess and refines it incrementally.<sup about=\"#mwt290\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-86\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-86\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-86\" id=\"mwAjQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAjU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAjY\">[</span>78<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAjc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAjg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gradient_descent\" title=\"Gradient descent\" id=\"mwAjk\">Gradient descent</a> is a type of local search that optimises a set of numerical parameters by incrementally adjusting them to minimise a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loss_function\" title=\"Loss function\" id=\"mwAjo\">loss function</a>. Variants of gradient descent are commonly used to train <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_network\" title=\"Artificial neural network\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAjs\">neural networks</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt293\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-87\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-87\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-87\" id=\"mwAjw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAj0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAj4\">[</span>79<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAj8\">]</span></span></a></sup> through the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backpropagation\" title=\"Backpropagation\" id=\"mwAkA\">backpropagation</a> algorithm.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAkE\">Another type of local search is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Evolutionary_computation\" title=\"Evolutionary computation\" id=\"mwAkI\">evolutionary computation</a>, which aims to iteratively improve a set of candidate solutions by \"mutating\" and \"recombining\" them, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_selection\" title=\"Artificial selection\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAkM\">selecting</a> only the fittest to survive each generation.<sup about=\"#mwt295\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-88\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-88\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-88\" id=\"mwAkQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAkU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAkY\">[</span>80<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAkc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAkg\">Distributed search processes can coordinate via <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Swarm_intelligence\" title=\"Swarm intelligence\" id=\"mwAkk\">swarm intelligence</a> algorithms. Two popular swarm algorithms used in search are <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Particle_swarm_optimization\" title=\"Particle swarm optimization\" id=\"mwAko\">particle swarm optimisation</a> (inspired by bird <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Flocking\" title=\"Flocking\" id=\"mwAks\">flocking</a>) and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ant_colony_optimization\" title=\"Ant colony optimization\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAkw\">art colony optimisation</a> (inspired by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ant_trail\" title=\"Ant trail\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAk0\">ant trails</a>).<sup about=\"#mwt296\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMerkleMiddendorf2013_89-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMerkleMiddendorf2013\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMerkleMiddendorf2013-89\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Merkle\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Middendorf\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2013\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMerkleMiddendorf2013-89\" id=\"mwAk4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAk8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAlA\">[</span>81<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAlE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"14\" id=\"mwAlI\" aria-labelledby=\"Logic\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Logic\">Logic</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwAlM\">Formal <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic\" title=\"Logic\" id=\"mwAlQ\">logic</a> is used for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automatic_reasoning\" title=\"Automatic reasoning\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAlU\">reasoning</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Knowledge_representation\" title=\"Knowledge representation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAlY\">knowledge representation</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt302\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-90\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-90\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-90\" id=\"mwAlc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAlg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAlk\">[</span>82<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAlo\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nFormal logic comes in two main forms: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Propositional_logic\" title=\"Propositional logic\" id=\"mwAls\">propositional logic</a> (which operates on statements that are true or false and uses <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logical_connective\" title=\"Logical connective\" id=\"mwAlw\">logical connectives</a> such as \"and\", \"or\", \"not\" and \"implies\")<sup about=\"#mwt306\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-91\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-91\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-91\" id=\"mwAl0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAl4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAl8\">[</span>83<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAmA\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Predicate_logic\" title=\"Predicate logic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAmE\">predicate logic</a> (which also operates on objects, predicates and relations and uses <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quantifier_(logic)\" title=\"Quantifier (logic)\" id=\"mwAmI\">quantifiers</a> such as \"<i id=\"mwAmM\">Every</i> <i id=\"mwAmQ\">X</i> is a <i id=\"mwAmU\">Y</i>\" and \"There are <i id=\"mwAmY\">some</i> <i id=\"mwAmc\">X</i>s that are <i id=\"mwAmg\">Y</i>s\").<sup about=\"#mwt311\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-92\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-92\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-92\" id=\"mwAmk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAmo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAms\">[</span>84<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAmw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAm0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deductive_reasoning\" title=\"Deductive reasoning\" id=\"mwAm4\">Deductive reasoning</a> in logic is the process of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logical_proof\" title=\"Logical proof\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAm8\">proving</a> a new statement (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logical_consequence\" title=\"Logical consequence\" id=\"mwAnA\">conclusion</a>) from other statements that are given and assumed to be true (the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Premise\" title=\"Premise\" id=\"mwAnE\">premises</a>).<sup about=\"#mwt313\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-93\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-93\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-93\" id=\"mwAnI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAnM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAnQ\">[</span>85<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAnU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Proofs can be structured as proof <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Tree_structure\" title=\"Tree structure\" id=\"mwAnY\">trees</a>, in which nodes are labelled by sentences, and children nodes are connected to parent nodes by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inference_rule\" title=\"Inference rule\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAnc\">inference rules</a>.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAng\">Given a problem and a set of premises, problem-solving reduces to searching for a proof tree whose root node is labelled by a solution of the problem and whose <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Leaf_nodes\" title=\"Leaf nodes\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAnk\">leaf nodes</a> are labelled by premises or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Axiom\" title=\"Axiom\" id=\"mwAno\">axioms</a>. In the case of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Horn_clause\" title=\"Horn clause\" id=\"mwAns\">Horn clauses</a>, problem-solving search can be performed by reasoning <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forward_chaining\" title=\"Forward chaining\" id=\"mwAnw\">forwards</a> from the premises or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backward_chaining\" title=\"Backward chaining\" id=\"mwAn0\">backwards</a> from the problem.<sup about=\"#mwt318\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-94\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-94\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-94\" id=\"mwAn4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAn8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAoA\">[</span>86<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAoE\">]</span></span></a></sup> In the more general case of the clausal form of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/First-order_logic\" title=\"First-order logic\" id=\"mwAoI\">first-order logic</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Resolution_(logic)\" title=\"Resolution (logic)\" id=\"mwAoM\">resolution</a> is a single, axiom-free rule of inference, in which a problem is solved by proving a contradiction from premises that include the negation of the problem to be solved.<sup about=\"#mwt320\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-95\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-95\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-95\" id=\"mwAoQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAoU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAoY\">[</span>87<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAoc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAog\">Inference in both Horn clause logic and first-order logic is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Undecidable_problem\" title=\"Undecidable problem\" id=\"mwAok\">undecidable</a>, and therefore <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intractable_problem\" title=\"Intractable problem\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAoo\">intractable</a>. However, backward reasoning with Horn clauses, which underpins computation in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic_programming\" title=\"Logic programming\" id=\"mwAos\">logic programming</a> language <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prolog\" title=\"Prolog\" id=\"mwAow\">Prolog</a>, is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turing_complete\" title=\"Turing complete\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAo0\">Turing complete</a>. Moreover, its efficiency is competitive with computation in other <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_programming\" title=\"Symbolic programming\" id=\"mwAo4\">symbolic programming</a> languages.<sup about=\"#mwt323\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-96\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-96\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-96\" id=\"mwAo8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwApA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwApE\">[</span>88<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwApI\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwApM\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuzzy_logic\" title=\"Fuzzy logic\" id=\"mwApQ\">Fuzzy logic</a> assigns a \"degree of truth\" between 0 and 1. It can therefore handle propositions that are vague and partially true.<sup about=\"#mwt326\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-97\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-97\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-97\" id=\"mwApU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwApY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwApc\">[</span>89<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwApg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwApk\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Non-monotonic_logic\" title=\"Non-monotonic logic\" id=\"mwApo\">Non-monotonic logics</a>, including logic programming with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Negation_as_failure\" title=\"Negation as failure\" id=\"mwAps\">negation as failure</a>, are designed to handle <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Default_reasoning\" title=\"Default reasoning\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwApw\">default reasoning</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt327\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Default_reasoning_32-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Default reasoning\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Default_reasoning-32\" id=\"mwAp0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAp4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAp8\">[</span>29<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAqA\">]</span></span></a></sup> Other specialised versions of logic have been developed to describe many complex domains.</p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"15\" id=\"mwAqE\" aria-labelledby=\"Probabilistic_methods_for_uncertain_reasoning\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Probabilistic_methods_for_uncertain_reasoning\">Probabilistic methods for uncertain reasoning</h3></div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size skin-invert-image\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwAqI\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:SimpleBayesNet.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwAqM\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:SimpleBayesNet.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/SimpleBayesNet.svg/500px-SimpleBayesNet.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0e/SimpleBayesNet.svg/960px-SimpleBayesNet.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"575\" data-file-height=\"325\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"198\" width=\"350\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.4\" id=\"mwAqQ\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwAqU\">A simple <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayesian_network\" title=\"Bayesian network\" id=\"mwAqY\">Bayesian network</a>, with the associated <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conditional_probability_table\" title=\"Conditional probability table\" id=\"mwAqc\">conditional probability tables</a></figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwAqg\">Many problems in AI (including reasoning, planning, learning, perception, and robotics) require the agent to operate with incomplete or uncertain information. AI researchers have devised a number of tools to solve these problems using methods from <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Probability\" title=\"Probability\" id=\"mwAqk\">probability</a> theory and economics.<sup about=\"#mwt332\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Stoch_98-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Stoch\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Stoch-98\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Stoch-98\" id=\"mwAqo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAqs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAqw\">[</span>90<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAq0\">]</span></span></a></sup> Precise mathematical tools have been developed that analyse how an agent can make choices and plan, using <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_theory\" title=\"Decision theory\" id=\"mwAq4\">decision theory</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_analysis\" title=\"Decision analysis\" id=\"mwAq8\">decision analysis</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt335\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-99\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-99\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-99\" id=\"mwArA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwArE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwArI\">[</span>91<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwArM\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_value_theory\" title=\"Information value theory\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwArQ\">information value theory</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt337\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-100\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-100\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-100\" id=\"mwArU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwArY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwArc\">[</span>92<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwArg\">]</span></span></a></sup> These tools include models such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Markov_decision_process\" title=\"Markov decision process\" id=\"mwArk\">Markov decision processes</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt339\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-101\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-101\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-101\" id=\"mwAro\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwArs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwArw\">[</span>93<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAr0\">]</span></span></a></sup> dynamic <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_network\" title=\"Decision network\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAr4\">decision networks</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt340\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Stochastic_temporal_models_102-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Stochastic temporal models\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Stochastic_temporal_models-102\" id=\"mwAr8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAsA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAsE\">[</span>94<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAsI\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_theory\" title=\"Game theory\" id=\"mwAsM\">game theory</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mechanism_design\" title=\"Mechanism design\" id=\"mwAsQ\">mechanism design</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt342\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-103\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-103\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-103\" id=\"mwAsU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAsY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAsc\">[</span>95<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAsg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAsk\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayesian_network\" title=\"Bayesian network\" id=\"mwAso\">Bayesian networks</a><sup about=\"#mwt359\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-104\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-104\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-104\" id=\"mwAss\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAsw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAs0\">[</span>96<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAs4\">]</span></span></a></sup> are a tool that can be used for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_reasoning\" title=\"Automated reasoning\" id=\"mwAs8\">reasoning</a> (using the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bayesian_inference\" title=\"Bayesian inference\" id=\"mwAtA\">Bayesian inference</a> algorithm),<sup about=\"#mwt343\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-106\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-106\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Compared with symbolic logic, formal Bayesian inference is computationally expensive. For inference to be tractable, most observations must be [[conditionally independent]] of one another. [[AdSense]] uses a Bayesian network with over 300&amp;nbsp;million edges to learn which ads to serve.{{Sfnp|Domingos|2015|loc=chpt. 6}}\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-106\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwAtE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAtI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAtM\">[</span>i<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAtQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt364\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-107\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-107\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-107\" id=\"mwAtU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAtY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAtc\">[</span>98<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAtg\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mwAtk\">learning</a> (using the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expectation–maximization_algorithm\" title=\"Expectation–maximization algorithm\" id=\"mwAto\">expectation–maximisation algorithm</a>),<sup about=\"#mwt349\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-109\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-109\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Expectation–maximisation, one of the most popular algorithms in machine learning, allows clustering in the presence of unknown [[latent variables]].{{Sfnp|Domingos|2015|p=210}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-109\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwAts\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAtw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAt0\">[</span>j<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAt4\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt369\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-110\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-110\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-110\" id=\"mwAt8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAuA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAuE\">[</span>100<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAuI\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automated_planning_and_scheduling\" title=\"Automated planning and scheduling\" id=\"mwAuM\">planning</a> (using <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_network\" title=\"Decision network\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAuQ\">decision networks</a>)<sup about=\"#mwt371\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-111\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-111\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-111\" id=\"mwAuU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAuY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAuc\">[</span>101<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAug\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_perception\" title=\"Machine perception\" id=\"mwAuk\">perception</a> (using <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dynamic_Bayesian_network\" title=\"Dynamic Bayesian network\" id=\"mwAuo\">dynamic Bayesian networks</a>).<sup about=\"#mwt372\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Stochastic_temporal_models_102-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Stochastic temporal models\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Stochastic_temporal_models-102\" id=\"mwAus\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAuw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAu0\">[</span>94<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAu4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAu8\">Probabilistic algorithms can also be used for filtering, prediction, smoothing, and finding explanations for streams of data, thus helping perception systems analyse processes that occur over time (e.g., <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hidden_Markov_model\" title=\"Hidden Markov model\" id=\"mwAvA\">hidden Markov models</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kalman_filter\" title=\"Kalman filter\" id=\"mwAvE\">Kalman filters</a>).<sup about=\"#mwt377\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Stochastic_temporal_models_102-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Stochastic temporal models\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Stochastic_temporal_models-102\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Stochastic_temporal_models-102\" id=\"mwAvI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAvM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAvQ\">[</span>94<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAvU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwAvY\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:EM_Clustering_of_Old_Faithful_data.gif\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwAvc\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:EM_Clustering_of_Old_Faithful_data.gif\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/6/69/EM_Clustering_of_Old_Faithful_data.gif/330px-EM_Clustering_of_Old_Faithful_data.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/69/EM_Clustering_of_Old_Faithful_data.gif?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x\" data-file-width=\"360\" data-file-height=\"309\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"266\" width=\"310\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.25\" id=\"mwAvg\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwAvk\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expectation–maximization_algorithm\" title=\"Expectation–maximization algorithm\" id=\"mwAvo\">Expectation–maximisation</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cluster_analysis\" title=\"Cluster analysis\" id=\"mwAvs\">clustering</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Old_Faithful\" title=\"Old Faithful\" id=\"mwAvw\">Old Faithful</a> eruption data starts from a random guess but then successfully converges on an accurate clustering of the two physically distinct modes of eruption.</figcaption></figure>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"16\" id=\"mwAv0\" aria-labelledby=\"Classifiers_and_statistical_learning_methods\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Classifiers_and_statistical_learning_methods\">Classifiers and statistical learning methods</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwAv4\">The simplest AI applications can be divided into two types: classifiers (e.g., \"if shiny then diamond\"), on one hand, and controllers (e.g., \"if diamond then pick up\"), on the other hand. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classifier_(mathematics)\" title=\"Classifier (mathematics)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAv8\">Classifiers</a><sup about=\"#mwt379\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-112\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-112\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-112\" id=\"mwAwA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAwE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAwI\">[</span>102<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAwM\">]</span></span></a></sup> are functions that use <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattern_matching\" title=\"Pattern matching\" id=\"mwAwQ\">pattern matching</a> to determine the closest match. They can be fine-tuned based on chosen examples using <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Supervised_learning\" title=\"Supervised learning\" id=\"mwAwU\">supervised learning</a>. Each pattern (also called an \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Random_variate\" title=\"Random variate\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAwY\">observation</a>\") is labeled with a certain predefined class. All the observations combined with their class labels are known as a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_set\" title=\"Data set\" id=\"mwAwc\">data set</a>. When a new observation is received, that observation is classified based on previous experience.<sup about=\"#mwt380\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Supervised_learning_54-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Supervised learning\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Supervised_learning-54\" id=\"mwAwg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAwk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAwo\">[</span>47<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAws\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAww\">There are many kinds of classifiers in use.<sup about=\"#mwt383\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-113\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-113\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-113\" id=\"mwAw0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAw4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAw8\">[</span>103<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAxA\">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Decision_tree\" title=\"Decision tree\" id=\"mwAxE\">decision tree</a> is the simplest and most widely used symbolic machine learning algorithm.<sup about=\"#mwt386\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-114\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-114\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-114\" id=\"mwAxI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAxM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAxQ\">[</span>104<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAxU\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/K-nearest_neighbor\" title=\"K-nearest neighbor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAxY\">K-nearest neighbour</a> algorithm was the most widely used analogical AI until the mid-1990s, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kernel_methods\" title=\"Kernel methods\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAxc\">Kernel methods</a> such as the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Support_vector_machine\" title=\"Support vector machine\" id=\"mwAxg\">support vector machine</a> (SVM) displaced k-nearest neighbour in the 1990s.<sup about=\"#mwt390\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-115\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-115\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-115\" id=\"mwAxk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAxo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAxs\">[</span>105<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAxw\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nThe <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Naive_Bayes_classifier\" title=\"Naive Bayes classifier\" id=\"mwAx0\">naive Bayes classifier</a> is reportedly the \"most widely used learner\"<sup about=\"#mwt391\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015152_116-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEDomingos2015152\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015152-116\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Domingos\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2015\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"152\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015152-116\" id=\"mwAx4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAx8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAyA\">[</span>106<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAyE\">]</span></span></a></sup> at Google, due in part to its scalability.<sup about=\"#mwt396\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-117\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-117\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-117\" id=\"mwAyI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAyM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAyQ\">[</span>107<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAyU\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_network\" title=\"Artificial neural network\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAyY\">Neural networks</a> are also used as classifiers.<sup about=\"#mwt397\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Neural_networks_118-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Neural networks\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Neural_networks-118\" id=\"mwAyc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAyg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAyk\">[</span>108<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAyo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"17\" id=\"mwAys\" aria-labelledby=\"Artificial_neural_networks\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Artificial_neural_networks\">Artificial neural networks</h3></div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwAyw\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Artificial_neural_network.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwAy0\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Artificial_neural_network.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Artificial_neural_network.svg/250px-Artificial_neural_network.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e4/Artificial_neural_network.svg/500px-Artificial_neural_network.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"560\" data-file-height=\"500\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"223\" width=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" id=\"mwAy4\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwAy8\">A neural network is an interconnected group of nodes, akin to the vast network of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuron\" title=\"Neuron\" id=\"mwAzA\">neurons</a> in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_brain\" title=\"Human brain\" id=\"mwAzE\">human brain</a>.</figcaption></figure>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAzI\">An artificial neural network is based on a collection of nodes also known as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neurons\" title=\"Artificial neurons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAzM\">artificial neurons</a>, which loosely model the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neurons\" title=\"Neurons\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAzQ\">neurons</a> in a biological brain. It is trained to recognise patterns; once trained, it can recognise those patterns in fresh data. There is an input, at least one hidden layer of nodes and an output. Each node applies a function and once the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weighting\" title=\"Weighting\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwAzU\">weight</a> crosses its specified threshold, the data is transmitted to the next layer. A network is typically called a deep neural network if it has at least 2 hidden layers.<sup about=\"#mwt400\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Neural_networks_118-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Neural networks\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Neural_networks-118\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Neural_networks-118\" id=\"mwAzY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAzc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAzg\">[</span>108<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAzk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwAzo\">Learning algorithms for neural networks use <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Local_search_(optimization)\" title=\"Local search (optimization)\" id=\"mwAzs\">local search</a> to choose the weights that will get the right output for each input during training. The most common training technique is the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Backpropagation\" title=\"Backpropagation\" id=\"mwAzw\">backpropagation</a> algorithm.<sup about=\"#mwt404\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-119\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-119\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-119\" id=\"mwAz0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwAz4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwAz8\">[</span>109<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA0A\">]</span></span></a></sup> Neural networks learn to model complex relationships between inputs and outputs and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattern_recognition\" title=\"Pattern recognition\" id=\"mwA0E\">find patterns</a> in data. In theory, a neural network can learn any function.<sup about=\"#mwt408\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-120\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-120\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-120\" id=\"mwA0I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA0M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA0Q\">[</span>110<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA0U\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwA0Y\">In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Feedforward_neural_network\" title=\"Feedforward neural network\" id=\"mwA0c\">feedforward neural networks</a> the signal passes in only one direction.<sup about=\"#mwt410\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-121\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-121\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-121\" id=\"mwA0g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA0k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA0o\">[</span>111<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA0s\">]</span></span></a></sup> The term <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perceptron\" title=\"Perceptron\" id=\"mwA0w\">perceptron</a> typically refers to a single-layer neural network.<sup about=\"#mwt412\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-122\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-122\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-122\" id=\"mwA00\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA04\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA08\">[</span>112<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA1A\">]</span></span></a></sup> In contrast, deep learning uses many layers.<sup about=\"#mwt417\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Deep_learning_123-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Deep learning\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Deep_learning-123\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Deep_learning-123\" id=\"mwA1E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA1I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA1M\">[</span>113<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA1Q\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recurrent_neural_network\" title=\"Recurrent neural network\" id=\"mwA1U\">Recurrent neural networks</a> (RNNs) feed the output signal back into the input, which allows short-term memories of previous input events. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Long_short-term_memory\" title=\"Long short-term memory\" id=\"mwA1Y\">Long short-term memory</a> networks (LSTMs) are recurrent neural networks that better preserve longterm dependencies and are less sensitive to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vanishing_gradient_problem\" title=\"Vanishing gradient problem\" id=\"mwA1c\">vanishing gradient problem</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt419\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-124\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-124\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-124\" id=\"mwA1g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA1k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA1o\">[</span>114<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA1s\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convolutional_neural_network\" title=\"Convolutional neural network\" id=\"mwA1w\">Convolutional neural networks</a> (CNNs) use layers of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kernel_(image_processing)\" title=\"Kernel (image processing)\" id=\"mwA10\">kernels</a> to more efficiently process local patterns. This local processing is especially important in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image_processing\" title=\"Image processing\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA14\">image processing</a>, where the early CNN layers typically identify simple local patterns such as edges and curves, with subsequent layers detecting more complex patterns like textures, and eventually whole objects.<sup about=\"#mwt421\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-125\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-125\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-125\" id=\"mwA18\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA2A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA2E\">[</span>115<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA2I\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"18\" id=\"mwA2M\" aria-labelledby=\"Deep_learning\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Deep_learning\">Deep learning</h3></div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwA2Q\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AI-ML-DL.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwA2U\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AI-ML-DL.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/AI-ML-DL.svg/250px-AI-ML-DL.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/b/bb/AI-ML-DL.svg/500px-AI-ML-DL.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"748\" data-file-height=\"826\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"232\" width=\"210\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 0.85\" id=\"mwA2Y\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwA2c\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_learning\" title=\"Deep learning\" id=\"mwA2g\">Deep learning</a> is a subset of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mwA2k\">machine learning</a>, which is itself a subset of artificial intelligence.<sup about=\"#mwt424\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-journalimcms.org_126-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"journalimcms.org\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-journalimcms.org-126\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-journalimcms.org-126\" id=\"mwA2o\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA2s\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA2w\">[</span>116<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA20\">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwA24\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_learning\" title=\"Deep learning\" id=\"mwA28\">Deep learning</a> uses several layers of neurons between the network\\'s inputs and outputs.<sup about=\"#mwt428\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Deep_learning_123-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Deep learning\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Deep_learning-123\" id=\"mwA3A\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA3E\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA3I\">[</span>113<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA3M\">]</span></span></a></sup> The multiple layers can progressively extract higher-level features from the raw input. For example, in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image_processing\" title=\"Image processing\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA3Q\">image processing</a>, lower layers may identify edges, while higher layers may identify the concepts relevant to a human such as digits, letters, or faces.<sup about=\"#mwt425\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDengYu2014199–200_127-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEDengYu2014199–200\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDengYu2014199–200-127\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Deng\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Yu\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2014\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"199–200\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDengYu2014199–200-127\" id=\"mwA3U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA3Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA3c\">[</span>117<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA3g\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwA3k\">Deep learning has profoundly improved the performance of programs in many important subfields of artificial intelligence, including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_vision\" title=\"Computer vision\" id=\"mwA3o\">computer vision</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_recognition\" title=\"Speech recognition\" id=\"mwA3s\">speech recognition</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_language_processing\" title=\"Natural language processing\" id=\"mwA3w\">natural language processing</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image_classification\" title=\"Image classification\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA30\">image classification</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt429\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECiresanMeierSchmidhuber2012_128-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTECiresanMeierSchmidhuber2012\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECiresanMeierSchmidhuber2012-128\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Ciresan\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Meier\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"Schmidhuber\"},\"4\":{\"wt\":\"2012\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTECiresanMeierSchmidhuber2012-128\" id=\"mwA34\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA38\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA4A\">[</span>118<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA4E\">]</span></span></a></sup> and others. The reason that deep learning performs so well in so many applications is not known as of 2021.<sup about=\"#mwt432\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021750_129-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021750\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021750-129\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"750\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021750-129\" id=\"mwA4I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA4M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA4Q\">[</span>119<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA4U\">]</span></span></a></sup> The sudden success of deep learning in 2012–2015 did not occur because of some new discovery or theoretical breakthrough (deep neural networks and backpropagation had been described by many people, as far back as the 1950s)<sup about=\"#mwt435\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-136\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-136\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Some form of deep neural networks (without a specific learning algorithm) were described by:\\\\n[[Warren S. McCulloch]] and [[Walter Pitts]] (1943);{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=17}}\\\\n[[Alan Turing]] (1948);{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=785}}\\\\n[[Karl Steinbuch]] and [[Roger David Joseph]] (1961).{{Sfnp|Schmidhuber|2022|loc=sect. 5}}\\\\nDeep or recurrent networks that learned (or used gradient descent) were developed by:\\\\n[[Frank Rosenblatt]] (1957);{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=785}}\\\\n[[Oliver Selfridge]] (1959);{{Sfnp|Schmidhuber|2022|loc=sect. 5}}\\\\n[[Alexey Ivakhnenko]] and [[Valentin Lapa]] (1965);{{Sfnp|Schmidhuber|2022|loc=sect. 6}}\\\\n[[Kaoru Nakano]] (1971);{{Sfnp|Schmidhuber|2022|loc=sect. 7}}\\\\n[[Shun-Ichi Amari]] (1972); {{Sfnp|Schmidhuber|2022|loc=sect. 7}} and [[John Joseph Hopfield]] (1982).{{Sfnp|Schmidhuber|2022|loc=sect. 7}}\\\\nPrecursors to backpropagation were developed by:\\\\n[[Henry J. Kelley]] (1960);{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=785}}\\\\n[[Arthur E. Bryson]] (1962);{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=785}}\\\\n[[Stuart Dreyfus]] (1962);{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=785}}\\\\n[[Arthur E. Bryson]] and [[Yu-Chi Ho]] (1969).{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=785}}\\\\nBackpropagation was independently developed by:\\\\n[[Seppo Linnainmaa]] (1970);{{Sfnp|Schmidhuber|2022|loc=sect. 8}} and [[Paul Werbos]] (1974).{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=785}}\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-136\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwA4Y\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA4c\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA4g\">[</span>k<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA4k\">]</span></span></a></sup> but because of two factors: the increase in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Compute_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Compute (machine learning)\" id=\"mwA4o\">computer power</a> (including the hundred-fold increase in speed by switching to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GPU\" title=\"GPU\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA4s\">GPUs</a>) and the availability of vast amounts of training data, especially the giant <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_datasets_for_machine-learning_research\" title=\"List of datasets for machine-learning research\" id=\"mwA4w\">curated datasets</a> used for benchmark testing, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ImageNet\" title=\"ImageNet\" id=\"mwA40\">ImageNet</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt483\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-138\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Geoffrey Hinton]] said, of his work on neural networks in the 1990s, \\\\\"our labeled datasets were thousands of times too small. [And] our computers were millions of times too slow.\\\\\"&lt;ref>Quoted in {{Harvtxt|Christian|2020|p=22}}&lt;/ref>\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-138\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwA44\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA48\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA5A\">[</span>l<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA5E\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"19\" id=\"mwA5I\" aria-labelledby=\"GPT\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"GPT\">GPT</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwA5M\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_pre-trained_transformer\" title=\"Generative pre-trained transformer\" id=\"mwA5Q\">Generative pre-trained transformers</a> (GPTs) are <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model\" title=\"Large language model\" id=\"mwA5U\">large language models</a> (LLMs) that generate text based on the semantic relationships between words in sentences. Text-based GPT models are pre-trained on a large <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Corpus_of_text\" title=\"Corpus of text\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA5Y\">corpus of text</a> that can be from the Internet. The pretraining consists of predicting the next <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lexical_analysis\" title=\"Lexical analysis\" id=\"mwA5c\">token</a> (a token being usually a word, subword, or punctuation). Throughout this pretraining, GPT models accumulate knowledge about the world and can then generate human-like text by repeatedly predicting the next token. Typically, a subsequent training phase makes the model more truthful, useful, and harmless, usually with a technique called <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reinforcement_learning_from_human_feedback\" title=\"Reinforcement learning from human feedback\" id=\"mwA5g\">reinforcement learning from human feedback</a> (RLHF). Current GPT models are prone to generating falsehoods called \"hallucinations\". These can be reduced with RLHF and quality data, but the problem has been getting worse for reasoning systems.<sup about=\"#mwt495\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-139\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-139\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-139\" id=\"mwA5k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA5o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA5s\">[</span>127<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA5w\">]</span></span></a></sup> Such systems are used in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatbot\" title=\"Chatbot\" id=\"mwA50\">chatbots</a>, which allow people to ask a question or request a task in simple text.<sup about=\"#mwt490\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESmith2023_140-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESmith2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESmith2023-140\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Smith\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESmith2023-140\" id=\"mwA54\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA58\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA6A\">[</span>128<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA6E\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt498\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-141\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-141\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-141\" id=\"mwA6I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA6M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA6Q\">[</span>129<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA6U\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwA6Y\">Current models and services include <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT\" title=\"ChatGPT\" id=\"mwA6c\">ChatGPT</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_AI\" title=\"Claude AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA6g\">Claude</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Gemini\" title=\"Google Gemini\" id=\"mwA6k\">Gemini</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Copilot\" title=\"Microsoft Copilot\" id=\"mwA6o\">Copilot</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_AI\" title=\"Meta AI\" id=\"mwA6s\">Meta AI</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt504\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-142\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-142\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-142\" id=\"mwA6w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA60\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA64\">[</span>130<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA68\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multimodal_learning\" title=\"Multimodal learning\" id=\"mwA7A\">Multimodal</a> GPT models can process different types of data (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Modality_(human–computer_interaction)\" title=\"Modality (human–computer interaction)\" id=\"mwA7E\">modalities</a>) such as images, videos, sound, and text.<sup about=\"#mwt499\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMarmouyet2023_143-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMarmouyet2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMarmouyet2023-143\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Marmouyet\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMarmouyet2023-143\" id=\"mwA7I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA7M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA7Q\">[</span>131<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA7U\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"20\" id=\"mwA7Y\" aria-labelledby=\"Hardware_and_software\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Hardware_and_software\">Hardware and software</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt505\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwA7c\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Programming languages for artificial intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Hardware for artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt506\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt505\" id=\"mwA7g\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programming_languages_for_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Programming languages for artificial intelligence\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Programming languages for artificial intelligence</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hardware_for_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Hardware for artificial intelligence\">Hardware for artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwA7k\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Raspberry_Pi_AI_Kit_for_Raspberry_Pi_5_complete_Kit_07.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwA7o\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Raspberry_Pi_AI_Kit_for_Raspberry_Pi_5_complete_Kit_07.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Raspberry_Pi_AI_Kit_for_Raspberry_Pi_5_complete_Kit_07.jpg/250px-Raspberry_Pi_AI_Kit_for_Raspberry_Pi_5_complete_Kit_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/1f/Raspberry_Pi_AI_Kit_for_Raspberry_Pi_5_complete_Kit_07.jpg/500px-Raspberry_Pi_AI_Kit_for_Raspberry_Pi_5_complete_Kit_07.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"4831\" data-file-height=\"3221\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"167\" width=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" id=\"mwA7s\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwA7w\">Raspberry Pi AI Kit</figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwA70\">In the late 2010s, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphics_processing_unit\" title=\"Graphics processing unit\" id=\"mwA74\">graphics processing units</a> (GPUs) that were increasingly designed with AI-specific enhancements and used with specialised <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TensorFlow\" title=\"TensorFlow\" id=\"mwA78\">TensorFlow</a> software had replaced previously used <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Central_processing_unit\" title=\"Central processing unit\" id=\"mwA8A\">central processing unit</a> (CPUs) as the dominant means for large-scale (commercial and academic) <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mwA8E\">machine learning</a> models\\' training.<sup about=\"#mwt507\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKobielus2019_144-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEKobielus2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKobielus2019-144\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Kobielus\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2019\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKobielus2019-144\" id=\"mwA8I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA8M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA8Q\">[</span>132<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA8U\">]</span></span></a></sup> Specialised <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Programming_language\" title=\"Programming language\" id=\"mwA8Y\">programming languages</a> such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prolog\" title=\"Prolog\" id=\"mwA8c\">Prolog</a> were used in early AI research,<sup about=\"#mwt512\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-145\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-145\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-145\" id=\"mwA8g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA8k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA8o\">[</span>133<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA8s\">]</span></span></a></sup> but <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General-purpose_programming_language\" title=\"General-purpose programming language\" id=\"mwA8w\">general-purpose programming languages</a> like <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Python_(programming_language)\" title=\"Python (programming language)\" id=\"mwA80\">Python</a> have become predominant.<sup about=\"#mwt515\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-146\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-146\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-146\" id=\"mwA84\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA88\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA9A\">[</span>134<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA9E\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwA9I\">The transistor density in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Integrated_circuit\" title=\"Integrated circuit\" id=\"mwA9M\">integrated circuits</a> has been observed to roughly double every 18 months—a trend known as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moore\\'s_law\" title=\"Moore\\'s law\" id=\"mwA9Q\">Moore\\'s law</a>, named after the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intel\" title=\"Intel\" id=\"mwA9U\">Intel</a> co-founder <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gordon_Moore\" title=\"Gordon Moore\" id=\"mwA9Y\">Gordon Moore</a>, who first identified it. Improvements in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GPUs\" title=\"GPUs\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA9c\">GPUs</a> have been even faster,<sup about=\"#mwt518\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-147\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-147\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-147\" id=\"mwA9g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA9k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA9o\">[</span>135<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA9s\">]</span></span></a></sup> a trend sometimes called <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Huang\\'s_law\" title=\"Huang\\'s law\" id=\"mwA9w\">Huang\\'s law</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt521\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-148\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-148\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-148\" id=\"mwA90\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwA94\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA98\">[</span>136<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwA-A\">]</span></span></a></sup> named after <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nvidia\" title=\"Nvidia\" id=\"mwA-E\">Nvidia</a> co-founder and CEO <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jensen_Huang\" title=\"Jensen Huang\" id=\"mwA-I\">Jensen Huang</a>.</p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"21\" id=\"mwA-M\" aria-labelledby=\"Applications\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Applications\">Applications</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt522\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwA-Q\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Applications of artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt523\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt522\" id=\"mwA-U\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Applications_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Applications of artificial intelligence\">Applications of artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwA-Y\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AI_Overviews_result_for_What_is_Wikipedia,_2_March_2026.png\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwA-c\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:AI_Overviews_result_for_What_is_Wikipedia,_2_March_2026.png\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/AI_Overviews_result_for_What_is_Wikipedia%2C_2_March_2026.png/250px-AI_Overviews_result_for_What_is_Wikipedia%2C_2_March_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/e/e3/AI_Overviews_result_for_What_is_Wikipedia%2C_2_March_2026.png/500px-AI_Overviews_result_for_What_is_Wikipedia%2C_2_March_2026.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1336\" data-file-height=\"1356\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"254\" width=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" id=\"mwA-g\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwA-k\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Overviews\" title=\"AI Overviews\" id=\"mwA-o\">AI Overviews</a>, an example of AI use on search engines</figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwA-s\">AI and machine learning technology is used in most of the essential applications of the 2020s, including:</p>\\n<ul id=\"mwA-w\"><li id=\"mwA-0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Search_engines\" title=\"Search engines\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA-4\">search engines</a> (such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Search\" title=\"Google Search\" id=\"mwA-8\">Google Search</a>)</li>\\n<li id=\"mwA_A\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Targeted_advertising\" title=\"Targeted advertising\" id=\"mwA_E\">targeting online advertisements</a></li>\\n<li id=\"mwA_I\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recommendation_systems\" title=\"Recommendation systems\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA_M\">recommendation systems</a> (offered by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Netflix\" title=\"Netflix\" id=\"mwA_Q\">Netflix</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube\" title=\"YouTube\" id=\"mwA_U\">YouTube</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)\" title=\"Amazon (company)\" id=\"mwA_Y\">Amazon</a>) driving <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Internet_traffic\" title=\"Internet traffic\" id=\"mwA_c\">internet traffic</a></li>\\n<li id=\"mwA_g\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marketing_and_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Marketing and artificial intelligence\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA_k\">targeted advertising</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AdSense\" title=\"AdSense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwA_o\">AdSense</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook\" title=\"Facebook\" id=\"mwA_s\">Facebook</a>)</li>\\n<li id=\"mwA_w\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_assistant\" title=\"Virtual assistant\" id=\"mwA_0\">virtual assistants</a> (such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Siri\" title=\"Siri\" id=\"mwA_4\">Siri</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_Alexa\" title=\"Amazon Alexa\" id=\"mwA_8\">Alexa</a>)</li>\\n<li id=\"mwBAA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomous_vehicles\" title=\"Autonomous vehicles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBAE\">autonomous vehicles</a> (including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unmanned_aerial_vehicle\" title=\"Unmanned aerial vehicle\" id=\"mwBAI\">drones</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Advanced_driver-assistance_system\" title=\"Advanced driver-assistance system\" id=\"mwBAM\">ADAS</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-driving_cars\" title=\"Self-driving cars\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBAQ\">self-driving cars</a>)</li>\\n<li id=\"mwBAU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Automatic_language_translation\" title=\"Automatic language translation\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBAY\">automatic language translation</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Translator\" title=\"Microsoft Translator\" id=\"mwBAc\">Microsoft Translator</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Translate\" title=\"Google Translate\" id=\"mwBAg\">Google Translate</a>)</li>\\n<li id=\"mwBAk\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facial_recognition_system\" title=\"Facial recognition system\" id=\"mwBAo\">facial recognition</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Computer\" title=\"Apple Computer\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBAs\">Apple</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FaceID\" title=\"FaceID\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBAw\">FaceID</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms\" title=\"Meta Platforms\" id=\"mwBA0\">Facebook</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepFace\" title=\"DeepFace\" id=\"mwBA4\">DeepFace</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google\" title=\"Google\" id=\"mwBA8\">Google</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FaceNet\" title=\"FaceNet\" id=\"mwBBA\">FaceNet</a>)</li>\\n<li id=\"mwBBE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Image_labeling\" title=\"Image labeling\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBBI\">image labelling</a> (used by Facebook, Apple\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Photos_(Apple)\" title=\"Photos (Apple)\" id=\"mwBBM\">Photos</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/TikTok\" title=\"TikTok\" id=\"mwBBQ\">TikTok</a>).</li></ul>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"22\" id=\"mwBBU\" aria-labelledby=\"AI-assisted_software_development\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"AI-assisted_software_development\">AI-assisted software development</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt524\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBBY\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"AI-assisted software development\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"List of AI-assisted software development tools\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt525\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt524\" id=\"mwBBc\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI-assisted_software_development\" title=\"AI-assisted software development\">AI-assisted software development</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_AI-assisted_software_development_tools\" title=\"List of AI-assisted software development tools\">List of AI-assisted software development tools</a></div>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"23\" id=\"mwBBg\" aria-labelledby=\"Chatbots\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Chatbots\">Chatbots</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt526\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBBk\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Chatbots\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"List of chatbots\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt527\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt526\" id=\"mwBBo\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatbots\" title=\"Chatbots\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Chatbots</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_chatbots\" title=\"List of chatbots\">List of chatbots</a></div>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"24\" id=\"mwBBs\" aria-labelledby=\"Physical_AI\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Physical_AI\">Physical AI</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt528\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBBw\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Physical artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt529\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt528\" id=\"mwBB0\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physical_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Physical artificial intelligence\">Physical artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"25\" id=\"mwBB4\" aria-labelledby=\"Health_and_medicine\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Health_and_medicine\">Health and medicine</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt530\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBB8\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial intelligence in healthcare\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt531\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt530\" id=\"mwBCA\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_in_healthcare\" title=\"Artificial intelligence in healthcare\">Artificial intelligence in healthcare</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBCE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaFold_2\" title=\"AlphaFold 2\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBCI\">AlphaFold 2</a> (2021) demonstrated the ability to approximate, in hours rather than months, the 3D <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Protein_structure\" title=\"Protein structure\" id=\"mwBCM\">structure of a protein</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt534\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-149\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-149\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-149\" id=\"mwBCQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBCU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBCY\">[</span>137<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBCc\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2023, it was reported that AI-guided drug discovery helped find a class of antibiotics capable of killing two different types of drug-resistant bacteria.<sup about=\"#mwt537\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-150\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-150\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-150\" id=\"mwBCg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBCk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBCo\">[</span>138<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBCs\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2024, researchers used machine learning to accelerate the search for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Parkinson\\'s_disease\" title=\"Parkinson\\'s disease\" id=\"mwBCw\">Parkinson\\'s disease</a> drug treatments. Their aim was to identify compounds that block the clumping, or aggregation, of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alpha-synuclein\" title=\"Alpha-synuclein\" id=\"mwBC0\">alpha-synuclein</a> (the protein that characterises Parkinson\\'s disease). They were able to speed up the initial screening process ten-fold and reduce the cost by a thousand-fold.<sup about=\"#mwt540\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-151\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-151\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-151\" id=\"mwBC4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBC8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBDA\">[</span>139<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBDE\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt543\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-152\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-152\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-152\" id=\"mwBDI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBDM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBDQ\">[</span>140<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBDU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBDY\">AI is increasingly being used in medical diagnostics, including the detection of diseases such as lung cancer from medical imaging like <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CT_scan\" title=\"CT scan\" id=\"mwBDc\">CT scans</a>. <sup about=\"#mwt546\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-153\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-153\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-153\" id=\"mwBDg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBDk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBDo\">[</span>141<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBDs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBDw\">A 2026 <i id=\"mwBD0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nature_(journal)\" title=\"Nature (journal)\" id=\"mwBD4\">Nature</a></i> article titled \"Dozens of AI disease-prediction models were trained on dubious data\" highlighted the use of unreliable data being used to train AI medical prediction models for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stroke\" title=\"Stroke\" id=\"mwBD8\">stroke</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diabetes\" title=\"Diabetes\" id=\"mwBEA\">diabetes</a> in 125 research articles. Evidence suggested some of the AI tools that were developed on unreliable data had been used on patients, although it was not clear if there were adverse outcomes.<sup about=\"#mwt549\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-154\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-154\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-154\" id=\"mwBEE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBEI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBEM\">[</span>142<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBEQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt552\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-155\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-155\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-155\" id=\"mwBEU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBEY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBEc\">[</span>143<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBEg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"26\" id=\"mwBEk\" aria-labelledby=\"Gaming\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Gaming\">Gaming</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt553\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBEo\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial intelligence in video games\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt554\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt553\" id=\"mwBEs\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_in_video_games\" title=\"Artificial intelligence in video games\">Artificial intelligence in video games</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBEw\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Game_AI\" title=\"Game AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBE0\">Game playing</a> programs have been used since the 1950s to demonstrate and test AI\\'s most advanced techniques.<sup about=\"#mwt557\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-156\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-156\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-156\" id=\"mwBE4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBE8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBFA\">[</span>144<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBFE\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM_Deep_Blue\" title=\"IBM Deep Blue\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBFI\">Deep Blue</a> became the first computer chess-playing system to beat a reigning world chess champion, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Garry_Kasparov\" title=\"Garry Kasparov\" id=\"mwBFM\">Garry Kasparov</a>, on 11 May 1997.<sup about=\"#mwt560\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-157\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-157\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-157\" id=\"mwBFQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBFU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBFY\">[</span>145<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBFc\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2011, in a <i id=\"mwBFg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jeopardy!\" title=\"Jeopardy!\" id=\"mwBFk\">Jeopardy!</a></i> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Quiz_show\" title=\"Quiz show\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBFo\">quiz show</a> exhibition match, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM\" title=\"IBM\" id=\"mwBFs\">IBM</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Question_answering_system\" title=\"Question answering system\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBFw\">question answering system</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Watson_(artificial_intelligence_software)\" title=\"Watson (artificial intelligence software)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBF0\">Watson</a>, defeated the two greatest <i id=\"mwBF4\">Jeopardy!</i> champions, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brad_Rutter\" title=\"Brad Rutter\" id=\"mwBF8\">Brad Rutter</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ken_Jennings\" title=\"Ken Jennings\" id=\"mwBGA\">Ken Jennings</a>, by a significant margin.<sup about=\"#mwt563\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-158\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-158\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-158\" id=\"mwBGE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBGI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBGM\">[</span>146<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBGQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> In March 2016, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaGo\" title=\"AlphaGo\" id=\"mwBGU\">AlphaGo</a> won 4 out of 5 games of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Go_(game)\" title=\"Go (game)\" id=\"mwBGY\">Go</a> in a match with Go champion <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lee_Sedol\" title=\"Lee Sedol\" id=\"mwBGc\">Lee Sedol</a>, becoming the first <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computer_Go\" title=\"Computer Go\" id=\"mwBGg\">computer Go</a>-playing system to beat a professional Go player without <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Go_handicaps\" title=\"Go handicaps\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBGk\">handicaps</a>. Then, in 2017, it <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaGo_versus_Ke_Jie\" title=\"AlphaGo versus Ke Jie\" id=\"mwBGo\">defeated Ke Jie</a>, who was the best Go player in the world.<sup about=\"#mwt566\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-159\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-159\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-159\" id=\"mwBGs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBGw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBG0\">[</span>147<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBG4\">]</span></span></a></sup> Other programs handle <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Imperfect_information\" title=\"Imperfect information\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBG8\">imperfect-information</a> games, such as the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Poker\" title=\"Poker\" id=\"mwBHA\">poker</a>-playing program <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pluribus_(poker_bot)\" title=\"Pluribus (poker bot)\" id=\"mwBHE\">Pluribus</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt569\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-160\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-160\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-160\" id=\"mwBHI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBHM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBHQ\">[</span>148<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBHU\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepMind\" title=\"DeepMind\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBHY\">DeepMind</a> developed increasingly generalistic <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reinforcement_learning\" title=\"Reinforcement learning\" id=\"mwBHc\">reinforcement learning</a> models, such as with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/MuZero\" title=\"MuZero\" id=\"mwBHg\">MuZero</a>, which could be trained to play chess, Go, or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atari\" title=\"Atari\" id=\"mwBHk\">Atari</a> games.<sup about=\"#mwt572\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-161\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-161\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-161\" id=\"mwBHo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBHs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBHw\">[</span>149<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBH0\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2019, DeepMind\\'s AlphaStar achieved grandmaster level in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/StarCraft_II\" title=\"StarCraft II\" id=\"mwBH4\">StarCraft II</a>, a particularly challenging real-time strategy game that involves incomplete knowledge of what happens on the map.<sup about=\"#mwt575\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-162\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-162\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-162\" id=\"mwBH8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBIA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIE\">[</span>150<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBII\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2021, an AI agent competed in a PlayStation <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gran_Turismo_(series)\" title=\"Gran Turismo (series)\" id=\"mwBIM\">Gran Turismo</a> competition, winning against four of the world\\'s best Gran Turismo drivers using deep reinforcement learning.<sup about=\"#mwt578\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-163\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-163\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-163\" id=\"mwBIQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBIU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIY\">[</span>151<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIc\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2024, Google DeepMind introduced SIMA, a type of AI capable of autonomously playing nine previously unseen <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open-world\" title=\"Open-world\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBIg\">open-world</a> video games by observing screen output, as well as executing short, specific tasks in response to natural language instructions.<sup about=\"#mwt581\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-164\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-164\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-164\" id=\"mwBIk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBIo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIs\">[</span>152<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBIw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"27\" id=\"mwBI0\" aria-labelledby=\"Mathematics\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Mathematics\">Mathematics</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt582\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBI4\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"AlphaDev\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt583\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt582\" id=\"mwBI8\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaDev\" title=\"AlphaDev\">AlphaDev</a></div>\\n<p id=\"mwBJA\">In mathematics, probabilistic large language models are versatile, but can also produce wrong answers in the form of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallucination_(artificial_intelligence)\" title=\"Hallucination (artificial intelligence)\" id=\"mwBJE\">hallucinations</a>. The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alibaba_Group\" title=\"Alibaba Group\" id=\"mwBJI\">Alibaba Group</a> developed a version of its <i id=\"mwBJM\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qwen\" title=\"Qwen\" id=\"mwBJQ\">Qwen</a></i> models called <i id=\"mwBJU\">Qwen2-Math</i>, that achieved state-of-the-art performance on several mathematical benchmarks, including 84% accuracy on the MATH dataset of competition mathematics problems.<sup about=\"#mwt586\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-VentureBeat_8_August_2024_165-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"VentureBeat 8 August 2024\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-VentureBeat_8_August_2024-165\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-VentureBeat_8_August_2024-165\" id=\"mwBJY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBJc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJg\">[</span>153<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBJk\">]</span></span></a></sup> In January 2025, Microsoft proposed the technique <i id=\"mwBJo\">rStar-Math</i> that leverages <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Monte_Carlo_tree_search\" title=\"Monte Carlo tree search\" id=\"mwBJs\">Monte Carlo tree search</a> and step-by-step reasoning, enabling a relatively small language model like <i id=\"mwBJw\">Qwen-7B</i> to solve 53% of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/American_Invitational_Mathematics_Examination\" title=\"American Invitational Mathematics Examination\" id=\"mwBJ0\">AIME</a> 2024 and 90% of the MATH benchmark problems.<sup about=\"#mwt589\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-166\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-166\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-166\" id=\"mwBJ4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBJ8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBKA\">[</span>154<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBKE\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_DeepMind\" title=\"Google DeepMind\" id=\"mwBKI\">Google DeepMind</a> has developed models for solving mathematical problems: <i id=\"mwBKM\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaTensor\" title=\"AlphaTensor\" id=\"mwBKQ\">AlphaTensor</a></i>, <i id=\"mwBKU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaGeometry\" title=\"AlphaGeometry\" id=\"mwBKY\">AlphaGeometry</a></i>, <i id=\"mwBKc\">AlphaProof</i>, <i id=\"mwBKg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaEvolve\" title=\"AlphaEvolve\" id=\"mwBKk\">AlphaEvolve</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/FunSearch\" title=\"FunSearch\" id=\"mwBKo\">FunSearch</a>.</i><sup about=\"#mwt592\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-167\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-167\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-167\" id=\"mwBKs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBKw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBK0\">[</span>155<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBK4\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt595\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-168\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-168\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-168\" id=\"mwBK8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBLA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLE\">[</span>156<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLI\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBLM\">When natural language is used to describe mathematical problems, converters can transform such prompts into a formal language such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lean_(proof_assistant)\" title=\"Lean (proof assistant)\" id=\"mwBLQ\">Lean</a> to define mathematical tasks. The experimental model <i id=\"mwBLU\">Gemini Deep Think</i> accepts natural language prompts directly and achieved gold medal results in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Math_Olympiad\" title=\"International Math Olympiad\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBLY\">International Math Olympiad</a> of 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt598\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-169\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-169\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-169\" id=\"mwBLc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBLg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLk\">[</span>157<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBLo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBLs\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topological_deep_learning\" title=\"Topological deep learning\" id=\"mwBLw\">Topological deep learning</a> integrates various <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Topological\" title=\"Topological\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBL0\">topological</a> approaches.</p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"28\" id=\"mwBL4\" aria-labelledby=\"Finance\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Finance\">Finance</h3></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBL8\">According to Nicolas Firzli, director of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/World_Pensions_&amp;_Investments_Forum\" title=\"World Pensions &amp; Investments Forum\" id=\"mwBMA\">World Pensions &amp; Investments Forum</a>, it may be too early to see the emergence of highly innovative AI-informed financial products and services. He argues that \"the deployment of AI tools will simply further automatise things: destroying tens of thousands of jobs in banking, financial planning, and pension advice in the process, but I\\'m not sure it will unleash a new wave of [e.g., sophisticated] pension innovation.\"<sup about=\"#mwt600\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-170\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-170\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-170\" id=\"mwBME\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBMI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMM\">[</span>158<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"29\" id=\"mwBMU\" aria-labelledby=\"Military\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Military\">Military</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt601\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBMY\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Military applications of artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt602\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt601\" id=\"mwBMc\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Military_applications_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Military applications of artificial intelligence\">Military applications of artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBMg\">Various countries are deploying AI military applications.<sup about=\"#mwt605\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CRS-2019_171-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CRS-2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-CRS-2019-171\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-CRS-2019-171\" id=\"mwBMk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBMo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMs\">[</span>159<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBMw\">]</span></span></a></sup> The main applications enhance <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Command_and_control\" title=\"Command and control\" id=\"mwBM0\">command and control</a>, communications, sensors, integration and interoperability.<sup about=\"#mwt608\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Slyusar-2019_172-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Slyusar-2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Slyusar-2019-172\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Slyusar-2019-172\" id=\"mwBM4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBM8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNA\">[</span>160<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNE\">]</span></span></a></sup> Research is targeting intelligence collection and analysis, logistics, cyber operations, information operations, and semiautonomous and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vehicular_automation\" title=\"Vehicular automation\" id=\"mwBNI\">autonomous vehicles</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt609\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CRS-2019_171-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CRS-2019\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-CRS-2019-171\" id=\"mwBNM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBNQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNU\">[</span>159<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNY\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI technologies enable coordination of sensors and effectors, threat detection and identification, marking of enemy positions, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Target_acquisition\" title=\"Target acquisition\" id=\"mwBNc\">target acquisition</a>, coordination and deconfliction of distributed <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Forward_observers_in_the_U.S._military\" title=\"Forward observers in the U.S. military\" id=\"mwBNg\">Joint Fires</a> between networked combat vehicles, both human-operated and autonomous.<sup about=\"#mwt610\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Slyusar-2019_172-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Slyusar-2019\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Slyusar-2019-172\" id=\"mwBNk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBNo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNs\">[</span>160<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBNw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBN0\">AI has been used in military operations in Iraq, Syria, Israel and Ukraine.<sup about=\"#mwt611\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-CRS-2019_171-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"CRS-2019\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-CRS-2019-171\" id=\"mwBN4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBN8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOA\">[</span>159<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOE\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt614\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-173\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-173\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-173\" id=\"mwBOI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBOM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOQ\">[</span>161<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOU\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt617\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Davies-2023_174-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Davies-2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Davies-2023-174\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Davies-2023-174\" id=\"mwBOY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBOc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOg\">[</span>162<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOk\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt620\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-175\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-175\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-175\" id=\"mwBOo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBOs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBOw\">[</span>163<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBO0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"30\" id=\"mwBO4\" aria-labelledby=\"Generative_AI\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Generative_AI\">Generative AI</h3></div>\\n<div class=\"excerpt-block\" about=\"#mwt621\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBO8\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Excerpt\",\"href\":\"./Template:Excerpt\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Generative artificial intelligence\"},\"only\":{\"wt\":\"paragraphs\"},\"paragraphs\":{\"wt\":\"1-3\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><span class=\"mw-empty-elt\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1353838603\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" about=\"#mwt622\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Excerpt/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'>.mw-parser-output .excerpt-hat .mw-editsection-like{font-style:normal}</style><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt623\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable dablink excerpt-hat selfref\">These paragraphs are an excerpt from <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\">Generative AI</a>.<span class=\"mw-editsection-like plainlinks\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a rel=\"mw:ExtLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Generative_AI&amp;action=edit\" class=\"external text\" data-mw-original-href=\"//en.wikipedia.org/w/index.php?title=Generative_AI&amp;action=edit\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></div><div class=\"excerpt\">\\n<p><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\">Generative artificial intelligence</a> (GenAI) is a subfield of artificial intelligence (AI) that uses <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_model\" title=\"Generative model\">generative models</a> to generate text, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_image\" title=\"Digital image\">images</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_video\" title=\"Digital video\">videos</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_audio\" title=\"Digital audio\">audio</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Software_code\" title=\"Software code\" class=\"mw-redirect\">software code</a> or other forms of data.<sup about=\"#mwt626\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-176\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-176\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-176\" id=\"mwBPA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBPE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPI\">[</span>164<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPM\">]</span></span></a></sup> These models <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\">learn the underlying patterns</a> and structures of their <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Training_data\" title=\"Training data\" class=\"mw-redirect\">training data</a>, and use them to generate new data<sup about=\"#mwt631\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-177\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-177\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-177\" id=\"mwBPQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBPU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPY\">[</span>165<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPc\">]</span></span></a></sup> in response to input, which often takes the form of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_language\" title=\"Natural language\">natural language</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Prompt_engineering\" title=\"Prompt engineering\">prompts</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt636\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Generative_AI_nytimes2_178-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Generative AI nytimes2\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Generative_AI_nytimes2-178\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Generative_AI_nytimes2-178\" id=\"mwBPg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBPk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPo\">[</span>166<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBPs\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt641\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Generative_AI_bloomberg2_179-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Generative AI bloomberg2\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Generative_AI_bloomberg2-179\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Generative_AI_bloomberg2-179\" id=\"mwBPw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBP0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBP4\">[</span>167<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBP8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p>The prevalence of generative AI tools has increased significantly since the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_boom\" title=\"AI boom\">AI boom</a> in the 2020s. This boom was made possible by improvements in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_learning\" title=\"Deep learning\">deep</a> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neural_network_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Neural network (machine learning)\">neural networks</a>, particularly <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model\" title=\"Large language model\">large language models</a> (LLMs), which are based on the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transformer_(machine_learning_model)\" title=\"Transformer (machine learning model)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">transformer</a> architecture. Generative AI <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Applications_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Applications of artificial intelligence\">applications</a> include <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatbots\" title=\"Chatbots\" class=\"mw-redirect\">chatbots</a> such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT\" title=\"ChatGPT\">ChatGPT</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Claude_(language_model)\" title=\"Claude (language model)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Claude</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Copilot\" title=\"Microsoft Copilot\">Microsoft Copilot</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepSeek_(chatbot)\" title=\"DeepSeek (chatbot)\">DeepSeek</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doubao\" title=\"Doubao\">Doubao</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gemini_(chatbot)\" title=\"Gemini (chatbot)\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Google Gemini</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Grok_(chatbot)\" title=\"Grok (chatbot)\">Grok</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kimi_(AI)\" title=\"Kimi (AI)\">Kimi</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Qwen\" title=\"Qwen\">Qwen</a>; <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text-to-image\" title=\"Text-to-image\" class=\"mw-redirect\">text-to-image</a> models such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DALL-E\" title=\"DALL-E\">DALL-E</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Adobe_Firefly\" title=\"Adobe Firefly\">Firefly</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stable_Diffusion\" title=\"Stable Diffusion\">Stable Diffusion</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Midjourney\" title=\"Midjourney\">Midjourney</a>; and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Text-to-video\" title=\"Text-to-video\" class=\"mw-redirect\">text-to-video</a> models such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Veo_(text-to-video_model)\" title=\"Veo (text-to-video model)\">Veo</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LTX-2\" title=\"LTX-2\" class=\"mw-redirect\">LTX</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sora_(text-to-video_model)\" title=\"Sora (text-to-video model)\">Sora</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt646\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-180\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-180\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-180\" id=\"mwBQA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBQE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQI\">[</span>168<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQM\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt651\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-181\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-181\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-181\" id=\"mwBQQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBQU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQY\">[</span>169<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQc\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt656\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Generative_AI_Metz-2024_182-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Generative AI Metz-2024\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Generative_AI_Metz-2024-182\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Generative_AI_Metz-2024-182\" id=\"mwBQg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBQk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQo\">[</span>170<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p>Companies in a variety of sectors have used generative AI, including those in software development, healthcare,<sup about=\"#mwt661\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-183\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-183\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-183\" id=\"mwBQw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBQ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQ4\">[</span>171<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBQ8\">]</span></span></a></sup> finance,<sup about=\"#mwt666\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-184\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-184\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-184\" id=\"mwBRA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBRE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBRI\">[</span>172<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBRM\">]</span></span></a></sup> entertainment,<sup about=\"#mwt671\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-185\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-185\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-185\" id=\"mwBRQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBRU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBRY\">[</span>173<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBRc\">]</span></span></a></sup> customer service,<sup about=\"#mwt676\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-186\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-186\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-186\" id=\"mwBRg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBRk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBRo\">[</span>174<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBRs\">]</span></span></a></sup> sales and marketing,<sup about=\"#mwt681\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Generative_AI_economist2_187-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Generative AI economist2\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Generative_AI_economist2-187\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Generative_AI_economist2-187\" id=\"mwBRw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBR0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBR4\">[</span>175<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBR8\">]</span></span></a></sup> art, writing,<sup about=\"#mwt686\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-188\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-188\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-188\" id=\"mwBSA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBSE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBSI\">[</span>176<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBSM\">]</span></span></a></sup> and product design.<sup about=\"#mwt691\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-189\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-189\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-189\" id=\"mwBSQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBSU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBSY\">[</span>177<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBSc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n<link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:Articles_with_excerpts\"/>\\n</div></div>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"31\" id=\"mwBSg\" aria-labelledby=\"Agents\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Agents\">Agents</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt694\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBSk\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Agentic AI\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt695\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt694\" id=\"mwBSo\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Agentic_AI\" title=\"Agentic AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Agentic AI</a></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt696\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBSs\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"OpenClaw\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"CrewAI\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt697\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt696\" id=\"mwBSw\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenClaw\" title=\"OpenClaw\">OpenClaw</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/CrewAI\" title=\"CrewAI\">CrewAI</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBS0\">AI agents are software entities designed to perceive their environment, make decisions, and take actions autonomously to achieve specific goals. These agents can interact with users, their environment, or other agents. AI agents are used in various applications, including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_assistant\" title=\"Virtual assistant\" id=\"mwBS4\">virtual assistants</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatbots\" title=\"Chatbots\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBS8\">chatbots</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Autonomous_vehicles\" title=\"Autonomous vehicles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBTA\">autonomous vehicles</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Video_game_console\" title=\"Video game console\" id=\"mwBTE\">game-playing systems</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Industrial_robotics\" title=\"Industrial robotics\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBTI\">industrial robotics</a>. AI agents operate within the constraints of their programming, available computational resources, and hardware limitations. This means they are restricted to performing tasks within their defined scope and have finite memory and processing capabilities. In real-world applications, AI agents often face time constraints for decision-making and action execution. Many AI agents incorporate learning algorithms, enabling them to improve their performance over time through experience or training. Using machine learning, AI agents can adapt to new situations and optimise their behaviour for their designated tasks.<sup about=\"#mwt700\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-190\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-190\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-190\" id=\"mwBTM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBTQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTU\">[</span>178<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTY\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt703\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-191\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-191\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-191\" id=\"mwBTc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBTg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTk\">[</span>179<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBTo\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt706\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-192\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-192\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-192\" id=\"mwBTs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBTw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBT0\">[</span>180<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBT4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"32\" id=\"mwBT8\" aria-labelledby=\"Web_search\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Web_search\">Web search</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwBUA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft\" title=\"Microsoft\" id=\"mwBUE\">Microsoft</a> introduced <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft_Copilot\" title=\"Microsoft Copilot\" id=\"mwBUI\">Copilot Search</a> in February 2023 under the name <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bing_Chat\" title=\"Bing Chat\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBUM\">Bing Chat</a>. Copilot Search provides AI-generated summaries.<sup about=\"#mwt709\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-193\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-193\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-193\" id=\"mwBUQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBUU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBUY\">[</span>181<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBUc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBUg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\" id=\"mwBUk\">Generative AI</a> features added to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Search\" title=\"Google Search\" id=\"mwBUo\">Google Search</a> include <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Overviews\" title=\"AI Overviews\" id=\"mwBUs\">AI Overviews</a> in May 2024<sup about=\"#mwt712\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-194\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-194\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-194\" id=\"mwBUw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBU0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBU4\">[</span>182<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBU8\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Mode\" title=\"AI Mode\" id=\"mwBVA\">AI Mode</a> in May 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt715\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-195\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-195\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-195\" id=\"mwBVE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBVI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBVM\">[</span>183<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBVQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"33\" id=\"mwBVU\" aria-labelledby=\"Sexuality\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Sexuality\">Sexuality</h3></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBVY\">Applications of AI in this domain include AI-enabled menstruation and fertility trackers that analyse user data to offer predictions,<sup about=\"#mwt718\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-196\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-196\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-196\" id=\"mwBVc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBVg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBVk\">[</span>184<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBVo\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI-integrated sex toys (e.g., <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Teledildonics\" title=\"Teledildonics\" id=\"mwBVs\">teledildonics</a>),<sup about=\"#mwt721\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-197\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-197\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-197\" id=\"mwBVw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBV0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBV4\">[</span>185<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBV8\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI-generated sexual education content,<sup about=\"#mwt724\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-198\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-198\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-198\" id=\"mwBWA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBWE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBWI\">[</span>186<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBWM\">]</span></span></a></sup> and AI agents that simulate sexual and romantic partners (e.g., <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Replika\" title=\"Replika\" id=\"mwBWQ\">Replika</a>).<sup about=\"#mwt727\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-199\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-199\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-199\" id=\"mwBWU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBWY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBWc\">[</span>187<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBWg\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI is also used for the production of non-consensual <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepfake_pornography\" title=\"Deepfake pornography\" id=\"mwBWk\">deepfake pornography</a>, raising significant ethical and legal concerns.<sup about=\"#mwt730\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-200\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-200\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-200\" id=\"mwBWo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBWs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBWw\">[</span>188<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBW0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBW4\">AI technologies have also been used to attempt to identify <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Online_gender-based_violence\" title=\"Online gender-based violence\" id=\"mwBW8\">online gender-based violence</a> and online <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sexual_grooming\" title=\"Sexual grooming\" id=\"mwBXA\">sexual grooming</a> of minors.<sup about=\"#mwt733\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-201\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-201\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-201\" id=\"mwBXE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBXI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBXM\">[</span>189<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBXQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt736\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-202\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-202\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-202\" id=\"mwBXU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBXY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBXc\">[</span>190<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBXg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"34\" id=\"mwBXk\" aria-labelledby=\"Other_industry-specific_tasks\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Other_industry-specific_tasks\">Other industry-specific tasks</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwBXo\">In a 2017 survey, one in five companies reported having incorporated \"AI\" in some offerings or processes.<sup about=\"#mwt739\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-203\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-203\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-203\" id=\"mwBXs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBXw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBX0\">[</span>191<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBX4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \\n\\n<p id=\"mwBX8\">In the field of evacuation and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Disaster\" title=\"Disaster\" id=\"mwBYA\">disaster</a> management, AI has been used to investigate patterns in large-scale and small-scale evacuations using historical data from GPS, videos or social media.<sup about=\"#mwt742\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-204\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-204\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-204\" id=\"mwBYE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBYI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYM\">[</span>192<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt745\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-205\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-205\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-205\" id=\"mwBYU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBYY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYc\">[</span>193<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYg\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt748\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-206\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-206\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-206\" id=\"mwBYk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBYo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYs\">[</span>194<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBYw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBY0\">During the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2024_Indian_general_election\" title=\"2024 Indian general election\" id=\"mwBY4\">2024 Indian elections</a>, US$50 million was spent on authorised AI-generated content, notably by creating <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepfake\" title=\"Deepfake\" id=\"mwBY8\">deepfakes</a> of allied (including sometimes deceased) politicians to better engage with voters, and by translating speeches to various local languages.<sup about=\"#mwt751\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-207\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-207\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-207\" id=\"mwBZA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBZE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZI\">[</span>195<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBZQ\">The use of generative AI by law firms for legal research resulted in the creation of the global \"AI Hallucination Cases\" database, in April 2025, established by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HEC_Paris\" title=\"HEC Paris\" id=\"mwBZU\">HEC Paris</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sciences_Po\" title=\"Sciences Po\" id=\"mwBZY\">Sciences Po</a> legal data analysis lecturer Damien Charlotin.<sup about=\"#mwt754\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-208\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-208\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-208\" id=\"mwBZc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBZg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZk\">[</span>196<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZo\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt757\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-209\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-209\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-209\" id=\"mwBZs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBZw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZ0\">[</span>197<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBZ4\">]</span></span></a></sup> By 2026, judges had issued sanctions and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bar_association\" title=\"Bar association\" id=\"mwBZ8\">bar associations</a> had issued warnings due to attorney submissions to the courts containing fabricated case law citations <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallucination_(artificial_intelligence)\" title=\"Hallucination (artificial intelligence)\" id=\"mwBaA\">hallucinated</a> by AI tools.<sup about=\"#mwt760\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-210\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-210\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-210\" id=\"mwBaE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBaI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBaM\">[</span>198<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBaQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt761\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBaU\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Hallucination (artificial intelligence)#In legal filings\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt762\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt761\" id=\"mwBaY\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hallucination_(artificial_intelligence)#In_legal_filings\" title=\"Hallucination (artificial intelligence)\">Hallucination (artificial intelligence) §<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>In legal filings</a></div>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"35\" id=\"mwBac\" aria-labelledby=\"Ethics\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Ethics\">Ethics</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt763\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBag\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Ethics of artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt764\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt763\" id=\"mwBak\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethics_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Ethics of artificial intelligence\">Ethics of artificial intelligence</a></div><p id=\"mwBao\">AI has potential benefits and potential risks.<sup about=\"#mwt776\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-211\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-211\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-211\" id=\"mwBas\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBaw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBa0\">[</span>199<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBa4\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI may be able to advance science and find solutions for serious problems: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demis_Hassabis\" title=\"Demis Hassabis\" id=\"mwBa8\">Demis Hassabis</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepMind\" title=\"DeepMind\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBbA\">DeepMind</a> hopes to \"solve intelligence, and then use that to solve everything else\".<sup about=\"#mwt765\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESimonite2016_212-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESimonite2016\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESimonite2016-212\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Simonite\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2016\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESimonite2016-212\" id=\"mwBbE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBbI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbM\">[</span>200<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, as the use of AI has become widespread, several unintended consequences and risks have been identified.<sup about=\"#mwt768\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987_213-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987-213\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"987\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987-213\" id=\"mwBbU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBbY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbc\">[</span>201<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbg\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt779\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-214\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-214\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-214\" id=\"mwBbk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBbo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbs\">[</span>202<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBbw\">]</span></span></a></sup> In-production systems can sometimes not factor ethics and bias into their AI training processes, especially when the AI algorithms are inherently unexplainable in deep learning.<sup about=\"#mwt771\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTELaskowski2023_215-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTELaskowski2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELaskowski2023-215\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Laskowski\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTELaskowski2023-215\" id=\"mwBb0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBb4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBb8\">[</span>203<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBcA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"36\" id=\"mwBcE\" aria-labelledby=\"Risks_and_harm\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Risks_and_harm\">Risks and harm</h3></div>\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"37\" id=\"mwBcI\" aria-labelledby=\"Privacy_and_copyright\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Privacy_and_copyright\">Privacy and copyright</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt780\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBcM\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Further\",\"href\":\"./Template:Further\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Information privacy\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial intelligence and copyright\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt781\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt780\" id=\"mwBcQ\">Further information: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_privacy\" title=\"Information privacy\">Information privacy</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_and_copyright\" title=\"Artificial intelligence and copyright\">Artificial intelligence and copyright</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBcU\">Machine learning algorithms require large amounts of data. The techniques used to acquire this data have raised concerns about <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Privacy\" title=\"Privacy\" id=\"mwBcY\">privacy</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surveillance\" title=\"Surveillance\" id=\"mwBcc\">surveillance</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Copyright\" title=\"Copyright\" id=\"mwBcg\">copyright</a>.</p>\\n\\n<!-- PRIVACY PROBLEM -->\\n<p id=\"mwBck\">AI-powered devices and services, such as virtual assistants and IoT products, continuously collect personal information, raising concerns about intrusive data gathering and unauthorised access by third parties. The loss of privacy is further exacerbated by AI\\'s ability to process and combine vast amounts of data, potentially leading to a surveillance society where individual activities are constantly monitored and analysed without adequate safeguards or transparency.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBco\">Sensitive user data collected may include online activity records, geolocation data, video, or audio.<sup about=\"#mwt782\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGAO2022_216-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEGAO2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGAO2022-216\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"GAO\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGAO2022-216\" id=\"mwBcs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBcw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBc0\">[</span>204<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBc4\">]</span></span></a></sup> For example, in order to build <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speech_recognition\" title=\"Speech recognition\" id=\"mwBc8\">speech recognition</a> algorithms, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)\" title=\"Amazon (company)\" id=\"mwBdA\">Amazon</a> has recorded millions of private conversations and allowed <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Temporary_worker\" title=\"Temporary worker\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBdE\">temporary workers</a> to listen to and transcribe some of them.<sup about=\"#mwt785\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEValinsky2019_217-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEValinsky2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEValinsky2019-217\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Valinsky\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2019\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEValinsky2019-217\" id=\"mwBdI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBdM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBdQ\">[</span>205<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBdU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Opinions about this widespread surveillance range from those who see it as a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Necessary_evil\" title=\"Necessary evil\" id=\"mwBdY\">necessary evil</a> to those for whom it is clearly <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unethical\" title=\"Unethical\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBdc\">unethical</a> and a violation of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Right_to_privacy\" title=\"Right to privacy\" id=\"mwBdg\">right to privacy</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt788\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991_218-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991-218\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"991\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991-218\" id=\"mwBdk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBdo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBds\">[</span>206<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBdw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n<!-- PRIVACY SOLUTIONS -->\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBd0\">AI developers argue that this is the only way to deliver valuable applications and have developed several techniques that attempt to preserve privacy while still obtaining the data, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_aggregation\" title=\"Data aggregation\" id=\"mwBd4\">data aggregation</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/De-identification\" title=\"De-identification\" id=\"mwBd8\">de-identification</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Differential_privacy\" title=\"Differential privacy\" id=\"mwBeA\">differential privacy</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt791\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991–992_219-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991–992\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991–992-219\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"991–992\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021991–992-219\" id=\"mwBeE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBeI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBeM\">[</span>207<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBeQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> Since 2016, some privacy experts, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cynthia_Dwork\" title=\"Cynthia Dwork\" id=\"mwBeU\">Cynthia Dwork</a>, have begun to view privacy in terms of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairness_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Fairness (machine learning)\" id=\"mwBeY\">fairness</a>. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Brian_Christian\" title=\"Brian Christian\" id=\"mwBec\">Brian Christian</a> wrote that experts have pivoted \"from the question of \\'what they know\\' to the question of \\'what they\\'re doing with it\\'.\"<sup about=\"#mwt794\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202063_220-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202063\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202063-220\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"63\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202063-220\" id=\"mwBeg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBek\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBeo\">[</span>208<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBes\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- COPYRIGHT AND GENERATIVE AI -->\\n<p id=\"mwBew\">Generative AI is often trained on unlicensed copyrighted works, including in domains such as images or computer code; the output is then used under the rationale of \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fair_use\" title=\"Fair use\" id=\"mwBe0\">fair use</a>\". Experts disagree about how well and under what circumstances this rationale will hold up in courts of law; relevant factors may include \"the purpose and character of the use of the copyrighted work\" and \"the effect upon the potential market for the copyrighted work\".<sup about=\"#mwt797\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEVincent2022_221-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEVincent2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2022-221\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Vincent\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2022-221\" id=\"mwBe4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBe8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBfA\">[</span>209<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBfE\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt808\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-222\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-222\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-222\" id=\"mwBfI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBfM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBfQ\">[</span>210<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBfU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Website owners can indicate that they do not want their content scraped via a \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robots.txt\" title=\"Robots.txt\" id=\"mwBfY\">robots.txt</a>\" file.<sup about=\"#mwt811\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-223\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-223\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-223\" id=\"mwBfc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBfg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBfk\">[</span>211<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBfo\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, some companies will scrape content regardless<sup about=\"#mwt814\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-224\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-224\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-224\" id=\"mwBfs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBfw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBf0\">[</span>212<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBf4\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt817\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-225\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-225\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-225\" id=\"mwBf8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBgA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgE\">[</span>213<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgI\">]</span></span></a></sup> because the robots.txt file has no real authority. In 2023, leading authors (including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Grisham\" title=\"John Grisham\" id=\"mwBgM\">John Grisham</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jonathan_Franzen\" title=\"Jonathan Franzen\" id=\"mwBgQ\">Jonathan Franzen</a>) sued AI companies for using their work to train generative AI.<sup about=\"#mwt800\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEReisner2023_226-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEReisner2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEReisner2023-226\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Reisner\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEReisner2023-226\" id=\"mwBgU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBgY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgc\">[</span>214<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgg\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt803\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAlterHarris2023_227-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEAlterHarris2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlterHarris2023-227\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Alter\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Harris\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAlterHarris2023-227\" id=\"mwBgk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBgo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgs\">[</span>215<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBgw\">]</span></span></a></sup> Another discussed approach is to envision a separate <i id=\"mwBg0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sui_generis\" title=\"Sui generis\" id=\"mwBg4\">sui generis</a></i> system of protection for creations generated by AI to ensure fair attribution and compensation for human authors.<sup about=\"#mwt820\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-228\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-228\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-228\" id=\"mwBg8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBhA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBhE\">[</span>216<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBhI\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"38\" id=\"mwBhM\" aria-labelledby=\"Dominance_by_tech_giants\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Dominance_by_tech_giants\">Dominance by tech giants</h4></div>\\n<p id=\"mwBhQ\">The commercial AI scene is dominated by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_Tech\" title=\"Big Tech\" id=\"mwBhU\">Big Tech</a> companies such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alphabet_Inc.\" title=\"Alphabet Inc.\" id=\"mwBhY\">Alphabet Inc.</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Amazon_(company)\" title=\"Amazon (company)\" id=\"mwBhc\">Amazon</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Apple_Inc.\" title=\"Apple Inc.\" id=\"mwBhg\">Apple Inc.</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms\" title=\"Meta Platforms\" id=\"mwBhk\">Meta Platforms</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft\" title=\"Microsoft\" id=\"mwBho\">Microsoft</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt823\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-229\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-229\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-229\" id=\"mwBhs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBhw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBh0\">[</span>217<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBh4\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt826\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-230\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-230\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-230\" id=\"mwBh8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBiA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiE\">[</span>218<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiI\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt829\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-231\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-231\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-231\" id=\"mwBiM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBiQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiU\">[</span>219<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiY\">]</span></span></a></sup> Some of these players already own the vast majority of existing <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud_computing\" title=\"Cloud computing\" id=\"mwBic\">cloud infrastructure</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computing\" title=\"Computing\" id=\"mwBig\">computing</a> power from <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Data_center\" title=\"Data center\" id=\"mwBik\">data centres</a>, allowing them to entrench further in the marketplace.<sup about=\"#mwt832\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-232\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-232\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-232\" id=\"mwBio\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBis\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBiw\">[</span>220<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBi0\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt835\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-233\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-233\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-233\" id=\"mwBi4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBi8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjA\">[</span>221<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBjI\">For most of 2025-2026, AI-related companies have dominated stock market returns. Recently, investors have started questioning whether the enormous spending on AI infrastructure and data centers will generate sufficient profits, leading to increased volatility in technology and semiconductor stocks. <sup about=\"#mwt839\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-234\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-234\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-234\" id=\"mwBjM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBjQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjU\">[</span>222<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBjY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"39\" id=\"mwBjc\" aria-labelledby=\"Power_needs_and_environmental_impacts\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Power_needs_and_environmental_impacts\">Power needs and environmental impacts</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt840\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBjg\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Environmental impacts of artificial intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"AI build-out financing\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt841\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt840\" id=\"mwBjk\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Environmental_impacts_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Environmental impacts of artificial intelligence\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Environmental impacts of artificial intelligence</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_build-out_financing\" title=\"AI build-out financing\">AI build-out financing</a></div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwBjo\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2015-_Data_center_power_demand_-_US.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwBjs\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2015-_Data_center_power_demand_-_US.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/2015-_Data_center_power_demand_-_US.svg/330px-2015-_Data_center_power_demand_-_US.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/16/2015-_Data_center_power_demand_-_US.svg/960px-2015-_Data_center_power_demand_-_US.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1200\" data-file-height=\"675\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"174\" width=\"310\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.25\" id=\"mwBjw\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwBj0\">Fuelled by a growth in AI, data centres\\' demand for power increased in the 2020s.<sup about=\"#mwt844\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-WashPost_20251225_235-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"WashPost_20251225\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-WashPost_20251225-235\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-WashPost_20251225-235\" id=\"mwBj4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBj8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBkA\">[</span>223<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBkE\">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBkI\">Technology companies have built electricity and artificial intelligence infrastructure to facilitate the AI boom of the 2020s. A 2025 report from the consulting firm <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/McKinsey_&amp;_Company\" title=\"McKinsey &amp; Company\" id=\"mwBkM\">McKinsey &amp; Company</a> estimated that by 2030, $2.7 trillion would be invested into AI infrastructure and data centres in the US, surpassing World War II\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Manhattan_Project\" title=\"Manhattan Project\" id=\"mwBkQ\">Manhattan Project</a> every month.<sup about=\"#mwt847\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-236\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-236\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-236\" id=\"mwBkU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBkY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBkc\">[</span>224<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBkg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBkk\">In January 2024, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Energy_Agency\" title=\"International Energy Agency\" id=\"mwBko\">International Energy Agency</a> (IEA) released <i id=\"mwBks\">Electricity 2024, Analysis and Forecast to 2026</i>.<sup about=\"#mwt850\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-237\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-237\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-237\" id=\"mwBkw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBk0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBk4\">[</span>225<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBk8\">]</span></span></a></sup> This is the first IEA report to make projections for data centres and power consumption by AI and cryptocurrency. The report states that power demand for these uses might double by 2026, with the additional power consumption equaling that of Japan.<sup about=\"#mwt853\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-238\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-238\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-238\" id=\"mwBlA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBlE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBlI\">[</span>226<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBlM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBlQ\">Power consumption by AI is responsible for an increase in fossil fuel use, and has delayed closings of obsolete, carbon-emitting coal energy facilities. A ChatGPT search involves 10 times as much electrical energy as a Google search.<sup about=\"#mwt856\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-239\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-239\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-239\" id=\"mwBlU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBlY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBlc\">[</span>227<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBlg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBlk\">A 2024 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Goldman_Sachs\" title=\"Goldman Sachs\" id=\"mwBlo\">Goldman Sachs</a> research paper, <i id=\"mwBls\">AI Data Centers and the Coming US Power Demand Surge</i>, found \"US power demand (is) likely to experience growth not seen in a generation....\" and forecasts that, by 2030, US data centres will consume 8% of US power, as opposed to 3% in 2022, presaging growth for the electrical power generation industry by a variety of means.<sup about=\"#mwt859\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-240\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-240\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-240\" id=\"mwBlw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBl0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBl4\">[</span>228<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBl8\">]</span></span></a></sup> Data centres\\' need for more and more electrical power is such that they might max out the electrical grid. The Big Tech companies counter that AI can be used to maximise the utilisation of the grid by all.<sup about=\"#mwt862\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-241\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-241\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-241\" id=\"mwBmA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBmE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmI\">[</span>229<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBmQ\">In 2024, <i id=\"mwBmU\">The Wall Street Journal</i> reported that big AI companies have begun negotiations with the US nuclear power providers to provide electricity to the data centres. In March 2024, Amazon purchased a Pennsylvania nuclear-powered data centre for US$650 million.<sup about=\"#mwt865\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-242\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-242\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-242\" id=\"mwBmY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBmc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmg\">[</span>230<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBmk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBmo\">In September 2024, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft\" title=\"Microsoft\" id=\"mwBms\">Microsoft</a> announced an agreement with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Constellation_Energy\" title=\"Constellation Energy\" id=\"mwBmw\">Constellation Energy</a> to re-open the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three_Mile_Island\" title=\"Three Mile Island\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBm0\">Three Mile Island</a> nuclear power plant to provide Microsoft with 100% of all electric power produced by the plant for 20 years. Reopening the plant, which suffered a partial nuclear meltdown of its Unit 2 reactor in 1979, will require Constellation to get through strict regulatory processes which will include extensive safety scrutiny from the US <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_Regulatory_Commission\" title=\"Nuclear Regulatory Commission\" id=\"mwBm4\">Nuclear Regulatory Commission</a>. If approved (this will be the first ever US re-commissioning of a nuclear plant), over 835 megawatts of power – enough for 800,000 homes – will be produced. The cost for re-opening and upgrading is estimated at US$1.6 billion and is dependent on tax breaks for nuclear power contained in the 2022 US <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Inflation_Reduction_Act\" title=\"Inflation Reduction Act\" id=\"mwBm8\">Inflation Reduction Act</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt868\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-243\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-243\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-243\" id=\"mwBnA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBnE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBnI\">[</span>231<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBnM\">]</span></span></a></sup> As of 2024, the US government and the state of Michigan have been investing almost US$2 billion to reopen the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Palisades_Nuclear_Generating_Station\" title=\"Palisades Nuclear Generating Station\" id=\"mwBnQ\">Palisades nuclear reactor</a> on Lake Michigan. Closed since 2022, the plant was scheduled to be reopened in October 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt871\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-244\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-244\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-244\" id=\"mwBnU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBnY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBnc\">[</span>232<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBng\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBnk\">After the last approval in September 2023, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taiwan\" title=\"Taiwan\" id=\"mwBno\">Taiwan</a> suspended the approval of data centres north of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Taoyuan,_Taiwan\" title=\"Taoyuan, Taiwan\" id=\"mwBns\">Taoyuan</a> with a capacity of more than 5 MW in 2024, due to power supply shortages.<sup about=\"#mwt874\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DatacenterDynamics_245-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"DatacenterDynamics\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-DatacenterDynamics-245\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-DatacenterDynamics-245\" id=\"mwBnw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBn0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBn4\">[</span>233<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBn8\">]</span></span></a></sup> Taiwan aims to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nuclear_power_phase-out\" title=\"Nuclear power phase-out\" id=\"mwBoA\">phase out nuclear power</a> by 2025.<sup about=\"#mwt875\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DatacenterDynamics_245-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"DatacenterDynamics\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-DatacenterDynamics-245\" id=\"mwBoE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBoI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBoM\">[</span>233<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBoQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \\n\\n<p id=\"mwBoU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Singapore\" title=\"Singapore\" id=\"mwBoY\">Singapore</a> imposed a ban on the opening of data centres in 2019 due to electric power, but lifted it in 2022.<sup about=\"#mwt876\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-DatacenterDynamics_245-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"DatacenterDynamics\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-DatacenterDynamics-245\" id=\"mwBoc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBog\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBok\">[</span>233<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBoo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBos\">Although most nuclear plants in Japan have been shut down after the 2011 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fukushima_nuclear_accident\" title=\"Fukushima nuclear accident\" id=\"mwBow\">Fukushima nuclear accident</a>, according to an October 2024 <i id=\"mwBo0\">Bloomberg</i> article in Japanese, cloud gaming services company Ubitus, in which Nvidia has a stake, is looking for land in Japan near a nuclear power plant for a new data centre for generative AI.<sup about=\"#mwt879\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-bloombergjp_246-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"bloombergjp\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-bloombergjp-246\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-bloombergjp-246\" id=\"mwBo4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBo8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpA\">[</span>234<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBpI\">On 1 November 2024, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Federal_Energy_Regulatory_Commission\" title=\"Federal Energy Regulatory Commission\" id=\"mwBpM\">Federal Energy Regulatory Commission</a> (FERC) rejected an application submitted by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Talen_Energy\" title=\"Talen Energy\" id=\"mwBpQ\">Talen Energy</a> for approval to supply some electricity from the nuclear power station <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Susquehanna_Steam_Electric_Station\" title=\"Susquehanna Steam Electric Station\" id=\"mwBpU\">Susquehanna</a> to Amazon\\'s data centre.<sup about=\"#mwt882\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Bloomberg20241104_247-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Bloomberg20241104\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Bloomberg20241104-247\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Bloomberg20241104-247\" id=\"mwBpY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBpc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpg\">[</span>235<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBpk\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nAccording to the Commission Chairman <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Willie_L._Phillips\" title=\"Willie L. Phillips\" id=\"mwBpo\">Willie L. Phillips</a>, it is a burden on the electricity grid as well as a significant cost-shifting concern to households and other business sectors.<sup about=\"#mwt883\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Bloomberg20241104_247-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Bloomberg20241104\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Bloomberg20241104-247\" id=\"mwBps\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBpw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBp0\">[</span>235<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBp4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBp8\">In 2025, a report prepared by the IEA estimated the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greenhouse_gas_emissions\" title=\"Greenhouse gas emissions\" id=\"mwBqA\">greenhouse gas emissions</a> from the energy consumption of AI at 180 million tons. By 2035, these emissions could rise to 300–500 million tonnes depending on what measures will be taken. This is below 1.5% of the energy sector emissions. The emissions reduction potential of AI was estimated at 5% of the energy sector emissions, but <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rebound_effect_(conservation)\" title=\"Rebound effect (conservation)\" id=\"mwBqE\">rebound effects</a> (for example if people switch from public transport to autonomous cars) can reduce it.<sup about=\"#mwt886\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-248\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-248\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-248\" id=\"mwBqI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBqM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBqQ\">[</span>236<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBqU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBqY\">In June 2026, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations_University_Institute_for_Water,_Environment_and_Health\" title=\"United Nations University Institute for Water, Environment and Health\" id=\"mwBqc\">United Nations University Institute for Water, Environment and Health</a> released a report about cumulative environmental impacts of AI, not only carbon. The report found that AI has significant negative impacts on land, water, and climate, as it uses large amounts of electricity, requires <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mining\" title=\"Mining\" id=\"mwBqg\">mining</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Critical_raw_materials\" title=\"Critical raw materials\" id=\"mwBqk\">minerals</a>, and generates large amounts of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Electronic_waste\" title=\"Electronic waste\" id=\"mwBqo\">electronic waste</a>. In 2025, data centres consumed more electricity than Saudi Arabia, and ChatGPT alone consumed an amount of water equivalent to the needs of 500,000 people in Sub-Saharan Africa. The negative impacts are not distributed equally across the planet but are concentrated in some places. Data centres are often built in places already suffering from water deficit. For example, AI deployment has already led to an increase in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Water_scarcity\" title=\"Water scarcity\" id=\"mwBqs\">water scarcity</a> in Mexico and Uruguay. It created problems with energy supply in Ireland, which forbade construction of new data centres near Dublin until 2028. Measures can involve tradeoffs, for example, transitioning from coal to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioenergy\" title=\"Bioenergy\" id=\"mwBqw\">bioenergy</a> reduces carbon footprint but increases the impact on land and water. Energy efficiency might not reduce environmental impact, because as AI becomes more efficient, it also becomes cheaper and more widely used.<sup about=\"#mwt889\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-UN_13-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"UN\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-UN-13\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-UN-13\" id=\"mwBq0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBq4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBq8\">[</span>11<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBrA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"40\" id=\"mwBrE\" aria-labelledby=\"Misinformation\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Misinformation\">Misinformation</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt890\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBrI\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Content moderation\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt891\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt890\" id=\"mwBrM\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Content_moderation\" title=\"Content moderation\">Content moderation</a></div>\\n<p id=\"mwBrQ\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/YouTube\" title=\"YouTube\" id=\"mwBrU\">YouTube</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facebook\" title=\"Facebook\" id=\"mwBrY\">Facebook</a> and others use <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recommender_system\" title=\"Recommender system\" id=\"mwBrc\">recommender systems</a> to guide users to more content. These AI programs were given the goal of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_optimization\" title=\"Mathematical optimization\" id=\"mwBrg\">maximising</a> user engagement (that is, the only goal was to keep people watching). The AI learned that users tended to choose <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misinformation\" title=\"Misinformation\" id=\"mwBrk\">misinformation</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conspiracy_theories\" title=\"Conspiracy theories\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBro\">conspiracy theories</a>, and extreme <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Partisan_(politics)\" title=\"Partisan (politics)\" id=\"mwBrs\">partisan</a> content, and, to keep them watching, the AI recommended more of it. Users also tended to watch more content on the same subject, so the AI led people into <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Filter_bubbles\" title=\"Filter bubbles\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBrw\">filter bubbles</a> where they received multiple versions of the same misinformation.<sup about=\"#mwt892\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTENicas2018_249-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTENicas2018\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENicas2018-249\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Nicas\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2018\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTENicas2018-249\" id=\"mwBr0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBr4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBr8\">[</span>237<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsA\">]</span></span></a></sup> This convinced many users that the misinformation was true, and ultimately undermined trust in institutions, the media and the government.<sup about=\"#mwt897\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-250\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-250\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-250\" id=\"mwBsE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBsI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsM\">[</span>238<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> The AI program had correctly learned to maximise its goal, but the result was harmful to society. After the U.S. election in 2016, major technology companies took some steps to mitigate the problem.<sup about=\"#mwt900\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-251\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-251\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-251\" id=\"mwBsU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBsY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsc\">[</span>239<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBsg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBsk\">In the early 2020s, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\" id=\"mwBso\">generative AI</a> began to create images, audio, and texts that are virtually indistinguishable from real photographs, recordings, or human writing,<sup about=\"#mwt912\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-252\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-252\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-252\" id=\"mwBss\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBsw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBs0\">[</span>240<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBs4\">]</span></span></a></sup> while realistic AI-generated videos became feasible in the mid-2020s.<sup about=\"#mwt915\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-253\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-253\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-253\" id=\"mwBs8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBtA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtE\">[</span>241<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtI\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt918\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-254\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-254\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-254\" id=\"mwBtM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBtQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtU\">[</span>242<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtY\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt921\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-255\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-255\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-255\" id=\"mwBtc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBtg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBtk\">[</span>243<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBto\">]</span></span></a></sup> It is possible for bad actors to use this technology to create massive amounts of misinformation and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_propaganda\" title=\"Computational propaganda\" id=\"mwBts\">computational propaganda</a> through techniques such as deepfakes.<sup about=\"#mwt901\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWilliams2023_256-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEWilliams2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilliams2023-256\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Williams\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWilliams2023-256\" id=\"mwBtw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBt0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBt4\">[</span>244<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBt8\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt904\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESamoilenkoSuvorova2023_257-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESamoilenkoSuvorova2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESamoilenkoSuvorova2023-257\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Samoilenko\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Suvorova\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESamoilenkoSuvorova2023-257\" id=\"mwBuA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBuE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBuI\">[</span>245<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBuM\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI pioneer and Nobel Prize-winning computer scientist <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geoffrey_Hinton\" title=\"Geoffrey Hinton\" id=\"mwBuQ\">Geoffrey Hinton</a> expressed concern about AI enabling \"authoritarian leaders to manipulate their electorates\" on a large scale, among other risks.<sup about=\"#mwt907\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTETaylorHern2023_258-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTETaylorHern2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTETaylorHern2023-258\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Taylor\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Hern\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTETaylorHern2023-258\" id=\"mwBuU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBuY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBuc\">[</span>246<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBug\">]</span></span></a></sup> The ability to influence electorates has been proved in at least one study. This same study shows more inaccurate statements from the models when they advocate for candidates of the political right.<sup about=\"#mwt924\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-259\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-259\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-259\" id=\"mwBuk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBuo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBus\">[</span>247<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBuw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBu0\">AI researchers at <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Microsoft\" title=\"Microsoft\" id=\"mwBu4\">Microsoft</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI\" title=\"OpenAI\" id=\"mwBu8\">OpenAI</a>, universities and other organisations have suggested using \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Proof_of_personhood#Approaches\" title=\"Proof of personhood\" id=\"mwBvA\">personhood credentials</a>\" as a way to overcome online deception enabled by AI models.<sup about=\"#mwt927\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-260\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-260\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-260\" id=\"mwBvE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBvI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBvM\">[</span>248<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBvQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"41\" id=\"mwBvU\" aria-labelledby=\"Algorithmic_bias_and_fairness\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Algorithmic_bias_and_fairness\">Algorithmic bias and fairness</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt928\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwBvY\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Algorithmic bias\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Fairness (machine learning)\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt929\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt928\" id=\"mwBvc\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithmic_bias\" title=\"Algorithmic bias\">Algorithmic bias</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairness_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Fairness (machine learning)\">Fairness (machine learning)</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBvg\">Machine learning applications can be <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithmic_bias\" title=\"Algorithmic bias\" id=\"mwBvk\">biased</a><sup about=\"#mwt930\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-262\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-262\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"In statistics, a [[Bias (statistics)|bias]] is a systematic error or deviation from the correct value. But in the context of [[Fairness (machine learning)|fairness]], it refers to a tendency in favour or against a certain group or individual characteristic, usually in a way that is considered unfair or harmful. A statistically unbiased AI system that produces disparate outcomes for different demographic groups may thus be viewed as biased in the ethical sense.&lt;ref name=\\\\\"Samuel-2022\\\\\"/>\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-262\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwBvo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBvs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBvw\">[</span>m<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBv0\">]</span></span></a></sup> if they learn from biased data.<sup about=\"#mwt936\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERose2023_263-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERose2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERose2023-263\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Rose\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERose2023-263\" id=\"mwBv4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBv8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBwA\">[</span>250<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBwE\">]</span></span></a></sup> The developers may not be aware that the bias exists.<sup about=\"#mwt939\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECNA2019_264-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTECNA2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECNA2019-264\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"CNA\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2019\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTECNA2019-264\" id=\"mwBwI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBwM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBwQ\">[</span>251<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBwU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Discriminatory behaviour by some LLMs can be observed in their output.<sup about=\"#mwt950\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-265\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-265\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-265\" id=\"mwBwY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBwc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBwg\">[</span>252<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBwk\">]</span></span></a></sup> Bias can be introduced by the way <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Training_data\" title=\"Training data\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBwo\">training data</a> is selected and by the way a model is deployed.<sup about=\"#mwt942\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGoffrey200817_266-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEGoffrey200817\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGoffrey200817-266\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Goffrey\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2008\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"17\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGoffrey200817-266\" id=\"mwBws\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBww\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBw0\">[</span>253<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBw4\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt945\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERose2023_263-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERose2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERose2023-263\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Rose\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERose2023-263\" id=\"mwBw8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBxA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBxE\">[</span>250<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBxI\">]</span></span></a></sup> If a biased algorithm is used to make decisions that can seriously <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Harm\" title=\"Harm\" id=\"mwBxM\">harm</a> people (as it can in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Health_equity\" title=\"Health equity\" id=\"mwBxQ\">medicine</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Credit_rating\" title=\"Credit rating\" id=\"mwBxU\">finance</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recruitment\" title=\"Recruitment\" id=\"mwBxY\">recruitment</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Public_housing\" title=\"Public housing\" id=\"mwBxc\">housing</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Policing\" title=\"Policing\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBxg\">policing</a>) then the algorithm may cause <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discrimination\" title=\"Discrimination\" id=\"mwBxk\">discrimination</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt955\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-267\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-267\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-267\" id=\"mwBxo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBxs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBxw\">[</span>254<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBx0\">]</span></span></a></sup> The field of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairness_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Fairness (machine learning)\" id=\"mwBx4\">fairness</a> studies how to prevent harms from algorithmic biases.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBx8\">On 28 June 2015, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google_Photos\" title=\"Google Photos\" id=\"mwByA\">Google Photos</a>\\'s new image labelling feature mistakenly identified Jacky Alcine and a friend as \"gorillas\" because they were black. The system was trained on a dataset that contained very few images of black people,<sup about=\"#mwt956\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202025_268-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202025\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202025-268\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"25\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202025-268\" id=\"mwByE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwByI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByM\">[</span>255<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> a problem called \"sample size disparity\".<sup about=\"#mwt959\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995_269-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995-269\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"995\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995-269\" id=\"mwByU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwByY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByc\">[</span>256<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByg\">]</span></span></a></sup> Google \"fixed\" this problem by preventing the system from labelling <i id=\"mwByk\">anything</i> as a \"gorilla\". Eight years later, in 2023, Google Photos still could not identify a gorilla, and neither could similar products from Apple, Facebook, Microsoft and Amazon.<sup about=\"#mwt962\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGrantHill2023_270-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEGrantHill2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGrantHill2023-270\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Grant\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Hill\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGrantHill2023-270\" id=\"mwByo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBys\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwByw\">[</span>257<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBy0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwBy4\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/COMPAS_(software)\" title=\"COMPAS (software)\" id=\"mwBy8\">COMPAS</a> is a commercial program widely used by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/U.S._court\" title=\"U.S. court\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBzA\">U.S. courts</a> to assess the likelihood of a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Defendant\" title=\"Defendant\" id=\"mwBzE\">defendant</a> becoming a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recidivist\" title=\"Recidivist\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwBzI\">recidivist</a>. In 2016, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Julia_Angwin\" title=\"Julia Angwin\" id=\"mwBzM\">Julia Angwin</a> at <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ProPublica\" title=\"ProPublica\" id=\"mwBzQ\">ProPublica</a> discovered that COMPAS exhibited racial bias, despite the fact that the program was not told the races of the defendants. Although the error rate for both whites and blacks was calibrated equal at exactly 61%, the errors for each race were different—the system consistently overestimated the chance that a black person would re-offend and would underestimate the chance that a white person would not re-offend.<sup about=\"#mwt965\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTELarsonAngwin2016_271-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTELarsonAngwin2016\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELarsonAngwin2016-271\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Larson\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Angwin\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2016\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTELarsonAngwin2016-271\" id=\"mwBzU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBzY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzc\">[</span>258<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzg\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2017, several researchers<sup about=\"#mwt968\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-273\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-273\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Including [[Jon Kleinberg]] ([[Cornell University]]), Sendhil Mullainathan ([[University of Chicago]]), Cynthia Chouldechova ([[Carnegie Mellon]]) and Sam Corbett-Davis ([[Stanford]]){{Sfnp|Christian|2020|p=67–70}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-273\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwBzk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBzo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzs\">[</span>n<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBzw\">]</span></span></a></sup> showed that it was mathematically impossible for COMPAS to accommodate all possible measures of fairness when the base rates of re-offence were different for whites and blacks in the data.<sup about=\"#mwt976\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-274\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-274\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-274\" id=\"mwBz0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwBz4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwBz8\">[</span>260<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0A\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB0E\">A program can make biased decisions even if the data does not explicitly mention a problematic feature (such as \"race\" or \"gender\"). The feature will correlate with other features (like \"address\", \"shopping history\" or \"first name\"), and the program will make the same decisions based on these features as it would on \"race\" or \"gender\".<sup about=\"#mwt981\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-275\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-275\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-275\" id=\"mwB0I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB0M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0Q\">[</span>261<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0U\">]</span></span></a></sup> Moritz Hardt said \"the most robust fact in this research area is that fairness through blindness doesn\\'t work.\"<sup about=\"#mwt983\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-276\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-276\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-276\" id=\"mwB0Y\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB0c\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0g\">[</span>262<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB0k\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB0o\">Criticism of COMPAS highlighted that machine learning models are designed to make \"predictions\" that are only valid if we assume that the future will resemble the past. If they are trained on data that includes the results of racist decisions in the past, machine learning models must predict that racist decisions will be made in the future. If an application then uses these predictions as <i id=\"mwB0s\">recommendations</i>, some of these \"recommendations\" will likely be racist.<sup about=\"#mwt993\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-277\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-277\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-277\" id=\"mwB0w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB00\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB04\">[</span>263<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB08\">]</span></span></a></sup> Thus, machine learning is not well suited to help make decisions in areas where there is hope that the future will be <i id=\"mwB1A\">better</i> than the past. It is descriptive rather than prescriptive.<sup about=\"#mwt984\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-279\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-279\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Moritz Hardt (a director at the [[Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems]]) argues that machine learning \\\\\"is fundamentally the wrong tool for a lot of domains, where you&apos;re trying to design interventions and mechanisms that change the world.\\\\\"&lt;ref>Quoted in {{Harvtxt|Christian|2020|p=80}}&lt;/ref>\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-279\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwB1E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB1I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB1M\">[</span>o<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB1Q\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB1U\">Bias and unfairness may go undetected because the developers are overwhelmingly white and male: among AI engineers, about 4% are black and 20% are women.<sup about=\"#mwt994\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995_269-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995-269\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"995\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021995-269\" id=\"mwB1Y\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB1c\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB1g\">[</span>256<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB1k\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB1o\">There are various conflicting definitions and mathematical models of fairness. These notions depend on ethical assumptions, and are influenced by beliefs about society. One broad category is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Distributive_justice\" title=\"Distributive justice\" id=\"mwB1s\">distributive fairness</a>, which focuses on the outcomes, often identifying groups and seeking to compensate for statistical disparities. Representational fairness tries to ensure that AI systems do not reinforce negative <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stereotype\" title=\"Stereotype\" id=\"mwB1w\">stereotypes</a> or render certain groups invisible. Procedural fairness focuses on the decision process rather than the outcome. The most relevant notions of fairness may depend on the context, notably the type of AI application and the stakeholders. The subjectivity in the notions of bias and fairness makes it difficult for companies to operationalise them. Having access to sensitive attributes such as race or gender is also considered by many AI ethicists to be necessary in order to compensate for biases, but it may conflict with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anti-discrimination_law\" title=\"Anti-discrimination law\" id=\"mwB10\">anti-discrimination laws</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt999\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Samuel-2022_261-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Samuel-2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Samuel-2022-261\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Samuel-2022-261\" id=\"mwB14\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB18\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2A\">[</span>249<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2E\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB2I\">At the 2022 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ACM_Conference_on_Fairness,_Accountability,_and_Transparency\" title=\"ACM Conference on Fairness, Accountability, and Transparency\" id=\"mwB2M\">ACM Conference on Fairness, Accountability, and Transparency</a> a paper reported that a CLIP‑based (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Contrastive_Language-Image_Pre-training\" title=\"Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB2Q\">Contrastive Language-Image Pre-training</a>) robotic system reproduced harmful gender‑ and race‑linked stereotypes in a simulated manipulation task. The authors recommended robot‑learning methods which physically manifest such harms be \"paused, reworked, or even wound down when appropriate, until outcomes can be proven safe, effective, and just.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1002\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-280\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-280\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-280\" id=\"mwB2U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB2Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2c\">[</span>265<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2g\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1005\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-281\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-281\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-281\" id=\"mwB2k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB2o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2s\">[</span>266<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB2w\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1008\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-282\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-282\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-282\" id=\"mwB20\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB24\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB28\">[</span>267<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB3A\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"42\" id=\"mwB3E\" aria-labelledby=\"Lack_of_transparency\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Lack_of_transparency\">Lack of transparency</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1009\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB3I\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Explainable AI\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Algorithmic transparency\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"Right to explanation\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1010\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1009\" id=\"mwB3M\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explainable_AI\" title=\"Explainable AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Explainable AI</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithmic_transparency\" title=\"Algorithmic transparency\">Algorithmic transparency</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Right_to_explanation\" title=\"Right to explanation\">Right to explanation</a></div>\\n<p id=\"mwB3Q\">Many AI systems are so complex that their designers cannot explain how they reach their decisions.<sup about=\"#mwt1011\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESample2017_283-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESample2017\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESample2017-283\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Sample\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2017\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESample2017-283\" id=\"mwB3U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB3Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB3c\">[</span>268<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB3g\">]</span></span></a></sup> Particularly with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_neural_networks\" title=\"Deep neural networks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB3k\">deep neural networks</a>, in which there are many non-<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Linear\" title=\"Linear\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB3o\">linear</a> relationships between inputs and outputs. But some popular explainability techniques exist.<sup about=\"#mwt1016\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-284\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-284\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-284\" id=\"mwB3s\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB3w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB30\">[</span>269<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB34\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB38\">It is impossible to be certain that a program is operating correctly if no one knows how exactly it works. There have been many cases where a machine learning program passed rigorous tests, but nevertheless learned something different than what the programmers intended. For example, a system that could identify skin diseases better than medical professionals was found to actually have a strong tendency to classify images with a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ruler\" title=\"Ruler\" id=\"mwB4A\">ruler</a> as \"cancerous\", because pictures of malignancies typically include a ruler to show the scale.<sup about=\"#mwt1017\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian2020110_285-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian2020110\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian2020110-285\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"110\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian2020110-285\" id=\"mwB4E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB4I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB4M\">[</span>270<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB4Q\">]</span></span></a></sup> Another machine learning system designed to help effectively allocate medical resources was found to classify patients with asthma as being at \"low risk\" of dying from pneumonia. Having asthma is actually a severe risk factor, but since the patients having asthma would usually get much more medical care, they were relatively unlikely to die according to the training data. The correlation between asthma and low risk of dying from pneumonia was real, but misleading.<sup about=\"#mwt1020\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202088–91_286-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202088–91\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202088–91-286\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"88–91\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202088–91-286\" id=\"mwB4U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB4Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB4c\">[</span>271<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB4g\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB4k\">People who have been harmed by an algorithm\\'s decision have a right to an explanation.<sup about=\"#mwt1031\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-287\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-287\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-287\" id=\"mwB4o\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB4s\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB4w\">[</span>272<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB40\">]</span></span></a></sup> Doctors, for example, are expected to clearly and completely explain to their colleagues the reasoning behind any decision they make. Early drafts of the European Union\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/General_Data_Protection_Regulation\" title=\"General Data Protection Regulation\" id=\"mwB44\">General Data Protection Regulation</a> in 2016 included an explicit statement that this right exists.<sup about=\"#mwt1023\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-288\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-288\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"When the law was passed in 2018, it still contained a form of this provision.\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-288\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwB48\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB5A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB5E\">[</span>p<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB5I\">]</span></span></a></sup> Industry experts noted that this is an unsolved problem with no solution in sight. Regulators argued that nevertheless the harm is real: if the problem has no solution, the tools should not be used.<sup about=\"#mwt1026\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202091_289-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202091\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202091-289\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"91\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202091-289\" id=\"mwB5M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB5Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB5U\">[</span>273<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB5Y\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB5c\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DARPA\" title=\"DARPA\" id=\"mwB5g\">DARPA</a> established the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explainable_Artificial_Intelligence\" title=\"Explainable Artificial Intelligence\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB5k\">XAI</a> (\"Explainable Artificial Intelligence\") program in 2014 to try to solve these problems.<sup about=\"#mwt1032\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202083_290-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202083\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202083-290\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"83\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202083-290\" id=\"mwB5o\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB5s\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB5w\">[</span>274<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB50\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB54\">Several approaches aim to address the transparency problem. SHAP enables to visualise the contribution of each feature to the output.<sup about=\"#mwt1035\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEVerma2021_291-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEVerma2021\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEVerma2021-291\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Verma\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVerma2021-291\" id=\"mwB58\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB6A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB6E\">[</span>275<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB6I\">]</span></span></a></sup> LIME can locally approximate a model\\'s outputs with a simpler, interpretable model.<sup about=\"#mwt1038\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERothman2020_292-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERothman2020\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERothman2020-292\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Rothman\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERothman2020-292\" id=\"mwB6M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB6Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB6U\">[</span>276<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB6Y\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multitask_learning\" title=\"Multitask learning\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB6c\">Multitask learning</a> provides a large number of outputs in addition to the target classification. These other outputs can help developers deduce what the network has learned.<sup about=\"#mwt1041\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian2020105–108_293-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian2020105–108\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian2020105–108-293\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"105–108\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian2020105–108-293\" id=\"mwB6g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB6k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB6o\">[</span>277<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB6s\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deconvolution\" title=\"Deconvolution\" id=\"mwB6w\">Deconvolution</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepDream\" title=\"DeepDream\" id=\"mwB60\">DeepDream</a> and other <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\" id=\"mwB64\">generative</a> methods can allow developers to see what different layers of a deep network for computer vision have learned, and produce output that can suggest what the network is learning.<sup about=\"#mwt1044\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian2020108–112_294-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian2020108–112\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian2020108–112-294\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"108–112\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian2020108–112-294\" id=\"mwB68\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB7A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB7E\">[</span>278<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB7I\">]</span></span></a></sup> For <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_pre-trained_transformer\" title=\"Generative pre-trained transformer\" id=\"mwB7M\">generative pre-trained transformers</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Anthropic\" title=\"Anthropic\" id=\"mwB7Q\">Anthropic</a> developed a technique based on <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dictionary_learning\" title=\"Dictionary learning\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB7U\">dictionary learning</a> that associates patterns of neuron activations with human-understandable concepts.<sup about=\"#mwt1049\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-295\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-295\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-295\" id=\"mwB7Y\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB7c\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB7g\">[</span>279<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB7k\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"43\" id=\"mwB7o\" aria-labelledby=\"Bad_actors_and_weaponised_AI\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Bad_actors_and_weaponised_AI\">Bad actors and weaponised AI</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1050\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB7s\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Lethal autonomous weapon\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial intelligence arms race\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"AI safety\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1051\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1050\" id=\"mwB7w\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lethal_autonomous_weapon\" title=\"Lethal autonomous weapon\">Lethal autonomous weapon</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_arms_race\" title=\"Artificial intelligence arms race\">Artificial intelligence arms race</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_safety\" title=\"AI safety\">AI safety</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB70\">Artificial intelligence provides a number of tools that are useful to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bad_actor\" title=\"Bad actor\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB74\">bad actors</a>, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Authoritarian\" title=\"Authoritarian\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB78\">authoritarian governments</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terrorist\" title=\"Terrorist\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB8A\">terrorists</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Criminals\" title=\"Criminals\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB8E\">criminals</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rogue_states\" title=\"Rogue states\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB8I\">rogue states</a>.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB8M\">A lethal autonomous weapon is a machine that locates, selects and engages human targets without human supervision.<sup about=\"#mwt1052\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-297\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-297\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"This is the [[United Nations]]&apos; definition, and includes things like [[land mines]] as well.{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=989}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-297\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwB8Q\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB8U\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB8Y\">[</span>q<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB8c\">]</span></span></a></sup> Widely available AI tools can be used by bad actors to develop inexpensive autonomous weapons and, if produced at scale, they are potentially <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weapons_of_mass_destruction\" title=\"Weapons of mass destruction\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB8g\">weapons of mass destruction</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1058\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990_298-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990-298\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"987–990\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990-298\" id=\"mwB8k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB8o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB8s\">[</span>281<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB8w\">]</span></span></a></sup> Even when used in conventional warfare, they currently cannot reliably choose targets and could potentially <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Murder\" title=\"Murder\" id=\"mwB80\">kill an innocent person</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1061\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990_298-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990-298\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"987–990\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021987–990-298\" id=\"mwB84\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB88\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB9A\">[</span>281<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB9E\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2014, 30 nations (including China) supported a ban on autonomous weapons under the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations\" title=\"United Nations\" id=\"mwB9I\">United Nations</a>\\' <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convention_on_Certain_Conventional_Weapons\" title=\"Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons\" id=\"mwB9M\">Convention on Certain Conventional Weapons</a>, however the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_States\" title=\"United States\" id=\"mwB9Q\">United States</a> and others disagreed.<sup about=\"#mwt1064\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021988_299-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021988\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021988-299\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"988\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021988-299\" id=\"mwB9U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB9Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB9c\">[</span>282<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB9g\">]</span></span></a></sup> By 2015, over fifty countries were reported to be researching battlefield robots.<sup about=\"#mwt1069\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-300\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-300\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-300\" id=\"mwB9k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB9o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB9s\">[</span>283<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB9w\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB90\">AI tools make it easier for authoritarian governments to efficiently control their citizens in several ways. Face and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Speaker_recognition\" title=\"Speaker recognition\" id=\"mwB94\">voice recognition</a> allow widespread <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Surveillance\" title=\"Surveillance\" id=\"mwB98\">surveillance</a>. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mwB-A\">Machine learning</a>, operating this data, can <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Classifier_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Classifier (machine learning)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB-E\">classify</a> potential enemies of the state and prevent them from hiding. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recommendation_systems\" title=\"Recommendation systems\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB-I\">Recommendation systems</a> can precisely target <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Propaganda\" title=\"Propaganda\" id=\"mwB-M\">propaganda</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misinformation\" title=\"Misinformation\" id=\"mwB-Q\">misinformation</a> for maximum effect. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deepfakes\" title=\"Deepfakes\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB-U\">Deepfakes</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Generative_AI\" title=\"Generative AI\" id=\"mwB-Y\">generative AI</a> aid in producing misinformation. Advanced AI can make authoritarian <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Technocracy\" title=\"Technocracy\" id=\"mwB-c\">centralised decision-making</a> more competitive than liberal and decentralised systems such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Market_(economics)\" title=\"Market (economics)\" id=\"mwB-g\">markets</a>. It lowers the cost and difficulty of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_warfare\" title=\"Digital warfare\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwB-k\">digital warfare</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spyware\" title=\"Spyware\" id=\"mwB-o\">advanced spyware</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1070\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHarari2018_301-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEHarari2018\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEHarari2018-301\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Harari\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2018\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHarari2018-301\" id=\"mwB-s\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB-w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB-0\">[</span>284<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB-4\">]</span></span></a></sup> All these technologies have been available since 2020 or earlier—AI <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Facial_recognition_system\" title=\"Facial recognition system\" id=\"mwB-8\">facial recognition systems</a> are already being used for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mass_surveillance\" title=\"Mass surveillance\" id=\"mwB_A\">mass surveillance</a> in China.<sup about=\"#mwt1075\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-302\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-302\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-302\" id=\"mwB_E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB_I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB_M\">[</span>285<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB_Q\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1078\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-303\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-303\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-303\" id=\"mwB_U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB_Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB_c\">[</span>286<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB_g\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwB_k\">There are many other ways in which AI is expected to help bad actors, some of which can not be foreseen. For example, machine-learning AI is able to design tens of thousands of toxic molecules in a matter of hours.<sup about=\"#mwt1079\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEUrbinaLentzosInvernizziEkins2022_304-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEUrbinaLentzosInvernizziEkins2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEUrbinaLentzosInvernizziEkins2022-304\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Urbina\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Lentzos\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"Invernizzi\"},\"4\":{\"wt\":\"Ekins\"},\"5\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEUrbinaLentzosInvernizziEkins2022-304\" id=\"mwB_o\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwB_s\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB_w\">[</span>287<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwB_0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"44\" id=\"mwB_4\" aria-labelledby=\"Technological_unemployment\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Technological_unemployment\">Technological unemployment</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1082\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwB_8\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Workplace impact of artificial intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Technological unemployment\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1083\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1082\" id=\"mwCAA\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Workplace_impact_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Workplace impact of artificial intelligence\">Workplace impact of artificial intelligence</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Technological_unemployment\" title=\"Technological unemployment\">Technological unemployment</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCAE\">Economists have frequently highlighted the risks of redundancies from AI, and speculated about unemployment if there is no adequate social policy for full employment.<sup about=\"#mwt1084\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022_305-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022-305\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"McGaughey\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022-305\" id=\"mwCAI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCAM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCAQ\">[</span>288<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCAU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- TOPIC: ESTIMATES OF THE AMOUNT OF UNEMPLOYMENT -->\\n<p id=\"mwCAY\">In the past, technology has tended to increase rather than reduce total employment, but economists acknowledge that \"we\\'re in uncharted territory\" with AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1101\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-306\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-306\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-306\" id=\"mwCAc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCAg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCAk\">[</span>289<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCAo\">]</span></span></a></sup> A survey of economists showed disagreement about whether the increasing use of robots and AI will cause a substantial increase in long-term <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Unemployment\" title=\"Unemployment\" id=\"mwCAs\">unemployment</a>, but they generally agree that it could be a net benefit if <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Productivity\" title=\"Productivity\" id=\"mwCAw\">productivity</a> gains are <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Redistribution_of_income_and_wealth\" title=\"Redistribution of income and wealth\" id=\"mwCA0\">redistributed</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1087\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEIGM_Chicago2017_307-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEIGM Chicago2017\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEIGM_Chicago2017-307\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"IGM Chicago\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2017\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEIGM_Chicago2017-307\" id=\"mwCA4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCA8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCBA\">[</span>290<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCBE\">]</span></span></a></sup> Risk estimates vary; for example, in the 2010s, Michael Osborne and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carl_Benedikt_Frey\" title=\"Carl Benedikt Frey\" id=\"mwCBI\">Carl Benedikt Frey</a> estimated 47% of U.S. jobs are at \"high risk\" of potential automation, while an OECD report classified only 9% of U.S. jobs as \"high risk\".<sup about=\"#mwt1090\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-309\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-309\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"See table 4; 9% is both the OECD average and the U.S. average.{{Sfnp|Arntz|Gregory|Zierahn|2016|p=33}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-309\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCBM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCBQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCBU\">[</span>r<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCBY\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1105\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-310\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-310\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-310\" id=\"mwCBc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCBg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCBk\">[</span>292<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCBo\">]</span></span></a></sup> The methodology of speculating about future employment levels has been criticised as lacking evidential foundation, and for implying that technology, rather than social policy, creates unemployment, as opposed to redundancies.<sup about=\"#mwt1096\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022_305-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022-305\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"McGaughey\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2022\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcGaughey2022-305\" id=\"mwCBs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCBw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCB0\">[</span>288<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCB4\">]</span></span></a></sup> In April 2023, it was reported that 70% of the jobs for Chinese video game illustrators had been eliminated by generative artificial intelligence.<sup about=\"#mwt1108\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-311\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-311\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-311\" id=\"mwCB8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCCA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCCE\">[</span>293<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCCI\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1111\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-312\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-312\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-312\" id=\"mwCCM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCCQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCCU\">[</span>294<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCCY\">]</span></span></a></sup> Early-career workers showed decreasing <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Employment_rate\" title=\"Employment rate\" id=\"mwCCc\">employment rates</a> in some AI-exposed occupations.<sup about=\"#mwt1114\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-o861_313-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"o861\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-o861-313\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-o861-313\" id=\"mwCCg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCCk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCCo\">[</span>295<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCCs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- TOPIC: WHICH JOBS ARE AT RISK? -->\\n<p id=\"mwCCw\">Unlike previous waves of automation, many middle-class jobs may be eliminated by artificial intelligence; <i id=\"mwCC0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Economist\" title=\"The Economist\" id=\"mwCC4\">The Economist</a></i> stated in 2015 that \"the worry that AI could do to white-collar jobs what steam power did to blue-collar ones during the Industrial Revolution\" is \"worth taking seriously\".<sup about=\"#mwt1115\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMorgenstern2015_314-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMorgenstern2015\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMorgenstern2015-314\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Morgenstern\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2015\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMorgenstern2015-314\" id=\"mwCC8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCDA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCDE\">[</span>296<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCDI\">]</span></span></a></sup> Jobs at extreme risk range from <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paralegal\" title=\"Paralegal\" id=\"mwCDM\">paralegals</a> to fast food cooks, while job demand is likely to increase for care-related professions ranging from personal healthcare to the clergy.<sup about=\"#mwt1120\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-315\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-315\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-315\" id=\"mwCDQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCDU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCDY\">[</span>297<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCDc\">]</span></span></a></sup> In July 2025, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ford_Motor_Company\" title=\"Ford Motor Company\" id=\"mwCDg\">Ford</a> CEO <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jim_Farley_(businessman)\" title=\"Jim Farley (businessman)\" id=\"mwCDk\">Jim Farley</a> predicted that \"artificial intelligence is going to replace literally half of all <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/White-collar_worker\" title=\"White-collar worker\" id=\"mwCDo\">white-collar workers</a> in the U.S.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1123\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-316\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-316\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-316\" id=\"mwCDs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCDw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCD0\">[</span>298<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCD4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCD8\">From the early days of the development of artificial intelligence, there have been arguments, for example, those put forward by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Joseph_Weizenbaum\" title=\"Joseph Weizenbaum\" id=\"mwCEA\">Joseph Weizenbaum</a>, who developed the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ELIZA\" title=\"ELIZA\" id=\"mwCEE\">ELIZA</a> chatbot between 1964 and 1966, about whether tasks that can be done by computers actually should be done by them, given the difference between computers and humans, and between quantitative calculation and qualitative, value-based judgement.<sup about=\"#mwt1126\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-317\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-317\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-317\" id=\"mwCEI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCEM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCEQ\">[</span>299<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCEU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"45\" id=\"mwCEY\" aria-labelledby=\"Substitution_for_human–human_interaction\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Substitution_for_human–human_interaction\"><span id=\"Substitution_for_human.E2.80.93human_interaction\" typeof=\"mw:FallbackId\"></span>Substitution for human–human interaction</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1127\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCEc\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"see also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Deaths linked to chatbots\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1128\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1127\" id=\"mwCEg\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deaths_linked_to_chatbots\" title=\"Deaths linked to chatbots\">Deaths linked to chatbots</a></div>\\n<p id=\"mwCEk\">With the increase of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loneliness#increasing_prevalence\" title=\"Loneliness\" id=\"mwCEo\">loneliness</a> in the early 21st century, AI is sometimes identified as a potential source of relief to this problem. It would be possible, via <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_anthropomorphism#Current_anthropomorphic_attributions\" title=\"AI anthropomorphism\" id=\"mwCEs\">human-like qualities built into AI products</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1131\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Anthropomorphism_318-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Anthropomorphism\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Anthropomorphism-318\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Anthropomorphism-318\" id=\"mwCEw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCE0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCE4\">[</span>300<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCE8\">]</span></span></a></sup> for individuals to assume that this need can be met by artificial means.<sup about=\"#mwt1134\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-ReevesNass1996_319-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"ReevesNass1996\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-ReevesNass1996-319\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-ReevesNass1996-319\" id=\"mwCFA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCFE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCFI\">[</span>301<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCFM\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1137\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-NassMoon2000_320-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"NassMoon2000\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NassMoon2000-320\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-NassMoon2000-320\" id=\"mwCFQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCFU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCFY\">[</span>302<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCFc\">]</span></span></a></sup> In some cases, people approach artificial intelligence for companionship when they believe that they would not find acceptance due to feeling outcast.<sup about=\"#mwt1140\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-321\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-321\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-321\" id=\"mwCFg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCFk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCFo\">[</span>303<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCFs\">]</span></span></a></sup> Examples of harm coming to humans from advanced <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chatbots\" title=\"Chatbots\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCFw\">chatbots</a> have been reported in courts in the United States, with AI companies accused of creating products that endanger humans through <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Illusion_of_understanding\" title=\"Illusion of understanding\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCF0\">emotional confusion or deception</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1143\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-322\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-322\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-322\" id=\"mwCF4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCF8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCGA\">[</span>304<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCGE\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1146\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-323\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-323\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-323\" id=\"mwCGI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCGM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCGQ\">[</span>305<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCGU\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"46\" id=\"mwCGY\" aria-labelledby=\"Existential_risk\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Existential_risk\">Existential risk</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1147\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCGc\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Existential risk from artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1148\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1147\" id=\"mwCGg\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Existential_risk_from_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Existential risk from artificial intelligence\">Existential risk from artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCGk\">Recent public debates in artificial intelligence have increasingly focused on its broader societal and ethical implications. It has been argued AI will become so powerful that humanity may irreversibly <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Loss_of_control_(AI)\" title=\"Loss of control (AI)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCGo\">lose control</a> of it. This could, as physicist <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stephen_Hawking\" title=\"Stephen Hawking\" id=\"mwCGs\">Stephen Hawking</a> stated, \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_catastrophic_risk\" title=\"Global catastrophic risk\" id=\"mwCGw\">spell the end of the human race</a>\".<sup about=\"#mwt1149\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECellan-Jones2014_324-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTECellan-Jones2014\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECellan-Jones2014-324\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Cellan-Jones\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2014\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTECellan-Jones2014-324\" id=\"mwCG0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCG4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCG8\">[</span>306<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCHA\">]</span></span></a></sup> This scenario has been common in science fiction, when a computer or robot suddenly develops a human-like \"self-awareness\" (or \"sentience\" or \"consciousness\") and becomes a malevolent character.<sup about=\"#mwt1152\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-326\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-326\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Sometimes called a \\\\\"[[robopocalypse]]\\\\\"{{Sfn|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=1001}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-326\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCHE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCHI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCHM\">[</span>s<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCHQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> These sci-fi scenarios are misleading in several ways.</p>\\n\\n<!-- Unnecessary sentience -->\\n<p id=\"mwCHU\">First, AI does not require human-like <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentience\" title=\"Sentience\" id=\"mwCHY\">sentience</a> to be an existential risk. Modern AI programs are given specific goals and use learning and intelligence to achieve them. Philosopher <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nick_Bostrom\" title=\"Nick Bostrom\" id=\"mwCHc\">Nick Bostrom</a> argued that if one gives <i id=\"mwCHg\">almost any</i> goal to a sufficiently powerful AI, it may choose to destroy humanity to achieve it (he used the example of an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Instrumental_convergence#Paperclip_maximizer\" title=\"Instrumental convergence\" id=\"mwCHk\">automated paperclip factory</a> that destroys the world to get more iron for paperclips).<sup about=\"#mwt1158\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBostrom2014_327-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEBostrom2014\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBostrom2014-327\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Bostrom\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2014\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBostrom2014-327\" id=\"mwCHo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCHs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCHw\">[</span>308<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCH0\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwCH4\">Stuart Russell</a> gives the example of household robot that tries to find a way to kill its owner to prevent it from being unplugged, reasoning that \"you can\\'t fetch the coffee if you\\'re dead.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1161\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussell2019_328-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussell2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussell2019-328\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2019\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussell2019-328\" id=\"mwCH8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCIA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCIE\">[</span>309<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCII\">]</span></span></a></sup> In order to be safe for humanity, a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superintelligence\" title=\"Superintelligence\" id=\"mwCIM\">superintelligence</a> would have to be genuinely <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_alignment\" title=\"AI alignment\" id=\"mwCIQ\">aligned</a> with humanity\\'s morality and values so that it is \"fundamentally on our side\".<sup about=\"#mwt1167\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-329\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-329\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-329\" id=\"mwCIU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCIY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCIc\">[</span>310<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCIg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- Acting in the world is unnecessary -->\\n<p id=\"mwCIk\">Second, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yuval_Noah_Harari\" title=\"Yuval Noah Harari\" id=\"mwCIo\">Yuval Noah Harari</a> argues that AI does not require a robot body or physical control to pose an existential risk. The essential parts of civilisation are not physical. Things like <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ideologies\" title=\"Ideologies\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCIs\">ideologies</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Law\" title=\"Law\" id=\"mwCIw\">law</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Government\" title=\"Government\" id=\"mwCI0\">government</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Money\" title=\"Money\" id=\"mwCI4\">money</a> and the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economy\" title=\"Economy\" id=\"mwCI8\">economy</a> are built on <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Language\" title=\"Language\" id=\"mwCJA\">language</a>; they exist because there are stories that billions of people believe. The current prevalence of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Misinformation\" title=\"Misinformation\" id=\"mwCJE\">misinformation</a> suggests that an AI could use language to convince people to believe anything, even to take actions that are destructive.<sup about=\"#mwt1168\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHarari2023_330-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEHarari2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEHarari2023-330\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Harari\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHarari2023-330\" id=\"mwCJI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCJM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCJQ\">[</span>311<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCJU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Geoffrey Hinton said in 2025 that <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model\" title=\"Large language model\" id=\"mwCJY\">modern AI</a> is particularly \"good at persuasion\" and getting better all the time. He asks, \"Suppose you wanted to invade the capital of the US. Do you have to go there and do it yourself? No. You just have to be good at persuasion.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1171\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEStewart2025_331-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEStewart2025\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEStewart2025-331\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Stewart\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2025\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEStewart2025-331\" id=\"mwCJc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCJg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCJk\">[</span>312<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCJo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- Warnings of existential risk -->\\n<p id=\"mwCJs\">The opinions amongst experts and industry insiders are mixed, with sizeable fractions both concerned and unconcerned by risk from eventual superintelligent AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1174\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMüllerBostrom2014_332-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMüllerBostrom2014\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMüllerBostrom2014-332\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Müller\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Bostrom\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2014\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMüllerBostrom2014-332\" id=\"mwCJw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCJ0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCJ4\">[</span>313<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCJ8\">]</span></span></a></sup> Personalities such as Stephen Hawking, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bill_Gates\" title=\"Bill Gates\" id=\"mwCKA\">Bill Gates</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Elon_Musk\" title=\"Elon Musk\" id=\"mwCKE\">Elon Musk</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1181\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-333\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-333\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-333\" id=\"mwCKI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCKM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCKQ\">[</span>314<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCKU\">]</span></span></a></sup> as well as AI pioneers such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geoffrey_Hinton\" title=\"Geoffrey Hinton\" id=\"mwCKY\">Geoffrey Hinton</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yoshua_Bengio\" title=\"Yoshua Bengio\" id=\"mwCKc\">Yoshua Bengio</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwCKg\">Stuart Russell</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Demis_Hassabis\" title=\"Demis Hassabis\" id=\"mwCKk\">Demis Hassabis</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sam_Altman\" title=\"Sam Altman\" id=\"mwCKo\">Sam Altman</a>, have expressed concerns about existential risk from AI.</p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCKs\">In May 2023, Geoffrey Hinton announced his resignation from Google in order to be able to \"freely speak out about the risks of AI\" without \"considering how this impacts Google\".<sup about=\"#mwt1184\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-334\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-334\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-334\" id=\"mwCKw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCK0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCK4\">[</span>315<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCK8\">]</span></span></a></sup> He notably mentioned risks of an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_takeover\" title=\"AI takeover\" id=\"mwCLA\">AI takeover</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1187\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-335\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-335\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-335\" id=\"mwCLE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCLI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCLM\">[</span>316<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCLQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> and stressed that in order to avoid the worst outcomes, establishing safety guidelines will require cooperation among those competing in use of AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1190\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-336\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-336\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-336\" id=\"mwCLU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCLY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCLc\">[</span>317<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCLg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCLk\">In 2023, many leading AI experts endorsed <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statement_on_AI_risk_of_extinction\" title=\"Statement on AI risk of extinction\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCLo\">the joint statement</a> that \"Mitigating the risk of extinction from AI should be a global priority alongside other societal-scale risks such as pandemics and nuclear war\".<sup about=\"#mwt1191\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEValance2023_337-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEValance2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEValance2023-337\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Valance\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEValance2023-337\" id=\"mwCLs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCLw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCL0\">[</span>318<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCL4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- Arguments against existential risk -->\\n<p id=\"mwCL8\">Some other researchers were more optimistic. AI pioneer <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jürgen_Schmidhuber\" title=\"Jürgen Schmidhuber\" id=\"mwCMA\">Jürgen Schmidhuber</a> did not sign the joint statement, emphasising that in 95% of all cases, AI research is about making \"human lives longer and healthier and easier.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1199\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-338\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-338\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-338\" id=\"mwCME\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCMI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCMM\">[</span>319<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCMQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> While the tools that are now being used to improve lives can also be used by bad actors, \"they can also be used against the bad actors.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1202\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-339\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-339\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-339\" id=\"mwCMU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCMY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCMc\">[</span>320<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCMg\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1205\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-340\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-340\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-340\" id=\"mwCMk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCMo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCMs\">[</span>321<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCMw\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Andrew_Ng\" title=\"Andrew Ng\" id=\"mwCM0\">Andrew Ng</a> also argued that \"it\\'s a mistake to fall for the doomsday hype on AI—and that regulators who do will only benefit vested interests.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1208\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-341\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-341\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-341\" id=\"mwCM4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCM8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCNA\">[</span>322<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCNE\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yann_LeCun\" title=\"Yann LeCun\" id=\"mwCNI\">Yann LeCun</a>, a Turing Award winner, disagreed with the idea that AI will subordinate humans \"simply because they are smarter, let alone destroy [us]\",<sup about=\"#mwt1211\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-342\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-342\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-342\" id=\"mwCNM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCNQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCNU\">[</span>323<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCNY\">]</span></span></a></sup> \"scoff[ing] at his peers\\' dystopian scenarios of supercharged misinformation and even, eventually, human extinction.\" In contrast, he claimed that \"intelligent machines will usher in a new renaissance for humanity, a new era of enlightenment.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1214\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-343\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-343\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-343\" id=\"mwCNc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCNg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCNk\">[</span>324<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCNo\">]</span></span></a></sup> In the early 2010s, experts argued that the risks are too distant in the future to warrant research or that humans will be valuable from the perspective of a superintelligent machine.<sup about=\"#mwt1219\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-344\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-344\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-344\" id=\"mwCNs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCNw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCN0\">[</span>325<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCN4\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, after 2016, the study of current and future risks and possible solutions became a serious area of research.<sup about=\"#mwt1194\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202067,_73_345-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202067, 73\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202067,_73-345\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"67, 73\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202067,_73-345\" id=\"mwCN8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCOA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCOE\">[</span>326<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCOI\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"47\" id=\"mwCOM\" aria-labelledby=\"Ethical_machines_and_alignment\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Ethical_machines_and_alignment\">Ethical machines and alignment</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1220\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCOQ\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Machine ethics\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"AI safety\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"AI alignment\"},\"4\":{\"wt\":\"Friendly artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1221\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1220\" id=\"mwCOU\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_ethics\" title=\"Machine ethics\">Machine ethics</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_safety\" title=\"AI safety\">AI safety</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_alignment\" title=\"AI alignment\">AI alignment</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Friendly_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Friendly artificial intelligence\">Friendly artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1222\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCOY\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Human–AI interaction\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1223\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1222\" id=\"mwCOc\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human–AI_interaction\" title=\"Human–AI interaction\">Human–AI interaction</a></div>\\n<p id=\"mwCOg\">Friendly AI are machines that have been designed from the beginning to minimise risks and to make choices that benefit humans. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eliezer_Yudkowsky\" title=\"Eliezer Yudkowsky\" id=\"mwCOk\">Eliezer Yudkowsky</a>, who coined the term, argues that developing friendly AI should be a higher research priority: it may require a large investment and it must be completed before AI becomes an existential risk.<sup about=\"#mwt1224\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEYudkowsky2008_346-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEYudkowsky2008\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEYudkowsky2008-346\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Yudkowsky\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2008\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEYudkowsky2008-346\" id=\"mwCOo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCOs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCOw\">[</span>327<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCO0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCO4\">Machines with intelligence have the potential to use their intelligence to make ethical decisions. The field of machine ethics provides machines with ethical principles and procedures for resolving ethical dilemmas.<sup about=\"#mwt1227\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011_347-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011-347\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Anderson\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Anderson\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2011\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011-347\" id=\"mwCO8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCPA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCPE\">[</span>328<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCPI\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nThe field of machine ethics is also called computational morality,<sup about=\"#mwt1230\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011_347-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011-347\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Anderson\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Anderson\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2011\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAndersonAnderson2011-347\" id=\"mwCPM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCPQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCPU\">[</span>328<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCPY\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nand was founded at an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AAAI\" title=\"AAAI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCPc\">AAAI</a> symposium in 2005.<sup about=\"#mwt1233\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAAAI2014_348-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEAAAI2014\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAAAI2014-348\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"AAAI\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2014\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAAAI2014-348\" id=\"mwCPg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCPk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCPo\">[</span>329<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCPs\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCPw\">Geoffrey Hinton has suggested researchers explore instilling human-aligned values, such as compassion, into AI systems as a safeguard, speculating about the possibility of building \"maternal instincts\" into AI models, so “they really care about people”.<sup about=\"#mwt1238\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-349\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-349\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-349\" id=\"mwCP0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCP4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCP8\">[</span>330<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCQA\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1241\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-350\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-350\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-350\" id=\"mwCQE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCQI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCQM\">[</span>331<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCQQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCQU\">Other approaches include <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wendell_Wallach\" title=\"Wendell Wallach\" id=\"mwCQY\">Wendell Wallach</a>\\'s \"artificial moral agents\"<sup about=\"#mwt1242\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWallach2010_351-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEWallach2010\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWallach2010-351\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Wallach\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2010\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWallach2010-351\" id=\"mwCQc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCQg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCQk\">[</span>332<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCQo\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwCQs\">Stuart J. Russell</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_Compatible#Russell\\'s_three_principles\" title=\"Human Compatible\" id=\"mwCQw\">three principles</a> for developing provably beneficial machines.<sup about=\"#mwt1245\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussell2019173_352-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussell2019173\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussell2019173-352\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2019\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"173\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussell2019173-352\" id=\"mwCQ0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCQ4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCQ8\">[</span>333<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCRA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"48\" id=\"mwCRE\" aria-labelledby=\"Open_source\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Open_source\">Open source</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1248\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCRI\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Open-source artificial intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Lists of open-source artificial intelligence software\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1249\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1248\" id=\"mwCRM\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Open-source_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Open-source artificial intelligence\">Open-source artificial intelligence</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lists_of_open-source_artificial_intelligence_software\" title=\"Lists of open-source artificial intelligence software\">Lists of open-source artificial intelligence software</a></div>\\n<p id=\"mwCRQ\">Active organisations in the AI open-source community include <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hugging_Face\" title=\"Hugging Face\" id=\"mwCRU\">Hugging Face</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1252\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-353\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-353\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-353\" id=\"mwCRY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCRc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCRg\">[</span>334<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCRk\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google\" title=\"Google\" id=\"mwCRo\">Google</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1255\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-354\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-354\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-354\" id=\"mwCRs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCRw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCR0\">[</span>335<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCR4\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/EleutherAI\" title=\"EleutherAI\" id=\"mwCR8\">EleutherAI</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Meta_Platforms\" title=\"Meta Platforms\" id=\"mwCSA\">Meta</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1258\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-355\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-355\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-355\" id=\"mwCSE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCSI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCSM\">[</span>336<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCSQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> Various AI models, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/LLaMA\" title=\"LLaMA\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCSU\">Llama 2</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mistral_AI\" title=\"Mistral AI\" id=\"mwCSY\">Mistral</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stable_Diffusion\" title=\"Stable Diffusion\" id=\"mwCSc\">Stable Diffusion</a>, have been made open-weight,<sup about=\"#mwt1261\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-356\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-356\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-356\" id=\"mwCSg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCSk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCSo\">[</span>337<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCSs\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1264\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-357\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-357\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-357\" id=\"mwCSw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCS0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCS4\">[</span>338<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCS8\">]</span></span></a></sup> meaning that their architecture and trained parameters (the \"weights\") are publicly available. Open-weight models can be freely <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fine-tuning_(deep_learning)\" title=\"Fine-tuning (deep learning)\" id=\"mwCTA\">fine-tuned</a>, which allows companies to specialise them with their own data and for their own use-case.<sup about=\"#mwt1267\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-358\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-358\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-358\" id=\"mwCTE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCTI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCTM\">[</span>339<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCTQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> Open-weight models are useful for research and innovation but can also be misused. Since they can be fine-tuned, any built-in security measure, such as objecting to harmful requests, can be trained away until it becomes ineffective. Some researchers warn that future AI models may develop dangerous capabilities (such as the potential to drastically facilitate <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bioterrorism\" title=\"Bioterrorism\" id=\"mwCTU\">bioterrorism</a>) and that once released on the Internet, they cannot be deleted everywhere if needed. They recommend pre-release audits and cost-benefit analyses.<sup about=\"#mwt1270\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-359\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-359\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-359\" id=\"mwCTY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCTc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCTg\">[</span>340<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCTk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"49\" id=\"mwCTo\" aria-labelledby=\"Frameworks\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Frameworks\">Frameworks</h3></div>\\n<p id=\"mwCTs\">Artificial intelligence projects can be guided by ethical considerations during the design, development, and implementation of an AI system. An AI framework such as the Care and Act Framework, developed by the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Turing_Institute\" title=\"Alan Turing Institute\" id=\"mwCTw\">Alan Turing Institute</a> and based on the SUM values, outlines four main ethical dimensions, defined as follows:<sup about=\"#mwt1273\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-360\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-360\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-360\" id=\"mwCT0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCT4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCT8\">[</span>341<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCUA\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1276\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-361\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-361\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-361\" id=\"mwCUE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCUI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCUM\">[</span>342<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCUQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n<ul id=\"mwCUU\"><li id=\"mwCUY\"><b id=\"mwCUc\">Respect</b> the dignity of individual people</li>\\n<li id=\"mwCUg\"><b id=\"mwCUk\">Connect</b> with other people sincerely, openly, and inclusively</li>\\n<li id=\"mwCUo\"><b id=\"mwCUs\">Care</b> for the wellbeing of everyone</li>\\n<li id=\"mwCUw\"><b id=\"mwCU0\">Protect</b> social values, justice, and the public interest</li></ul>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCU4\">Other developments in ethical frameworks include those decided upon during the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Asilomar_Conference_on_Beneficial_AI\" title=\"Asilomar Conference on Beneficial AI\" id=\"mwCU8\">Asilomar Conference</a>, the Montreal Declaration for Responsible AI, and the IEEE\\'s Ethics of Autonomous Systems initiative, among others;<sup about=\"#mwt1279\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-362\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-362\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-362\" id=\"mwCVA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCVE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCVI\">[</span>343<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCVM\">]</span></span></a></sup> however, these principles are not without criticism, especially regarding the people chosen to contribute to these frameworks.<sup about=\"#mwt1282\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-363\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-363\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-363\" id=\"mwCVQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCVU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCVY\">[</span>344<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCVc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCVg\">Promotion of the wellbeing of the people and communities that these technologies affect requires consideration of the social and ethical implications at all stages of AI system design, development and implementation, and collaboration between job roles such as data scientists, product managers, data engineers, domain experts, and delivery managers.<sup about=\"#mwt1285\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-364\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-364\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-364\" id=\"mwCVk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCVo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCVs\">[</span>345<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCVw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCV0\">The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Safety_Institute_(United_Kingdom)\" title=\"AI Safety Institute (United Kingdom)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCV4\">UK AI Safety Institute</a> released in 2024 a testing toolset called \\'Inspect\\' for AI safety evaluations available under an MIT open-source licence which is freely available on GitHub and can be improved with third-party packages. It can be used to evaluate AI models in a range of areas including core knowledge, ability to reason, and autonomous capabilities.<sup about=\"#mwt1288\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-365\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-365\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-365\" id=\"mwCV8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCWA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCWE\">[</span>346<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCWI\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"50\" id=\"mwCWM\" aria-labelledby=\"Regulation\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Regulation\">Regulation</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1289\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCWQ\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Regulation of artificial intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Regulation of algorithms\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"AI safety\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1290\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1289\" id=\"mwCWU\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regulation_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Regulation of artificial intelligence\">Regulation of artificial intelligence</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Regulation_of_algorithms\" title=\"Regulation of algorithms\">Regulation of algorithms</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_safety\" title=\"AI safety\">AI safety</a></div>\\n\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwCWY\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Vice_President_Harris_at_the_group_photo_of_the_2023_AI_Safety_Summit.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwCWc\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Vice_President_Harris_at_the_group_photo_of_the_2023_AI_Safety_Summit.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Vice_President_Harris_at_the_group_photo_of_the_2023_AI_Safety_Summit.jpg/330px-Vice_President_Harris_at_the_group_photo_of_the_2023_AI_Safety_Summit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/3/36/Vice_President_Harris_at_the_group_photo_of_the_2023_AI_Safety_Summit.jpg/960px-Vice_President_Harris_at_the_group_photo_of_the_2023_AI_Safety_Summit.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" alt=\"AI Safety Summit\" data-file-width=\"2048\" data-file-height=\"1369\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"201\" width=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.2\" id=\"mwCWg\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwCWk\">The first global <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Safety_Summit_2023\" title=\"AI Safety Summit 2023\" id=\"mwCWo\">AI Safety Summit</a> was held in the United Kingdom in November 2023 with a declaration calling for international cooperation.</figcaption></figure>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCWs\">The regulation of artificial intelligence is the development of public sector policies and laws for promoting and regulating AI; it is therefore related to the broader regulation of algorithms.<sup about=\"#mwt1320\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-366\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-366\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-366\" id=\"mwCWw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCW0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCW4\">[</span>347<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCW8\">]</span></span></a></sup> The regulatory and policy landscape for AI is an emerging issue in jurisdictions globally.<sup about=\"#mwt1291\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTELaw_Library_of_Congress_(U.S.)._Global_Legal_Research_Directorate2019_367-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTELaw Library of Congress (U.S.). Global Legal Research Directorate2019\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELaw_Library_of_Congress_(U.S.)._Global_Legal_Research_Directorate2019-367\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Law Library of Congress (U.S.). Global Legal Research Directorate\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2019\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTELaw_Library_of_Congress_(U.S.)._Global_Legal_Research_Directorate2019-367\" id=\"mwCXA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCXE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCXI\">[</span>348<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCXM\">]</span></span></a></sup> According to AI Index at <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanford\" title=\"Stanford\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCXQ\">Stanford</a>, the annual number of AI-related laws passed in the 127 survey countries jumped from one passed in 2016 to 37 passed in 2022 alone.<sup about=\"#mwt1294\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEVincent2023_368-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEVincent2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2023-368\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Vincent\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2023-368\" id=\"mwCXU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCXY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCXc\">[</span>349<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCXg\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1297\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEStanford_University2023_369-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEStanford University2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEStanford_University2023-369\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Stanford University\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEStanford_University2023-369\" id=\"mwCXk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCXo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCXs\">[</span>350<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCXw\">]</span></span></a></sup> Between 2016 and 2020, more than 30 countries adopted dedicated strategies for AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1300\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021_370-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"UNESCO\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\" id=\"mwCX0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCX4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCX8\">[</span>351<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCYA\">]</span></span></a></sup> Most EU member states had released national AI strategies, as had <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_industry_in_Canada\" title=\"Artificial intelligence industry in Canada\" id=\"mwCYE\">Canada</a>, China, India, Japan, Mauritius, the Russian Federation, Saudi Arabia, United Arab Emirates, U.S., and Vietnam. Others were in the process of elaborating their own AI strategy, including Bangladesh, Malaysia and Tunisia.<sup about=\"#mwt1303\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021_370-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"UNESCO\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\" id=\"mwCYI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCYM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCYQ\">[</span>351<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCYU\">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Partnership_on_Artificial_Intelligence\" title=\"Global Partnership on Artificial Intelligence\" id=\"mwCYY\">Global Partnership on Artificial Intelligence</a> was launched in June 2020, stating a need for AI to be developed in accordance with human rights and democratic values, to ensure public confidence and trust in the technology.<sup about=\"#mwt1306\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021_370-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"UNESCO\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\" id=\"mwCYc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCYg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCYk\">[</span>351<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCYo\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_Kissinger\" title=\"Henry Kissinger\" id=\"mwCYs\">Henry Kissinger</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Eric_Schmidt\" title=\"Eric Schmidt\" id=\"mwCYw\">Eric Schmidt</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Huttenlocher\" title=\"Daniel Huttenlocher\" id=\"mwCY0\">Daniel Huttenlocher</a> published a joint statement in November 2021 calling for a government commission to regulate AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1309\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKissinger2021_371-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEKissinger2021\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKissinger2021-371\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Kissinger\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKissinger2021-371\" id=\"mwCY4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCY8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZA\">[</span>352<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZE\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2023, OpenAI leaders published recommendations for the governance of superintelligence, which they believe may happen in less than 10 years.<sup about=\"#mwt1312\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAltmanBrockmanSutskever2023_372-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEAltmanBrockmanSutskever2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAltmanBrockmanSutskever2023-372\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Altman\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Brockman\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"Sutskever \"},\"4\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAltmanBrockmanSutskever2023-372\" id=\"mwCZI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCZM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZQ\">[</span>353<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZU\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2023, the United Nations also launched an advisory body to provide recommendations on AI governance; the body comprises technology company executives, government officials and academics.<sup about=\"#mwt1323\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-373\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-373\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-373\" id=\"mwCZY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCZc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZg\">[</span>354<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZk\">]</span></span></a></sup> On 1 August 2024, the EU <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_Intelligence_Act\" title=\"Artificial Intelligence Act\" id=\"mwCZo\">Artificial Intelligence Act</a> entered into force, establishing the first comprehensive EU-wide AI regulation.<sup about=\"#mwt1326\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-374\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-374\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-374\" id=\"mwCZs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCZw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZ0\">[</span>355<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCZ4\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2024, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Council_of_Europe\" title=\"Council of Europe\" id=\"mwCZ8\">Council of Europe</a> created the first international legally binding treaty on AI, called the \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Framework_Convention_on_Artificial_Intelligence_and_Human_Rights,_Democracy_and_the_Rule_of_Law\" title=\"Framework Convention on Artificial Intelligence and Human Rights, Democracy and the Rule of Law\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCaA\">Framework Convention on Artificial Intelligence and Human Rights, Democracy and the Rule of Law</a>\". It was adopted by the European Union, the United States, the United Kingdom, and other signatories.<sup about=\"#mwt1329\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-375\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-375\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-375\" id=\"mwCaE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCaI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCaM\">[</span>356<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCaQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCaU\">In a 2022 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ipsos\" title=\"Ipsos\" id=\"mwCaY\">Ipsos</a> survey, attitudes towards AI varied greatly by country; 78% of Chinese citizens, but only 35% of Americans, agreed that \"products and services using AI have more benefits than drawbacks\".<sup about=\"#mwt1330\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEVincent2023_368-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEVincent2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2023-368\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Vincent\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEVincent2023-368\" id=\"mwCac\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCag\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCak\">[</span>349<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCao\">]</span></span></a></sup> A 2023 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Reuters\" title=\"Reuters\" id=\"mwCas\">Reuters</a>/Ipsos poll found that 61% of Americans agree, and 22% disagree, that AI poses risks to humanity.<sup about=\"#mwt1333\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEEdwards2023_376-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEEdwards2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEEdwards2023-376\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Edwards\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEEdwards2023-376\" id=\"mwCaw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCa0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCa4\">[</span>357<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCa8\">]</span></span></a></sup> In a 2023 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fox_News\" title=\"Fox News\" id=\"mwCbA\">Fox News</a> poll, 35% of Americans thought it \"very important\", and an additional 41% thought it \"somewhat important\", for the federal government to regulate AI, versus 13% responding \"not very important\" and 8% responding \"not at all important\".<sup about=\"#mwt1336\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKasperowicz2023_377-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEKasperowicz2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKasperowicz2023-377\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Kasperowicz\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKasperowicz2023-377\" id=\"mwCbE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCbI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCbM\">[</span>358<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCbQ\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1339\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEFox_News2023_378-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEFox News2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEFox_News2023-378\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Fox News\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEFox_News2023-378\" id=\"mwCbU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCbY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCbc\">[</span>359<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCbg\">]</span></span></a></sup> A 2026 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/NBC_News\" title=\"NBC News\" id=\"mwCbk\">NBC News</a> Decision Desk poll powered by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SurveyMonkey\" title=\"SurveyMonkey\" id=\"mwCbo\">SurveyMonkey</a> found that 52% of American adults used AI tools very often or sometimes, but only 18% said they could trust AI-generated information most or almost all of the time, and 70% were more worried than excited about AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1344\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-379\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-379\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-379\" id=\"mwCbs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCbw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCb0\">[</span>360<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCb4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCb8\">In November 2023, the first global <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Safety_Summit_2023\" title=\"AI Safety Summit 2023\" id=\"mwCcA\">AI Safety Summit</a> was held in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bletchley_Park\" title=\"Bletchley Park\" id=\"mwCcE\">Bletchley Park</a> in the UK to discuss the near and far term risks of AI and the possibility of mandatory and voluntary regulatory frameworks.<sup about=\"#mwt1347\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-380\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-380\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-380\" id=\"mwCcI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCcM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCcQ\">[</span>361<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCcU\">]</span></span></a></sup> 28 countries including the United States, China, and the European Union issued a declaration at the start of the summit, calling for international co-operation to manage the challenges and risks of artificial intelligence.<sup about=\"#mwt1350\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-381\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-381\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-381\" id=\"mwCcY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCcc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCcg\">[</span>362<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCck\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1353\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-382\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-382\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-382\" id=\"mwCco\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCcs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCcw\">[</span>363<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCc0\">]</span></span></a></sup> In May 2024 at the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_Seoul_Summit_2024\" title=\"AI Seoul Summit 2024\" id=\"mwCc4\">AI Seoul Summit</a>, 16 global AI tech companies agreed to safety commitments on the development of AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1356\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-383\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-383\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-383\" id=\"mwCc8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCdA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCdE\">[</span>364<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCdI\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1359\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-384\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-384\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-384\" id=\"mwCdM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCdQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCdU\">[</span>365<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCdY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCdc\">In March 2026, the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations\" title=\"United Nations\" id=\"mwCdg\">United Nations</a> convened the inaugural meeting of the Independent International Scientific Panel on AI, a 40-member expert body established under the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Global_Digital_Compact\" title=\"Global Digital Compact\" id=\"mwCdk\">Global Digital Compact</a> to produce annual evidence-based reports on AI\\'s societal impacts.<sup about=\"#mwt1362\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-385\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-385\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-385\" id=\"mwCdo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCds\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCdw\">[</span>366<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCd0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"51\" id=\"mwCd4\" aria-labelledby=\"History\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"History\">History</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1363\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCd8\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"History of artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1364\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1363\" id=\"mwCeA\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/History_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"History of artificial intelligence\">History of artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1365\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCeE\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"For timeline\",\"href\":\"./Template:For_timeline\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1366\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1365\" id=\"mwCeI\">For a chronological guide, see <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Timeline_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Timeline of artificial intelligence\">Timeline of artificial intelligence</a>.</div>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwCeM\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2024_AI_patents_by_country_-_artificial_intelligence.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwCeQ\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:2024_AI_patents_by_country_-_artificial_intelligence.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/2024_AI_patents_by_country_-_artificial_intelligence.svg/250px-2024_AI_patents_by_country_-_artificial_intelligence.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/0c/2024_AI_patents_by_country_-_artificial_intelligence.svg/500px-2024_AI_patents_by_country_-_artificial_intelligence.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1200\" data-file-height=\"750\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"156\" width=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" id=\"mwCeU\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwCeY\">In 2024, AI patents in China and the US numbered more than three-fourths of AI patents worldwide.<sup about=\"#mwt1367\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-RandDworld_20241103_386-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"RandDworld_20241103\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-RandDworld_20241103-386\" id=\"mwCec\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCeg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCek\">[</span>367<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCeo\">]</span></span></a></sup> Though China had more AI patents, the US had 35% more patents per AI patent-applicant company than China.<sup about=\"#mwt1370\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-RandDworld_20241103_386-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"RandDworld_20241103\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-RandDworld_20241103-386\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-RandDworld_20241103-386\" id=\"mwCes\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCew\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCe0\">[</span>367<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCe4\">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>\\n<!-- DON\\'T INCLUDE HISTORICAL PRECURSORS (THEY BELONG TO THE SEPARATE \\'HISTORY OF AI\\' ARTICLE) -->\\n<!-- MAJOR INTELLECTUAL PRECURSORS: LOGIC, THEORY OF COMPUTATION, CYBERNETICS, INFORMATION THEORY, NEUROBIOLOGY, SPECULATION: Antiquity &#x2D; 1955 -->\\n<p id=\"mwCe8\">The study of mechanical or \"formal\" reasoning began with philosophers and mathematicians in antiquity. The study of logic led directly to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Turing\" title=\"Alan Turing\" id=\"mwCfA\">Alan Turing</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theory_of_computation\" title=\"Theory of computation\" id=\"mwCfE\">theory of computation</a>, which suggested that a machine, by shuffling symbols as simple as \"0\" and \"1\", could simulate any conceivable form of mathematical reasoning.<sup about=\"#mwt1371\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219_387-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219-387\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"9\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219-387\" id=\"mwCfI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCfM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCfQ\">[</span>368<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCfU\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1390\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Clarendon_Press-2004_388-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Clarendon Press-2004\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Clarendon_Press-2004-388\" id=\"mwCfY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCfc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCfg\">[</span>369<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCfk\">]</span></span></a></sup> This, along with concurrent discoveries in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cybernetics\" title=\"Cybernetics\" id=\"mwCfo\">cybernetics</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_theory\" title=\"Information theory\" id=\"mwCfs\">information theory</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neurobiology\" title=\"Neurobiology\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCfw\">neurobiology</a>, led researchers to consider the possibility of building an \"electronic brain\".<sup about=\"#mwt1374\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-390\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-390\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"Electronic brain\\\\\" was the term used by the press around this time.{{Sfn|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=9}}&lt;ref>{{Cite web |title=Google books ngram |url=https://books.google.com/ngrams/graph?content=electronic+brain&amp;year_start=1930&amp;year_end=2019&amp;corpus=en-2019&amp;smoothing=3 |access-date=5 October 2024 |archive-date=5 October 2024 |archive-url=https://web.archive.org/web/20241005170209/https://books.google.com/ngrams/graph?content=electronic+brain&amp;year_start=1930&amp;year_end=2019&amp;corpus=en-2019&amp;smoothing=3 |url-status=live}}&lt;/ref>\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-390\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCf0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCf4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCf8\">[</span>t<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCgA\">]</span></span></a></sup> They developed several areas of research that would become part of AI,<sup about=\"#mwt1395\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-391\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-391\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-391\" id=\"mwCgE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCgI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCgM\">[</span>371<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCgQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren_Sturgis_McCulloch\" title=\"Warren Sturgis McCulloch\" id=\"mwCgU\">McCulloch</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Pitts\" title=\"Walter Pitts\" id=\"mwCgY\">Pitts</a> design for \"artificial neurons\" in 1943,<sup about=\"#mwt1387\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117_130-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117-130\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"17\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117-130\" id=\"mwCgc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCgg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCgk\">[</span>120<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCgo\">]</span></span></a></sup> and Turing\\'s influential 1950 paper \\'<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computing_Machinery_and_Intelligence\" title=\"Computing Machinery and Intelligence\" id=\"mwCgs\">Computing Machinery and Intelligence</a>\\', which introduced the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turing_test\" title=\"Turing test\" id=\"mwCgw\">Turing test</a> and showed that \"machine intelligence\" was plausible.<sup about=\"#mwt1396\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Turing_392-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Turing\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Turing-392\" id=\"mwCg0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCg4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCg8\">[</span>372<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwChA\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1399\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Clarendon_Press-2004_388-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Clarendon Press-2004\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Clarendon_Press-2004-388\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Clarendon_Press-2004-388\" id=\"mwChE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwChI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwChM\">[</span>369<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwChQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- 1956&#x2D;1974 -->\\n<p id=\"mwChU\">The field of AI research was founded at <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dartmouth_workshop\" title=\"Dartmouth workshop\" id=\"mwChY\">a workshop</a> at <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dartmouth_College\" title=\"Dartmouth College\" id=\"mwChc\">Dartmouth College</a> in 1956.<sup about=\"#mwt1400\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-394\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-394\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Daniel Crevier wrote, \\\\\"the conference is generally recognized as the official birthdate of the new science.\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Crevier|1993|pp=47–49}} [[Stuart J. Russell|Russell]] and [[Norvig]] called the conference \\\\\"the inception of artificial intelligence.\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=17}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-394\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwChg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwChk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCho\">[</span>u<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwChs\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1428\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Dartmouth_workshop_6-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Dartmouth workshop\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Dartmouth_workshop-6\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Dartmouth_workshop-6\" id=\"mwChw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCh0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCh4\">[</span>4<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCh8\">]</span></span></a></sup> The first AI program, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic_Theorist\" title=\"Logic Theorist\" id=\"mwCiA\">Logic Theorist</a>, was presented at the workshop, created by future Turing Award winner <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allen_Newell\" title=\"Allen Newell\" id=\"mwCiE\">Allen Newell</a> and future Nobel Laureate <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbert_A._Simon\" title=\"Herbert A. Simon\" id=\"mwCiI\">Herbert A. Simon</a>, in collaboration with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cliff_Shaw\" title=\"Cliff Shaw\" id=\"mwCiM\">J. C. Shaw</a>. Many of the workshop attendees became the leaders of AI research in the 1960s.<sup about=\"#mwt1409\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-396\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-396\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Stuart J. Russell|Russell]] and [[Norvig]] wrote \\\\\"for the next 20 years the field would be dominated by these people and their students.\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2003|p=17}}\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-396\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCiQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCiU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCiY\">[</span>v<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCic\">]</span></span></a></sup> They and their students produced programs that the press described as \"astonishing\":<sup about=\"#mwt1415\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-398\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-398\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Stuart J. Russell|Russell]] and [[Norvig]] wrote, \\\\\"it was astonishing whenever a computer did anything kind of smartish\\\\\".{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2003|p=18}}\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-398\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCig\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCik\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCio\">[</span>w<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCis\">]</span></span></a></sup> computers were learning <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Checkers\" title=\"Checkers\" id=\"mwCiw\">checkers</a> strategies, solving word problems in algebra, proving <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theorem\" title=\"Theorem\" id=\"mwCi0\">logical theorems</a> and speaking English.<sup about=\"#mwt1421\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-399\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-399\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"The programs described are [[Arthur Samuel (computer scientist)|Arthur Samuel]]&apos;s checkers program for the [[IBM 701]], [[Daniel Bobrow]]&apos;s [[STUDENT]], [[Allen Newell|Newell]] and [[Herbert A. Simon|Simon]]&apos;s [[Logic Theorist]] and [[Terry Winograd]]&apos;s [[SHRDLU]].\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-399\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCi4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCi8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCjA\">[</span>x<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCjE\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1433\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Succ1_7-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Succ1\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Succ1-7\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Succ1-7\" id=\"mwCjI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCjM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCjQ\">[</span>5<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCjU\">]</span></span></a></sup> Artificial intelligence laboratories were set up at a number of British and U.S. universities in the latter 1950s and early 1960s.<sup about=\"#mwt1434\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Clarendon_Press-2004_388-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Clarendon Press-2004\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Clarendon_Press-2004-388\" id=\"mwCjY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCjc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCjg\">[</span>369<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCjk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- Optimism of the 60s and first AI \"winter\": 1974 -->\\n<p id=\"mwCjo\">Researchers in the 1960s and the 1970s were convinced that their methods would eventually succeed in creating a machine with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_general_intelligence\" title=\"Artificial general intelligence\" id=\"mwCjs\">general intelligence</a> and considered this the goal of their field.<sup about=\"#mwt1435\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTENewquist199486–86_400-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTENewquist199486–86\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENewquist199486–86-400\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Newquist\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1994\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"86–86\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTENewquist199486–86-400\" id=\"mwCjw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCj0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCj4\">[</span>376<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCj8\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1965 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbert_A._Simon\" title=\"Herbert A. Simon\" id=\"mwCkA\">Herbert Simon</a> predicted, \"machines will be capable, within twenty years, of doing any work a man can do\".<sup about=\"#mwt1455\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-401\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-401\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-401\" id=\"mwCkE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCkI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCkM\">[</span>377<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCkQ\">]</span></span></a></sup>In 1967 <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvin_Minsky\" title=\"Marvin Minsky\" id=\"mwCkU\">Marvin Minsky</a> agreed, writing that \"within a generation<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwCkY\">\\xa0</span>... the problem of creating \\'artificial intelligence\\' will substantially be solved\".<sup about=\"#mwt1458\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-402\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-402\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-402\" id=\"mwCkc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCkg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCkk\">[</span>378<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCko\">]</span></span></a></sup> They had, however, underestimated the difficulty of the problem.<sup about=\"#mwt1438\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-404\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-404\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Stuart J. Russell|Russell]] and [[Norvig]] wrote: \\\\\"in almost all cases, these early systems failed on more difficult problems\\\\\".{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=21}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-404\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCks\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCkw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCk0\">[</span>y<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCk4\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1974, both the U.S. and British governments cut off exploratory research in response to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lighthill_report\" title=\"Lighthill report\" id=\"mwCk8\">criticism</a> of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sir_James_Lighthill\" title=\"Sir James Lighthill\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwClA\">Sir James Lighthill</a><sup about=\"#mwt1444\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTELighthill1973_405-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTELighthill1973\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELighthill1973-405\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Lighthill\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1973\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTELighthill1973-405\" id=\"mwClE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwClI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwClM\">[</span>380<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwClQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> and ongoing pressure from the U.S. Congress to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mansfield_Amendment\" title=\"Mansfield Amendment\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwClU\">fund more productive projects</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1447\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTENRC1999212–213_406-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTENRC1999212–213\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENRC1999212–213-406\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"NRC\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1999\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"212–213\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTENRC1999212–213-406\" id=\"mwClY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwClc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwClg\">[</span>381<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwClk\">]</span></span></a></sup> Minsky and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Papert\" title=\"Papert\" id=\"mwClo\">Papert</a>\\'s book <i id=\"mwCls\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Perceptrons_(book)\" title=\"Perceptrons (book)\" id=\"mwClw\">Perceptrons</a></i> was understood as proving that <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_neural_networks\" title=\"Artificial neural networks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCl0\">artificial neural networks</a> would never be useful for solving real-world tasks, thus discrediting the approach altogether.<sup about=\"#mwt1450\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202122_407-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202122\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202122-407\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"22\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202122-407\" id=\"mwCl4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCl8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCmA\">[</span>382<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCmE\">]</span></span></a></sup> The \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_winter\" title=\"AI winter\" id=\"mwCmI\">AI winter</a>\", a period when obtaining funding for AI projects was difficult, followed.<sup about=\"#mwt1464\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-First_AI_Winter_9-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"First AI Winter\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-First_AI_Winter-9\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-First_AI_Winter-9\" id=\"mwCmM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCmQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCmU\">[</span>7<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCmY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- 1980s and second AI winter -->\\n<p id=\"mwCmc\">In the early 1980s, AI research was revived by the commercial success of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expert_system\" title=\"Expert system\" id=\"mwCmg\">expert systems</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1471\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-408\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-408\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-408\" id=\"mwCmk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCmo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCms\">[</span>383<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCmw\">]</span></span></a></sup> a form of AI program that simulated the knowledge and analytical skills of human experts. By 1985, the market for AI had reached over a billion dollars. At the same time, Japan\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fifth_generation_computer\" title=\"Fifth generation computer\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCm0\">fifth generation computer</a> project inspired the U.S. and British governments to restore funding for <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Academic_research\" title=\"Academic research\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCm4\">academic research</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1477\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Fund01_8-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Fund01\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Fund01-8\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Fund01-8\" id=\"mwCm8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCnA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCnE\">[</span>6<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCnI\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, beginning with the collapse of the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lisp_Machine\" title=\"Lisp Machine\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCnM\">Lisp Machine</a> market in 1987, AI once again fell into disrepute, and a second, longer-lasting winter began.<sup about=\"#mwt1483\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Second_AI_Winter_10-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Second AI Winter\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Second_AI_Winter-10\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Second_AI_Winter-10\" id=\"mwCnQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCnU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCnY\">[</span>8<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCnc\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- Embodied robotics, uncertain reasoning, and connectionism in the 1980s -->\\n<p id=\"mwCng\">Up to this point, most of AI\\'s funding had gone to projects that used high-level <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_AI\" title=\"Symbolic AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCnk\">symbols</a> to represent <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mental_objects\" title=\"Mental objects\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCno\">mental objects</a> like plans, goals, beliefs, and known facts. In the 1980s, some researchers began to doubt that this approach would be able to imitate all the processes of human cognition, especially <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_perception\" title=\"Machine perception\" id=\"mwCns\">perception</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotics\" title=\"Robotics\" id=\"mwCnw\">robotics</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Machine_learning\" title=\"Machine learning\" id=\"mwCn0\">learning</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pattern_recognition\" title=\"Pattern recognition\" id=\"mwCn4\">pattern recognition</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1484\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202124_409-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202124\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202124-409\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"24\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202124-409\" id=\"mwCn8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCoA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCoE\">[</span>384<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCoI\">]</span></span></a></sup> and began to look into \"sub-symbolic\" approaches.<sup about=\"#mwt1487\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTENilsson19987_410-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTENilsson19987\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENilsson19987-410\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Nilsson\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1998\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"7\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTENilsson19987-410\" id=\"mwCoM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCoQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCoU\">[</span>385<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCoY\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodney_Brooks\" title=\"Rodney Brooks\" id=\"mwCoc\">Rodney Brooks</a> rejected \"representation\" in general and focussed directly on engineering machines that move and survive.<sup about=\"#mwt1490\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-415\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-415\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[embodied mind|Embodied]] approaches to AI{{Sfnp|McCorduck|2004|pp=454–462}} were championed by [[Hans Moravec]]{{Sfnp|Moravec|1988}} and [[Rodney Brooks]]{{Sfnp|Brooks|1990}} and went by many names: [[Nouvelle AI]].{{Sfnp|Brooks|1990}} [[Developmental robotics]].&lt;ref>[[Developmental robotics]]: {{Harvtxt|Weng|McClelland|Pentland|Sporns|2001}}, {{Harvtxt|Lungarella|Metta|Pfeifer|Sandini|2003}}, {{Harvtxt|Asada|Hosoda|Kuniyoshi|Ishiguro|2009}}, {{Harvtxt|Oudeyer|2010}}&lt;/ref>\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-415\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCog\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCok\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCoo\">[</span>z<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCos\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judea_Pearl\" title=\"Judea Pearl\" id=\"mwCow\">Judea Pearl</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lotfi_Zadeh\" title=\"Lotfi Zadeh\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCo0\">Lotfi Zadeh</a>, and others developed methods that handled incomplete and uncertain information by making reasonable guesses rather than precise logic.<sup about=\"#mwt1518\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Stoch_98-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Stoch\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Stoch-98\" id=\"mwCo4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCo8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCpA\">[</span>90<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCpE\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1512\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202125_416-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202125\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202125-416\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"25\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202125-416\" id=\"mwCpI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCpM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCpQ\">[</span>390<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCpU\">]</span></span></a></sup> But the most important development was the revival of \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Connectionism\" title=\"Connectionism\" id=\"mwCpY\">connectionism</a>\", including neural network research, by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geoffrey_Hinton\" title=\"Geoffrey Hinton\" id=\"mwCpc\">Geoffrey Hinton</a> and others.<sup about=\"#mwt1521\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-417\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-417\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-417\" id=\"mwCpg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCpk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCpo\">[</span>391<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCps\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1990, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yann_LeCun\" title=\"Yann LeCun\" id=\"mwCpw\">Yann LeCun</a> successfully showed that <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Convolutional_neural_networks\" title=\"Convolutional neural networks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCp0\">convolutional neural networks</a> can recognise handwritten digits, the first of many successful applications of neural networks.<sup about=\"#mwt1515\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202126_418-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202126\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202126-418\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"26\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202126-418\" id=\"mwCp4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCp8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCqA\">[</span>392<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCqE\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- 1990s: narrow, formal AI and its detractors -->\\n<p id=\"mwCqI\">AI gradually restored its reputation in the late 1990s and early 21st century by exploiting formal mathematical methods and by finding specific solutions to specific problems. This \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narrow_AI\" title=\"Narrow AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCqM\">narrow</a>\" and \"formal\" focus allowed researchers to produce verifiable results and collaborate with other fields (such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Statistics\" title=\"Statistics\" id=\"mwCqQ\">statistics</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economics\" title=\"Economics\" id=\"mwCqU\">economics</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mathematical_optimization\" title=\"Mathematical optimization\" id=\"mwCqY\">mathematics</a>).<sup about=\"#mwt1524\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Formal_and_narrow_methods_adopted_in_the_1990s_419-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Formal and narrow methods adopted in the 1990s\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Formal_and_narrow_methods_adopted_in_the_1990s-419\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Formal_and_narrow_methods_adopted_in_the_1990s-419\" id=\"mwCqc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCqg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCqk\">[</span>393<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCqo\">]</span></span></a></sup> By 2000, solutions developed by AI researchers were being widely used, although in the 1990s they were rarely described as \"artificial intelligence\" (a tendency known as the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_effect\" title=\"AI effect\" id=\"mwCqs\">AI effect</a>).<sup about=\"#mwt1528\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-420\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-420\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-420\" id=\"mwCqw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCq0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCq4\">[</span>394<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCq8\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nHowever, several academic researchers became concerned that AI was no longer pursuing its original goal of creating versatile, fully intelligent machines. Beginning around 2002, they founded the subfield of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_general_intelligence\" title=\"Artificial general intelligence\" id=\"mwCrA\">artificial general intelligence</a> (or \"AGI\"), which had several well-funded institutions by the 2010s.<sup about=\"#mwt1529\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Artificial_general_intelligence_80-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Artificial general intelligence\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Artificial_general_intelligence-80\" id=\"mwCrE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCrI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCrM\">[</span>72<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCrQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!--DEEP LEARNING BOOM 2012–present-->\\n<p id=\"mwCrU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Deep_learning\" title=\"Deep learning\" id=\"mwCrY\">Deep learning</a> began to dominate industry benchmarks in 2012 and was adopted throughout the field.<sup about=\"#mwt1533\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Deep_learning_revolution_11-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Deep learning revolution\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Deep_learning_revolution-11\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Deep_learning_revolution-11\" id=\"mwCrc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCrg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCrk\">[</span>9<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCro\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nFor many specific tasks, other methods were abandoned.<sup about=\"#mwt1534\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-422\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-422\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Matteo Wong wrote in &apos;&apos;[[The Atlantic]]&apos;&apos;: \\\\\"Whereas for decades, computer-science fields such as natural-language processing, computer vision, and robotics used extremely different methods, now they all use a programming method called \\\\\"deep learning\\\\\". As a result, their code and approaches have become more similar, and their models are easier to integrate into one another.\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Wong|2023}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-422\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCrs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCrw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCr0\">[</span>aa<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCr4\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nDeep learning\\'s success was based on both hardware improvements (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moore\\'s_law\" title=\"Moore\\'s law\" id=\"mwCr8\">faster computers</a>,<sup about=\"#mwt1547\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-423\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-423\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-423\" id=\"mwCsA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCsE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCsI\">[</span>396<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCsM\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graphics_processing_unit\" title=\"Graphics processing unit\" id=\"mwCsQ\">graphics processing units</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cloud_computing\" title=\"Cloud computing\" id=\"mwCsU\">cloud computing</a><sup about=\"#mwt1540\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEClark2015b_424-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEClark2015b\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEClark2015b-424\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Clark\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2015b\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEClark2015b-424\" id=\"mwCsY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCsc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCsg\">[</span>397<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCsk\">]</span></span></a></sup>) and access to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Big_data\" title=\"Big data\" id=\"mwCso\">large amounts of data</a><sup about=\"#mwt1549\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-425\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-425\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-425\" id=\"mwCss\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCsw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCs0\">[</span>398<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCs4\">]</span></span></a></sup> (including curated datasets,<sup about=\"#mwt1543\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEClark2015b_424-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEClark2015b\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEClark2015b-424\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Clark\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2015b\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEClark2015b-424\" id=\"mwCs8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCtA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCtE\">[</span>397<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCtI\">]</span></span></a></sup> such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ImageNet\" title=\"ImageNet\" id=\"mwCtM\">ImageNet</a>). Neural-network approaches also advanced <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Natural_language_processing\" title=\"Natural language processing\" id=\"mwCtQ\">natural language processing</a>. In 2013, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Word2vec\" title=\"Word2vec\" id=\"mwCtU\">word2vec</a> introduced efficient methods for learning distributed <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Word_embedding\" title=\"Word embedding\" id=\"mwCtY\">word representations</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1552\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Apidianaki2023_426-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Apidianaki2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Apidianaki2023-426\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Apidianaki2023-426\" id=\"mwCtc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCtg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCtk\">[</span>399<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCto\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 2014–2015, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seq2seq\" title=\"Seq2seq\" id=\"mwCts\">sequence-to-sequence</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Attention_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Attention (machine learning)\" id=\"mwCtw\">attention</a> mechanisms advanced neural machine translation.<sup about=\"#mwt1555\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-LeCunBengioHinton2015_427-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"LeCunBengioHinton2015\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-LeCunBengioHinton2015-427\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-LeCunBengioHinton2015-427\" id=\"mwCt0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCt4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCt8\">[</span>400<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCuA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCuE\">Deep learning\\'s success led to an enormous increase in interest and funding in AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1556\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-428\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-428\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Jack Clark wrote in [[Bloomberg News|Bloomberg]]: \\\\\"After a half-decade of quiet breakthroughs in artificial intelligence, 2015 has been a landmark year. Computers are smarter and learning faster than ever\\\\\", and noted that the number of software projects that use machine learning at [[Google]] increased from a \\\\\"sporadic usage\\\\\" in 2012 to more than 2,700 projects in 2015.{{Sfnp|Clark|2015b}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-428\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwCuI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCuM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCuQ\">[</span>ab<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCuU\">]</span></span></a></sup> The amount of machine learning research (measured by total publications) increased by 50% in the years 2015–2019.<sup about=\"#mwt1562\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021_370-3\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"UNESCO\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEUNESCO2021-370\" id=\"mwCuY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCuc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCug\">[</span>351<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCuk\">]</span></span></a></sup></p><!-- ALIGNMENT PROBLEM -->\\n\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwCuo\"><a href=\\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:20250202_\"AI\"_(search_term)_on_Google_Trends.svg\\' class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwCus\"><img resource=\\'https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:20250202_\"AI\"_(search_term)_on_Google_Trends.svg\\' src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/20250202_%22AI%22_%28search_term%29_on_Google_Trends.svg/250px-20250202_%22AI%22_%28search_term%29_on_Google_Trends.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/c/cb/20250202_%22AI%22_%28search_term%29_on_Google_Trends.svg/500px-20250202_%22AI%22_%28search_term%29_on_Google_Trends.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"1000\" data-file-height=\"750\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"188\" width=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" id=\"mwCuw\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwCu0\">The number of Google searches for the term \"AI\" accelerated in 2022.</figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwCu4\">In 2016, issues of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithmic_fairness\" title=\"Algorithmic fairness\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCu8\">fairness</a> and the misuse of technology were catapulted into centre stage at machine learning conferences, publications vastly increased, funding became available, and many researchers re-focussed their careers on these issues. The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_alignment\" title=\"AI alignment\" id=\"mwCvA\">alignment problem</a> became a serious field of academic study.<sup about=\"#mwt1565\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202067,_73_345-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202067, 73\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202067,_73-345\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Christian\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"67, 73\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202067,_73-345\" id=\"mwCvE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCvI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCvM\">[</span>326<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCvQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<!-- AI Boom 2020–present -->\\n<p id=\"mwCvU\">In 2015, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AlphaGo\" title=\"AlphaGo\" id=\"mwCvY\">AlphaGo</a>, developed by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/DeepMind\" title=\"DeepMind\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCvc\">DeepMind</a>, beat the world champion <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Go_player\" title=\"Go player\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCvg\">Go player</a>. The program taught only the game\\'s rules and developed a strategy by itself. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GPT-3\" title=\"GPT-3\" id=\"mwCvk\">GPT-3</a> is a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Large_language_model\" title=\"Large language model\" id=\"mwCvo\">large language model</a> that was released in 2020 by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI\" title=\"OpenAI\" id=\"mwCvs\">OpenAI</a> and is capable of generating high-quality human-like text.<sup about=\"#mwt1576\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-429\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-429\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-429\" id=\"mwCvw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCv0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCv4\">[</span>401<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCv8\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ChatGPT\" title=\"ChatGPT\" id=\"mwCwA\">ChatGPT</a>, launched on 30 November 2022, became the fastest-growing consumer software application in history, gaining over 100 million users in two months.<sup about=\"#mwt1579\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-430\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-430\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-430\" id=\"mwCwE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCwI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCwM\">[</span>402<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCwQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> It marked what is widely regarded as AI\\'s breakout year, bringing it into the public consciousness.<sup about=\"#mwt1582\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-431\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-431\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-431\" id=\"mwCwU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCwY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCwc\">[</span>403<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCwg\">]</span></span></a></sup> These programs, and others, inspired an aggressive <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_boom\" title=\"AI boom\" id=\"mwCwk\">AI boom</a>, where large companies began investing billions of dollars in AI research. According to AI Impacts, about US$50 billion annually was invested in \"AI\" around 2022 in the U.S. alone and about 20% of the new U.S. computer science PhD graduates have specialised in \"AI\".<sup about=\"#mwt1568\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDiFeliciantonio2023_432-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEDiFeliciantonio2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDiFeliciantonio2023-432\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"DiFeliciantonio\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDiFeliciantonio2023-432\" id=\"mwCwo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCws\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCww\">[</span>404<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCw0\">]</span></span></a></sup> About 800,000 \"AI\"-related U.S. job openings existed in 2022.<sup about=\"#mwt1571\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGoswami2023_433-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEGoswami2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGoswami2023-433\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Goswami\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2023\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGoswami2023-433\" id=\"mwCw4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCw8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCxA\">[</span>405<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCxE\">]</span></span></a></sup> According to PitchBook research, 22% of newly funded <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Startups\" title=\"Startups\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCxI\">startups</a> in 2024 claimed to be AI companies.<sup about=\"#mwt1585\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-434\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-434\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-434\" id=\"mwCxM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCxQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCxU\">[</span>406<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCxY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"52\" id=\"mwCxc\" aria-labelledby=\"Philosophy\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Philosophy\">Philosophy</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1586\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCxg\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Philosophy of artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1587\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1586\" id=\"mwCxk\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophy_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Philosophy of artificial intelligence\">Philosophy of artificial intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCxo\">Philosophical debates have historically sought to determine the nature of intelligence and how to make intelligent machines.<sup about=\"#mwt1590\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-435\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-435\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-435\" id=\"mwCxs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCxw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCx0\">[</span>407<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCx4\">]</span></span></a></sup> Another major focus has been whether machines can be conscious, and the associated ethical implications.<sup about=\"#mwt1593\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Jarow-2024_436-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Jarow-2024\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Jarow-2024-436\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Jarow-2024-436\" id=\"mwCx8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCyA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyE\">[</span>408<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyI\">]</span></span></a></sup> Many other topics in philosophy are relevant to AI, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Epistemology\" title=\"Epistemology\" id=\"mwCyM\">epistemology</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Free_will\" title=\"Free will\" id=\"mwCyQ\">free will</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1596\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-437\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-437\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-437\" id=\"mwCyU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCyY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyc\">[</span>409<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyg\">]</span></span></a></sup> Rapid advancements have intensified public discussions on the philosophy and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethics_of_AI\" title=\"Ethics of AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwCyk\">ethics of AI</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1597\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Jarow-2024_436-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Jarow-2024\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Jarow-2024-436\" id=\"mwCyo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCys\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCyw\">[</span>408<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCy0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"53\" id=\"mwCy4\" aria-labelledby=\"Defining_artificial_intelligence\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Defining_artificial_intelligence\">Defining artificial intelligence</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1598\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwCy8\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Synthetic intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Intelligent agent\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial mind (disambiguation){{!}}Artificial mind\"},\"4\":{\"wt\":\"Virtual intelligence\"},\"5\":{\"wt\":\"Dartmouth workshop\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1599\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1598\" id=\"mwCzA\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Synthetic_intelligence\" title=\"Synthetic intelligence\">Synthetic intelligence</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligent_agent\" title=\"Intelligent agent\">Intelligent agent</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_mind_(disambiguation)\" title=\"Artificial mind (disambiguation)\" class=\"mw-redirect mw-disambig\">Artificial mind</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Virtual_intelligence\" title=\"Virtual intelligence\">Virtual intelligence</a>, and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dartmouth_workshop\" title=\"Dartmouth workshop\">Dartmouth workshop</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwCzE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Turing\" title=\"Alan Turing\" id=\"mwCzI\">Alan Turing</a> investigated whether machines can show intelligent behaviour and think. In 1950, he proposed the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Turing_test\" title=\"Turing test\" id=\"mwCzM\">Turing test</a>, which measures the ability of a machine to simulate human conversation.<sup about=\"#mwt1605\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-438\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-438\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-438\" id=\"mwCzQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCzU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzY\">[</span>410<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzc\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1611\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Turing_392-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Turing\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Turing-392\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Turing-392\" id=\"mwCzg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCzk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzo\">[</span>372<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCzs\">]</span></span></a></sup> Since we can only observe the behaviour of the machine, it does not matter if it is \"actually\" thinking or literally has a \"mind\". Turing notes that <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Problem_of_other_minds\" title=\"Problem of other minds\" id=\"mwCzw\">we can not determine these things about other people</a> but \"it is usual to have a polite convention that everyone thinks.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1600\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\\'cite_ref-FOOTNOTETuring1950Under_\"The_Argument_from_Consciousness\"_439-0\\' rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTETuring1950Under \\\\\"The Argument from Consciousness\\\\\"\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTETuring1950Under_\\\\\"The_Argument_from_Consciousness\\\\\"-439\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Turing\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1950\"},\"loc\":{\"wt\":\"Under \\\\\"The Argument from Consciousness\\\\\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\\'#cite_note-FOOTNOTETuring1950Under_\"The_Argument_from_Consciousness\"-439\\' id=\"mwCz0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwCz4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwCz8\">[</span>411<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC0A\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwC0E\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Weakness_of_Turing_test_1.svg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwC0I\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Weakness_of_Turing_test_1.svg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Weakness_of_Turing_test_1.svg/250px-Weakness_of_Turing_test_1.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/57/Weakness_of_Turing_test_1.svg/500px-Weakness_of_Turing_test_1.svg.png?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail 2x\" data-file-width=\"433\" data-file-height=\"316\" data-file-type=\"drawing\" height=\"182\" width=\"250\" class=\"mw-file-element\" id=\"mwC0M\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwC0Q\">The Turing test can provide some evidence of intelligence, but it penalises non-human intelligent behaviour.<sup about=\"#mwt1614\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-440\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-440\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-440\" id=\"mwC0U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC0Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC0c\">[</span>412<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC0g\">]</span></span></a></sup></figcaption></figure>\\n<p id=\"mwC0k\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwC0o\">Russell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norvig\" title=\"Norvig\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC0s\">Norvig</a> agree with Turing that intelligence must be defined in terms of external behaviour, not internal structure.<sup about=\"#mwt1615\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4_1-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"1–4\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\" id=\"mwC0w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC00\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC04\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC08\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, they are critical that the test requires the machine to imitate humans. \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aeronautics\" title=\"Aeronautics\" id=\"mwC1A\">Aeronautical engineering</a> texts\", they wrote, \"do not define the goal of their field as making \\'machines that fly so exactly like <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pigeon\" title=\"Pigeon\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC1E\">pigeons</a> that they can fool other pigeons.<span style=\"padding-right:.15em;\" about=\"#mwt1618\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC1I\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"&apos; \\\\\"\",\"href\":\"./Template:&apos;_\\\\\"\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}\\'>\\'</span><span about=\"#mwt1618\">\"</span><sup about=\"#mwt1619\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20213_441-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20213\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20213-441\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"3\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20213-441\" id=\"mwC1M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC1Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1U\">[</span>413<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1Y\">]</span></span></a></sup> AI founder <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_McCarthy_(computer_scientist)\" title=\"John McCarthy (computer scientist)\" id=\"mwC1c\">John McCarthy</a> agreed, writing that \"Artificial intelligence is not, by definition, simulation of human intelligence\".<sup about=\"#mwt1622\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMaker2006_442-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMaker2006\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMaker2006-442\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Maker\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2006\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMaker2006-442\" id=\"mwC1g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC1k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1o\">[</span>414<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC1s\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC1w\">McCarthy defines intelligence as \"the computational part of the ability to achieve goals in the world\".<sup about=\"#mwt1625\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcCarthy1999_443-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMcCarthy1999\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCarthy1999-443\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"McCarthy\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1999\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCarthy1999-443\" id=\"mwC10\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC14\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC18\">[</span>415<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2A\">]</span></span></a></sup> Another AI founder, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Marvin_Minsky\" title=\"Marvin Minsky\" id=\"mwC2E\">Marvin Minsky</a>, similarly describes it as \"the ability to solve hard problems\".<sup about=\"#mwt1628\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMinsky1986_444-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMinsky1986\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinsky1986-444\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Minsky\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1986\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMinsky1986-444\" id=\"mwC2I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC2M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2Q\">[</span>416<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2U\">]</span></span></a></sup> <i id=\"mwC2Y\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_Intelligence:_A_Modern_Approach\" title=\"Artificial Intelligence: A Modern Approach\" id=\"mwC2c\">Artificial Intelligence: A Modern Approach</a></i> defines it as the study of agents that perceive their environment and take actions that maximise their chances of achieving defined goals.<sup about=\"#mwt1631\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4_1-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"1–4\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\" id=\"mwC2g\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC2k\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2o\">[</span>1<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC2s\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \\n\\n<p id=\"mwC2w\">The many differing definitions of AI have been critically analysed.<sup about=\"#mwt1636\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-445\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-445\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-445\" id=\"mwC20\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC24\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC28\">[</span>417<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3A\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1639\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-446\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-446\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-446\" id=\"mwC3E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC3I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3M\">[</span>418<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3Q\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1642\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-447\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-447\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-447\" id=\"mwC3U\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC3Y\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3c\">[</span>419<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3g\">]</span></span></a></sup> During the 2020s AI boom, the term has been used as a marketing <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Buzzword\" title=\"Buzzword\" id=\"mwC3k\">buzzword</a> to promote products and services which do not use AI.<sup about=\"#mwt1645\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-448\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-448\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-448\" id=\"mwC3o\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC3s\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC3w\">[</span>420<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC30\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"54\" id=\"mwC34\" aria-labelledby=\"Legal_definitions\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Legal_definitions\">Legal definitions</h4></div>\\n<p id=\"mwC38\">The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/International_Organization_for_Standardization\" title=\"International Organization for Standardization\" id=\"mwC4A\">International Organization for Standardization</a> describes an AI system as a \"an engineered system that generates outputs such as content, forecasts, recommendations, or decisions for a given set of human‑defined objectives, and can operate with varying levels of automation\".<sup about=\"#mwt1648\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-449\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-449\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-449\" id=\"mwC4E\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC4I\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4M\">[</span>421<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4Q\">]</span></span></a></sup> The <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_Intelligence_Act\" title=\"Artificial Intelligence Act\" id=\"mwC4U\">EU AI Act</a> defines an AI system as \"a machine-based system that is designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy and that may exhibit adaptiveness after deployment, and that, for explicit or implicit objectives, infers, from the input it receives, how to generate outputs such as predictions, content, recommendations, or decisions that can influence physical or virtual environments\".<sup about=\"#mwt1651\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-450\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-450\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-450\" id=\"mwC4Y\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC4c\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4g\">[</span>422<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC4k\">]</span></span></a></sup> In the United States, influential but non‑binding guidance such as the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/National_Institute_of_Standards_and_Technology\" title=\"National Institute of Standards and Technology\" id=\"mwC4o\">National Institute of Standards and Technology</a>\\'s AI Risk Management Framework describes an AI system as \"an engineered or machine-based system that can, for a given set of objectives, generate outputs such as predictions, recommendations, or decisions influencing real or virtual environments. AI systems are designed to operate with varying levels of autonomy\".<sup about=\"#mwt1654\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-451\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-451\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-451\" id=\"mwC4s\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC4w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC40\">[</span>423<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC44\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"55\" id=\"mwC48\" aria-labelledby=\"Evaluating_approaches_to_AI\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Evaluating_approaches_to_AI\">Evaluating approaches to AI</h3></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC5A\">No established unifying theory or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paradigm\" title=\"Paradigm\" id=\"mwC5E\">paradigm</a> has guided AI research for most of its history.<sup about=\"#mwt1655\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-453\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-453\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"[[Nils Nilsson (researcher)|Nils Nilsson]] wrote in 1983: \\\\\"Simply put, there is wide disagreement in the field about what AI is all about.\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Nilsson|1983|p=10}}\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-453\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwC5I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC5M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC5Q\">[</span>ac<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC5U\">]</span></span></a></sup> The unprecedented success of statistical machine learning in the 2010s eclipsed all other approaches (so much so that some sources, especially in the business world, use the term \"artificial intelligence\" to mean \"machine learning with neural networks\"). This approach is mostly <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sub-symbolic\" title=\"Sub-symbolic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC5Y\">sub-symbolic</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_computing\" title=\"Soft computing\" id=\"mwC5c\">soft</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Narrow_AI\" title=\"Narrow AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC5g\">narrow</a>.</p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"56\" id=\"mwC5k\" aria-labelledby=\"Symbolic_AI_and_its_limits\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Symbolic_AI_and_its_limits\">Symbolic AI and its limits</h4></div>\\n<p id=\"mwC5o\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Symbolic_AI\" title=\"Symbolic AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC5s\">Symbolic AI</a> (or \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/GOFAI\" title=\"GOFAI\" id=\"mwC5w\">GOFAI</a>\")<sup about=\"#mwt1661\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHaugeland1985112–117_454-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEHaugeland1985112–117\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEHaugeland1985112–117-454\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Haugeland\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1985\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"112–117\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHaugeland1985112–117-454\" id=\"mwC50\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC54\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC58\">[</span>425<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6A\">]</span></span></a></sup> simulated the high-level conscious reasoning that people use when they solve puzzles, express legal reasoning and do mathematics. It was highly successful at some \"intelligent\" tasks such as algebra or IQ tests. In 1976, Newell and Simon proposed the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Physical_symbol_systems_hypothesis\" title=\"Physical symbol systems hypothesis\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC6E\">physical symbol systems hypothesis</a>: \"A physical symbol system has the necessary and sufficient means of general intelligent action.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1667\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-455\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-455\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-455\" id=\"mwC6I\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC6M\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6Q\">[</span>426<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6U\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC6Y\">However, the symbolic approach failed on many tasks that humans solve easily, such as learning, recognising an object or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Commonsense_reasoning\" title=\"Commonsense reasoning\" id=\"mwC6c\">commonsense reasoning</a>. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moravec\\'s_paradox\" title=\"Moravec\\'s paradox\" id=\"mwC6g\">Moravec\\'s paradox</a> is the discovery that high-level \"intelligent\" tasks were easy for AI, but low level \"instinctive\" tasks were extremely difficult.<sup about=\"#mwt1677\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-456\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-456\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-456\" id=\"mwC6k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC6o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6s\">[</span>427<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC6w\">]</span></span></a></sup> Philosopher <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hubert_Dreyfus\" title=\"Hubert Dreyfus\" id=\"mwC60\">Hubert Dreyfus</a> had <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Dreyfus\\'_critique_of_AI\" title=\"Dreyfus\\' critique of AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC64\">argued</a> since the 1960s that human expertise depends on embodied, situational know-how that is not representable as explicit symbolic rules rather than conscious symbol manipulation, and on having a \"feel\" for the situation, rather than explicit symbolic knowledge.<sup about=\"#mwt1684\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-457\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-457\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-457\" id=\"mwC68\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC7A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7E\">[</span>428<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7I\">]</span></span></a></sup> Although his arguments had been ridiculed and ignored when they were first presented, eventually, AI research came to agree with him.<sup about=\"#mwt1668\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-459\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-459\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\\\\n\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Daniel Crevier wrote that \\\\\"time has proven the accuracy and perceptiveness of some of Dreyfus&apos;s comments. Had he formulated them less aggressively, constructive actions they suggested might have been taken much earlier.\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Crevier|1993|p=125}}\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-459\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwC7M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC7Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7U\">[</span>ad<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7Y\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1685\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Psychological_evidence_of_the_prevalence_of_sub_17-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Psychological evidence of the prevalence of sub\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Psychological_evidence_of_the_prevalence_of_sub-17\" id=\"mwC7c\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC7g\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7k\">[</span>15<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC7o\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC7s\">The issue is not resolved: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sub-symbolic\" title=\"Sub-symbolic\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC7w\">sub-symbolic</a> reasoning can make many of the same inscrutable mistakes that human intuition does, such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Algorithmic_bias\" title=\"Algorithmic bias\" id=\"mwC70\">algorithmic bias</a>. Critics such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Noam_Chomsky\" title=\"Noam Chomsky\" id=\"mwC74\">Noam Chomsky</a> argue continuing research into symbolic AI will still be necessary to attain general intelligence,<sup about=\"#mwt1686\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTELangley2011_460-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTELangley2011\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTELangley2011-460\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Langley\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2011\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTELangley2011-460\" id=\"mwC78\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC8A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC8E\">[</span>430<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC8I\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1689\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKatz2012_461-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEKatz2012\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKatz2012-461\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Katz\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2012\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKatz2012-461\" id=\"mwC8M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC8Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC8U\">[</span>431<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC8Y\">]</span></span></a></sup> in part because sub-symbolic AI is a move away from <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Explainable_AI\" title=\"Explainable AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC8c\">explainable AI</a>: it can be difficult or impossible to understand why a modern statistical AI program made a particular decision. The emerging field of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neuro-symbolic_AI\" title=\"Neuro-symbolic AI\" id=\"mwC8g\">neuro-symbolic artificial intelligence</a> attempts to bridge the two approaches.</p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"57\" id=\"mwC8k\" aria-labelledby=\"Neat_vs._scruffy\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Neat_vs._scruffy\">Neat vs. scruffy</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1692\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC8o\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Neats and scruffies\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1693\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1692\" id=\"mwC8s\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Neats_and_scruffies\" title=\"Neats and scruffies\">Neats and scruffies</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC8w\">\"Neats\" hope that intelligent behaviour is described using simple, elegant principles (such as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic\" title=\"Logic\" id=\"mwC80\">logic</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Optimization\" title=\"Optimization\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC84\">optimisation</a>). \"Scruffies\" expect that it necessarily requires solving a large number of unrelated problems. Neats defend their programs with theoretical rigour, scruffies rely mainly on incremental testing to see if they work. This issue was actively discussed in the 1970s and 1980s.<sup about=\"#mwt1703\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-462\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-462\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-462\" id=\"mwC88\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC9A\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9E\">[</span>432<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9I\">]</span></span></a></sup> The rise of deep learning may represent a shift toward the scruffies.<sup about=\"#mwt1694\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202142_463-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202142\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202142-463\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"42\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202142-463\" id=\"mwC9M\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC9Q\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9U\">[</span>433<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC9Y\">]</span></span></a></sup></p> \\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"58\" id=\"mwC9c\" aria-labelledby=\"Soft_vs._hard_computing\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Soft_vs._hard_computing\">Soft vs. hard computing</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1704\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC9g\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Soft computing\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1705\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1704\" id=\"mwC9k\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Soft_computing\" title=\"Soft computing\">Soft computing</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC9o\">Finding a provably correct or optimal solution is <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intractability_(complexity)\" title=\"Intractability (complexity)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC9s\">intractable</a> for many important problems.<sup about=\"#mwt1706\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Intractability_and_efficiency_and_the_combinatorial_explosion_16-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Intractability and efficiency and the combinatorial explosion\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Intractability_and_efficiency_and_the_combinatorial_explosion-16\" id=\"mwC9w\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC90\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC94\">[</span>14<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC98\">]</span></span></a></sup> Soft computing is a set of techniques, including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Genetic_algorithms\" title=\"Genetic algorithms\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC-A\">genetic algorithms</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fuzzy_logic\" title=\"Fuzzy logic\" id=\"mwC-E\">fuzzy logic</a> and neural networks, that are tolerant of imprecision, uncertainty, partial truth and approximation. Soft computing was introduced in the late 1980s and most successful AI programs in the 21st century are examples of soft computing with neural networks.</p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"59\" id=\"mwC-I\" aria-labelledby=\"Narrow_vs._general_AI\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Narrow_vs._general_AI\">Narrow vs. general AI</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1707\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC-M\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Weak artificial intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial general intelligence\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1708\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1707\" id=\"mwC-Q\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Weak_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Weak artificial intelligence\">Weak artificial intelligence</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_general_intelligence\" title=\"Artificial general intelligence\">Artificial general intelligence</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC-U\">AI researchers are divided as to whether to pursue the goals of artificial general intelligence and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superintelligence\" title=\"Superintelligence\" id=\"mwC-Y\">superintelligence</a> directly or to solve as many specific problems as possible (narrow AI) in hopes these solutions will lead indirectly to the field\\'s long-term goals.<sup about=\"#mwt1709\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEPennachinGoertzel2007_464-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEPennachinGoertzel2007\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEPennachinGoertzel2007-464\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Pennachin\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Goertzel\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2007\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEPennachinGoertzel2007-464\" id=\"mwC-c\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC-g\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC-k\">[</span>434<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC-o\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1712\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERoberts2016_465-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERoberts2016\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERoberts2016-465\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Roberts\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2016\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERoberts2016-465\" id=\"mwC-s\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC-w\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC-0\">[</span>435<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC-4\">]</span></span></a></sup> General intelligence is difficult to define and difficult to measure, and modern AI has had more verifiable successes by focusing on specific problems with specific solutions. The sub-field of artificial general intelligence studies this area exclusively.</p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"60\" id=\"mwC-8\" aria-labelledby=\"Machine_consciousness,_sentience,_and_mind\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Machine_consciousness,_sentience,_and_mind\"><span id=\"Machine_consciousness.2C_sentience.2C_and_mind\" typeof=\"mw:FallbackId\"></span>Machine consciousness, sentience, and mind</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1715\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC_A\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Philosophy of artificial intelligence\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial consciousness\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1716\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1715\" id=\"mwC_E\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophy_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Philosophy of artificial intelligence\">Philosophy of artificial intelligence</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_consciousness\" title=\"Artificial consciousness\">Artificial consciousness</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwC_I\">There is no settled consensus in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophy_of_mind\" title=\"Philosophy of mind\" id=\"mwC_M\">philosophy of mind</a> on whether a machine can have a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mind\" title=\"Mind\" id=\"mwC_Q\">mind</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Consciousness\" title=\"Consciousness\" id=\"mwC_U\">consciousness</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subjective_character_of_experience\" title=\"Subjective character of experience\" id=\"mwC_Y\">subjective experiences</a> in the same sense that human beings do. This issue considers the internal experiences of the machine, rather than its external behaviour. Mainstream AI research considers this issue irrelevant because it does not affect the goals of the field: to build machines that can solve problems using intelligence. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwC_c\">Russell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norvig\" title=\"Norvig\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwC_g\">Norvig</a> add that \"[t]he additional project of making a machine conscious in exactly the way humans are is not one that we are equipped to take on.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1717\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021986_466-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021986\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021986-466\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"986\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021986-466\" id=\"mwC_k\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwC_o\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_s\">[</span>436<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwC_w\">]</span></span></a></sup> However, the question has become central to the philosophy of mind. It is also typically the central question at issue in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_in_fiction\" title=\"Artificial intelligence in fiction\" id=\"mwC_0\">artificial intelligence in fiction</a>.</p>\\n\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"61\" id=\"mwC_4\" aria-labelledby=\"Consciousness\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Consciousness\">Consciousness</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1720\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwC_8\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Hard problem of consciousness\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Theory of mind\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1721\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1720\" id=\"mwDAA\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hard_problem_of_consciousness\" title=\"Hard problem of consciousness\">Hard problem of consciousness</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Theory_of_mind\" title=\"Theory of mind\">Theory of mind</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDAE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/David_Chalmers\" title=\"David Chalmers\" id=\"mwDAI\">David Chalmers</a> identified two problems in understanding the mind, which he named the \"hard\" and \"easy\" problems of consciousness.<sup about=\"#mwt1722\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChalmers1995_467-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChalmers1995\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChalmers1995-467\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Chalmers\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1995\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChalmers1995-467\" id=\"mwDAM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDAQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDAU\">[</span>437<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDAY\">]</span></span></a></sup> The easy problem is understanding how the brain processes signals, makes plans and controls behaviour. The hard problem is explaining how this <i id=\"mwDAc\">feels</i> or why it should feel like anything at all, assuming we are right in thinking that it truly does feel like something (Dennett\\'s consciousness illusionism says this is an illusion). While human <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Information_processing_(psychology)\" title=\"Information processing (psychology)\" id=\"mwDAg\">information processing</a> is easy to explain, human <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Subjective_experience\" title=\"Subjective experience\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDAk\">subjective experience</a> is difficult to explain. For example, it is easy to imagine a colour-blind person who has learned to identify which objects in their field of view are red, but it is not clear what would be required for the person to <i id=\"mwDAo\">know what red looks like</i>.<sup about=\"#mwt1725\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDennett1991_468-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEDennett1991\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDennett1991-468\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Dennett\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1991\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDennett1991-468\" id=\"mwDAs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDAw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDA0\">[</span>438<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDA4\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"62\" id=\"mwDA8\" aria-labelledby=\"Computationalism_and_functionalism\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"Computationalism_and_functionalism\">Computationalism and functionalism</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1728\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDBA\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Computational theory of mind\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Functionalism (philosophy of mind)\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1729\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1728\" id=\"mwDBE\">Main articles: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_theory_of_mind\" title=\"Computational theory of mind\">Computational theory of mind</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Functionalism_(philosophy_of_mind)\" title=\"Functionalism (philosophy of mind)\">Functionalism (philosophy of mind)</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDBI\">Computationalism is the position in the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophy_of_mind\" title=\"Philosophy of mind\" id=\"mwDBM\">philosophy of mind</a> that the human mind is an information processing system and that thinking is a form of computing. Computationalism argues that the relationship between mind and body is similar or identical to the relationship between software and hardware and thus may be a solution to the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mind–body_problem\" title=\"Mind–body problem\" id=\"mwDBQ\">mind–body problem</a>. This philosophical position was inspired by the work of AI researchers and cognitive scientists in the 1960s and was originally proposed by philosophers <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jerry_Fodor\" title=\"Jerry Fodor\" id=\"mwDBU\">Jerry Fodor</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hilary_Putnam\" title=\"Hilary Putnam\" id=\"mwDBY\">Hilary Putnam</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1730\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEHorst2005_469-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEHorst2005\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEHorst2005-469\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Horst\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2005\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEHorst2005-469\" id=\"mwDBc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDBg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDBk\">[</span>439<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDBo\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDBs\">Philosopher <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Searle\" title=\"John Searle\" id=\"mwDBw\">John Searle</a> characterised this position as \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Strong_AI_hypothesis\" title=\"Strong AI hypothesis\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDB0\">strong AI</a>\": \"The appropriately programmed computer with the right inputs and outputs would thereby have a mind in exactly the same sense human beings have minds.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1733\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Searle\\'s_strong_AI_473-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Searle&apos;s strong AI\",\"group\":\"lower-alpha\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Searle&apos;s_strong_AI-473\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Efn\",\"href\":\"./Template:Efn\"},\"params\":{\"name\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"Searle&apos;s strong AI\\\\\"\"},\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Searle presented this definition of \\\\\"Strong AI\\\\\" in 1999.{{Sfnp|Searle|1999}} Searle&apos;s original formulation was \\\\\"The appropriately programmed computer really is a mind, in the sense that computers given the right programs can be literally said to understand and have other cognitive states.\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Searle|1980|p=1}} Strong AI is defined similarly by [[Stuart J. Russell|Russell]] and [[Norvig]]: \\\\\"Strong AI – the assertion that machines that do so are &apos;&apos;actually&apos;&apos; consciously thinking (as opposed to &apos;&apos;simulating&apos;&apos; thinking).\\\\\"{{Sfnp|Russell|Norvig|2021|p=1032}}\\\\n\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Searle\\'s_strong_AI-473\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDB4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDB8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCA\">[</span>ae<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCE\">]</span></span></a></sup> Searle challenges this claim with his <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Chinese_room\" title=\"Chinese room\" id=\"mwDCI\">Chinese room</a> argument, which attempts to show that even a computer capable of perfectly simulating human behaviour would not have a mind.<sup about=\"#mwt1750\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-474\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-474\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-474\" id=\"mwDCM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDCQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCU\">[</span>443<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDCY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"63\" id=\"mwDCc\" aria-labelledby=\"AI_welfare_and_rights\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading4\"><h4 id=\"AI_welfare_and_rights\">AI welfare and rights</h4></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1751\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDCg\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"See also\",\"href\":\"./Template:See_also\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Ethics of artificial intelligence#AI welfare\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1752\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1751\" id=\"mwDCk\">See also: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ethics_of_artificial_intelligence#AI_welfare\" title=\"Ethics of artificial intelligence\">Ethics of artificial intelligence §<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>AI welfare</a></div>\\n<p id=\"mwDCo\">It is difficult or impossible to reliably evaluate whether an advanced <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentient_AI\" title=\"Sentient AI\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDCs\">AI is sentient</a> (has the ability to feel), and if so, to what degree.<sup about=\"#mwt1755\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-475\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-475\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-475\" id=\"mwDCw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDC0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDC4\">[</span>444<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDC8\">]</span></span></a></sup> But if there is a significant chance that a given machine can feel and suffer, then it may be entitled to certain rights or welfare protection measures, similarly to animals.<sup about=\"#mwt1758\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Thomson-2022_476-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Thomson-2022\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Thomson-2022-476\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Thomson-2022-476\" id=\"mwDDA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDDE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDI\">[</span>445<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDM\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1761\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Kateman-2023_477-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Kateman-2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Kateman-2023-477\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Kateman-2023-477\" id=\"mwDDQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDDU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDY\">[</span>446<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDc\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sapience\" title=\"Sapience\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDDg\">Sapience</a> (a set of capacities related to high intelligence, such as discernment or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Self-awareness\" title=\"Self-awareness\" id=\"mwDDk\">self-awareness</a>) may provide another moral basis for AI rights.<sup about=\"#mwt1762\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Thomson-2022_476-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Thomson-2022\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Thomson-2022-476\" id=\"mwDDo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDDs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDDw\">[</span>445<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDD0\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robot_rights\" title=\"Robot rights\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDD4\">Robot rights</a> are also sometimes proposed as a practical way to integrate autonomous agents into society.<sup about=\"#mwt1765\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-478\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-478\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-478\" id=\"mwDD8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDEA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEE\">[</span>447<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEI\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDEM\">In 2017, the European Union considered granting \"electronic personhood\" to some of the most capable AI systems. Similarly to the legal status of companies, it would have conferred rights but also responsibilities.<sup about=\"#mwt1768\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-479\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-479\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-479\" id=\"mwDEQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDEU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEY\">[</span>448<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEc\">]</span></span></a></sup> Critics argued in 2018 that granting rights to AI systems would downplay the importance of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Human_rights\" title=\"Human rights\" id=\"mwDEg\">human rights</a>, and that legislation should focus on user needs rather than speculative futuristic scenarios. They also noted that robots lacked the autonomy to take part in society on their own.<sup about=\"#mwt1771\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-480\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-480\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-480\" id=\"mwDEk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDEo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEs\">[</span>449<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDEw\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1774\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-481\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-481\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-481\" id=\"mwDE0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDE4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDE8\">[</span>450<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFA\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDFE\">Progress in AI increased interest in the topic. Proponents of AI welfare and rights often argue that AI sentience, if it emerges, would be particularly easy to deny. They warn that this may be a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Moral_blindness\" title=\"Moral blindness\" id=\"mwDFI\">moral blind spot</a> analogous to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Slavery\" title=\"Slavery\" id=\"mwDFM\">slavery</a> or <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Factory_farming\" title=\"Factory farming\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDFQ\">factory farming</a>, which could lead to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Suffering_risks\" title=\"Suffering risks\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDFU\">large-scale suffering</a> if sentient AI is created and carelessly exploited.<sup about=\"#mwt1775\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Kateman-2023_477-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Kateman-2023\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Kateman-2023-477\" id=\"mwDFY\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDFc\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFg\">[</span>446<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFk\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1776\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Thomson-2022_476-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Thomson-2022\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Thomson-2022-476\" id=\"mwDFo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDFs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDFw\">[</span>445<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDF0\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section></section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"64\" id=\"mwDF4\" aria-labelledby=\"Future\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Future\">Future</h2></div>\\n<section data-mw-section-id=\"65\" id=\"mwDF8\" aria-labelledby=\"Superintelligence_and_the_singularity\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Superintelligence_and_the_singularity\">Superintelligence and the singularity</h3></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDGA\">A <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Superintelligence\" title=\"Superintelligence\" id=\"mwDGE\">superintelligence</a> is a hypothetical agent that would possess intelligence far surpassing that of the brightest and most gifted human mind.<sup about=\"#mwt1777\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERoberts2016_465-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERoberts2016\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERoberts2016-465\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Roberts\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2016\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERoberts2016-465\" id=\"mwDGI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDGM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDGQ\">[</span>435<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDGU\">]</span></span></a></sup> If research into <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_general_intelligence\" title=\"Artificial general intelligence\" id=\"mwDGY\">artificial general intelligence</a> produced sufficiently intelligent software, it might be able to <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Recursive_self-improvement\" title=\"Recursive self-improvement\" id=\"mwDGc\">reprogram and improve itself</a>. The improved software would be even better at improving itself, leading to what <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/I._J._Good\" title=\"I. J. Good\" id=\"mwDGg\">I. J. Good</a> called an \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligence_explosion\" title=\"Intelligence explosion\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDGk\">intelligence explosion</a>\" and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Vernor_Vinge\" title=\"Vernor Vinge\" id=\"mwDGo\">Vernor Vinge</a> called a \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Technological_singularity\" title=\"Technological singularity\" id=\"mwDGs\">singularity</a>\".<sup about=\"#mwt1785\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-482\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-482\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-482\" id=\"mwDGw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDG0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDG4\">[</span>451<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDG8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDHA\">In <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_Intelligence:_A_Modern_Approach\" title=\"Artificial Intelligence: A Modern Approach\" id=\"mwDHE\">Artificial Intelligence: A Modern Approach</a>, Russel and Norvig cast doubt on the possibility of a singularity, arguing that \"so far, every technology has followed an <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/S-shaped_curve\" title=\"S-shaped curve\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDHI\">S-shaped curve</a>\", and that \"sometimes it is not possible to keep the growth going.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1786\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211005_483-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211005\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211005-483\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"p\":{\"wt\":\"1005\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211005-483\" id=\"mwDHM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDHQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDHU\">[</span>452<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDHY\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"66\" id=\"mwDHc\" aria-labelledby=\"Transhumanism\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading3\"><h3 id=\"Transhumanism\">Transhumanism</h3></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1789\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDHg\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Transhumanism\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1790\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1789\" id=\"mwDHk\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Transhumanism\" title=\"Transhumanism\">Transhumanism</a></div>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDHo\">Robot designer <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Moravec\" title=\"Hans Moravec\" id=\"mwDHs\">Hans Moravec</a>, cyberneticist <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kevin_Warwick\" title=\"Kevin Warwick\" id=\"mwDHw\">Kevin Warwick</a> and inventor <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ray_Kurzweil\" title=\"Ray Kurzweil\" id=\"mwDH0\">Ray Kurzweil</a> have predicted that humans and machines may merge in the future into <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cyborg\" title=\"Cyborg\" id=\"mwDH4\">cyborgs</a> that are more capable and powerful than either. This idea, called transhumanism, has roots in the writings of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aldous_Huxley\" title=\"Aldous Huxley\" id=\"mwDH8\">Aldous Huxley</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robert_Ettinger\" title=\"Robert Ettinger\" id=\"mwDIA\">Robert Ettinger</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1794\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-484\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-484\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-484\" id=\"mwDIE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDII\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDIM\">[</span>453<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDIQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDIU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Edward_Fredkin\" title=\"Edward Fredkin\" id=\"mwDIY\">Edward Fredkin</a> argues that \"artificial intelligence is the next step in evolution\", an idea first proposed by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Samuel_Butler_(novelist)\" title=\"Samuel Butler (novelist)\" id=\"mwDIc\">Samuel Butler</a>\\'s \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darwin_among_the_Machines\" title=\"Darwin among the Machines\" id=\"mwDIg\">Darwin among the Machines</a>\" as far back as 1863, and expanded upon by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/George_Dyson_(science_historian)\" title=\"George Dyson (science historian)\" id=\"mwDIk\">George Dyson</a> in his 1998 book <i id=\"mwDIo\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Darwin_Among_the_Machines#Evolution_of_Global_Intelligence\" title=\"Darwin Among the Machines\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDIs\">Darwin Among the Machines: The Evolution of Global Intelligence</a></i>.<sup about=\"#mwt1798\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-485\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-485\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-485\" id=\"mwDIw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDI0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDI4\">[</span>454<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDI8\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section></section><section data-mw-section-id=\"67\" id=\"mwDJA\" aria-labelledby=\"In_fiction\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"In_fiction\">In fiction</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1799\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDJE\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Main\",\"href\":\"./Template:Main\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial intelligence in fiction\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1368532237\" about=\"#mwt1800\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Hatnote/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'/></span><div role=\"note\" class=\"hatnote navigation-not-searchable\" about=\"#mwt1799\" id=\"mwDJI\">Main article: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_in_fiction\" title=\"Artificial intelligence in fiction\">Artificial intelligence in fiction</a></div>\\n\\n<figure class=\"mw-default-size\" typeof=\"mw:File/Thumb\" id=\"mwDJM\"><a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Capek_play.jpg\" class=\"mw-file-description\" id=\"mwDJQ\"><img resource=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File:Capek_play.jpg\" src=\"//thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/8/87/Capek_play.jpg/330px-Capek_play.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail\" decoding=\"async\" loading=\"lazy\" srcset=\"//upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/8/87/Capek_play.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&amp;utm_campaign=parser&amp;utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled 2x\" data-file-width=\"566\" data-file-height=\"316\" data-file-type=\"bitmap\" height=\"167\" width=\"300\" class=\"mw-file-element mw-file-upright\" style=\"--mw-file-upright: 1.2\" id=\"mwDJU\"/></a><figcaption id=\"mwDJY\">The word \"robot\" itself was coined by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karel_Čapek\" title=\"Karel Čapek\" id=\"mwDJc\">Karel Čapek</a> in his 1921 play <i id=\"mwDJg\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R.U.R.\" title=\"R.U.R.\" id=\"mwDJk\">R.U.R.</a></i>, the title standing for \"Rossum\\'s Universal Robots\".</figcaption></figure>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDJo\">Thought-capable artificial beings have appeared as storytelling devices since antiquity,<sup about=\"#mwt1805\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-AI_in_myth_486-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"AI in myth\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-AI_in_myth-486\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-AI_in_myth-486\" id=\"mwDJs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDJw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDJ0\">[</span>455<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDJ4\">]</span></span></a></sup> and have been a persistent theme in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Science_fiction\" title=\"Science fiction\" id=\"mwDJ8\">science fiction</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1801\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004340–400_487-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004340–400\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004340–400-487\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"McCorduck\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2004\"},\"pp\":{\"wt\":\"340–400\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004340–400-487\" id=\"mwDKA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDKE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDKI\">[</span>456<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDKM\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDKQ\">A common <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trope_(literature)\" title=\"Trope (literature)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDKU\">trope</a> in these works began with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mary_Shelley\" title=\"Mary Shelley\" id=\"mwDKY\">Mary Shelley</a>\\'s <i id=\"mwDKc\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frankenstein\" title=\"Frankenstein\" id=\"mwDKg\">Frankenstein</a></i>, where a human creation becomes a threat to its masters. This includes such works as <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2001:_A_Space_Odyssey_(novel)\" title=\"2001: A Space Odyssey (novel)\" id=\"mwDKk\">Arthur C. Clarke\\'s</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/2001:_A_Space_Odyssey\" title=\"2001: A Space Odyssey\" id=\"mwDKo\">Stanley Kubrick\\'s</a> <i id=\"mwDKs\">2001: A Space Odyssey</i> (both 1968), with <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/HAL_9000\" title=\"HAL 9000\" id=\"mwDKw\">HAL 9000</a>, the murderous computer in charge of the <i id=\"mwDK0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Discovery_One\" title=\"Discovery One\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDK4\">Discovery One</a></i> spaceship, as well as <i id=\"mwDK8\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Blade_Runner\" title=\"Blade Runner\" id=\"mwDLA\">Blade Runner</a></i> (1982), <i id=\"mwDLE\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Terminator\" title=\"The Terminator\" id=\"mwDLI\">The Terminator</a></i> (1984) and <i id=\"mwDLM\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Matrix\" title=\"The Matrix\" id=\"mwDLQ\">The Matrix</a></i> (1999). In contrast, the rare loyal robots such as Gort from <i id=\"mwDLU\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Day_the_Earth_Stood_Still\" title=\"The Day the Earth Stood Still\" id=\"mwDLY\">The Day the Earth Stood Still</a></i> (1951) and Bishop from <i id=\"mwDLc\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Aliens_(film)\" title=\"Aliens (film)\" id=\"mwDLg\">Aliens</a></i> (1986) are less prominent in popular culture.<sup about=\"#mwt1806\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEButtazzo2001_488-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEButtazzo2001\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEButtazzo2001-488\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Buttazzo\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2001\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEButtazzo2001-488\" id=\"mwDLk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDLo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDLs\">[</span>457<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDLw\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDL0\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Isaac_Asimov\" title=\"Isaac Asimov\" id=\"mwDL4\">Isaac Asimov</a> introduced the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Three_Laws_of_Robotics\" title=\"Three Laws of Robotics\" id=\"mwDL8\">Three Laws of Robotics</a> in many stories, most notably with the \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Multivac\" title=\"Multivac\" id=\"mwDMA\">Multivac</a>\" super-intelligent computer. Asimov\\'s laws are often brought up during lay discussions of machine ethics;<sup about=\"#mwt1809\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEAnderson2008_489-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEAnderson2008\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEAnderson2008-489\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Anderson\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2008\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEAnderson2008-489\" id=\"mwDME\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDMI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMM\">[</span>458<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMQ\">]</span></span></a></sup> while almost all artificial intelligence researchers are familiar with Asimov\\'s laws through popular culture, they generally consider the laws useless for many reasons, one of which is their ambiguity.<sup about=\"#mwt1812\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcCauley2007_490-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMcCauley2007\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCauley2007-490\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"McCauley\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"2007\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCauley2007-490\" id=\"mwDMU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDMY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMc\">[</span>459<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDMg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n<p id=\"mwDMk\">Several works use AI to force us to confront the fundamental question of what makes us human, showing us artificial beings that have <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sentience\" title=\"Sentience\" id=\"mwDMo\">the ability to feel</a>, and thus to suffer. This appears in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karel_Čapek\" title=\"Karel Čapek\" id=\"mwDMs\">Karel Čapek</a>\\'s <i id=\"mwDMw\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/R.U.R.\" title=\"R.U.R.\" id=\"mwDM0\">R.U.R.</a></i>, the films <i id=\"mwDM4\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/A.I._Artificial_Intelligence\" title=\"A.I. Artificial Intelligence\" id=\"mwDM8\">A.I. Artificial Intelligence</a></i> and <i id=\"mwDNA\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ex_Machina_(film)\" title=\"Ex Machina (film)\" id=\"mwDNE\">Ex Machina</a></i>, as well as the novel <i id=\"mwDNI\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Do_Androids_Dream_of_Electric_Sheep%3F\" title=\"Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?\" id=\"mwDNM\">Do Androids Dream of Electric Sheep?</a></i>, by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philip_K._Dick\" title=\"Philip K. Dick\" id=\"mwDNQ\">Philip K. Dick</a>. Dick considers the idea that our understanding of human subjectivity is altered by technology created with artificial intelligence.<sup about=\"#mwt1815\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEGalvan1997_491-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEGalvan1997\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEGalvan1997-491\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Sfnp\",\"href\":\"./Template:Sfnp\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Galvan\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"1997\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEGalvan1997-491\" id=\"mwDNU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDNY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDNc\">[</span>460<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDNg\">]</span></span></a></sup></p>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"68\" id=\"mwDNk\" aria-labelledby=\"See_also\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"See_also\">See also</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1818\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDNo\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"div col\",\"href\":\"./Template:Div_col\"},\"params\":{\"colwidth\":{\"wt\":\"30em\"}},\"i\":0}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial consciousness\"}},\"i\":1}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial intelligence and elections\"}},\"i\":2}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Artificial intelligence content detection\"}},\"i\":3}},\"\\\\n* [[Artificial intelligence in Wikimedia projects]] – Use of artificial intelligence to develop Wikipedia and other Wikimedia projects\\\\n* [[Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence]] (AAAI)\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Behavior selection algorithm\"}},\"i\":4}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Business process automation\"}},\"i\":5}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Case-based reasoning\"}},\"i\":6}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Computational intelligence\"}},\"i\":7}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Digital immortality\"}},\"i\":8}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Emergent algorithm\"}},\"i\":9}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Female gendering of AI technologies\"}},\"i\":10}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Glossary of artificial intelligence\"}},\"i\":11}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Intelligence amplification\"}},\"i\":12}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Intelligent agent\"}},\"i\":13}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Intelligent automation\"}},\"i\":14}},\"\\\\n* [[List of computer books#Artificial intelligence|List of artificial intelligence books]]\\\\n* [[List of artificial intelligence algorithms]]\\\\n* [[List of artificial intelligence companies]]\\\\n* [[List of artificial intelligence institutions]]\\\\n* [[List of artificial intelligence journals]]\\\\n* [[List of artificial intelligence projects]]\\\\n* [[List of university artificial intelligence research centers]]\\\\n* [[Lists of open-source artificial intelligence software]]\\\\n* [[List of proprietary artificial intelligence software]]\\\\n* [[List of robotics software]]\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Mind uploading\"}},\"i\":15}},\"\\\\n* [[Organoid intelligence]] – Use of brain cells and brain organoids for intelligent computing\\\\n* [[Outline of deep learning]]\\\\n* [[Outline of machine learning]]\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Pseudorandomness\"}},\"i\":16}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Robotic process automation\"}},\"i\":17}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"The Last Day (novel)\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"&apos;&apos;The Last Day&apos;&apos;\"}},\"i\":18}},\"\\\\n* \",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Annotated link\",\"href\":\"./Template:Annotated_link\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Wetware computer\"}},\"i\":19}},\"\\\\n\",{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"div col end\",\"href\":\"./Template:Div_col_end\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":20}}]}\\'><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1184024115\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" about=\"#mwt1819\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Div col/styles.css\"}}\\'>.mw-parser-output .div-col{margin-top:0.3em;column-width:30em}.mw-parser-output .div-col-small{font-size:90%}.mw-parser-output .div-col-rules{column-rule:1px solid #aaa}.mw-parser-output .div-col dl,.mw-parser-output .div-col ol,.mw-parser-output .div-col ul{margin-top:0}.mw-parser-output .div-col li,.mw-parser-output .div-col dd{page-break-inside:avoid;break-inside:avoid-column}</style></span><div class=\"div-col   \" style=\"column-width: 30em;\" about=\"#mwt1818\" id=\"mwDNs\">\\n<ul><li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_consciousness\" title=\"Artificial consciousness\">Artificial consciousness</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Hypothetical consciousness in artificial systems</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_and_elections\" title=\"Artificial intelligence and elections\">Artificial intelligence and elections</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_content_detection\" title=\"Artificial intelligence content detection\">Artificial intelligence content detection</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Software to detect AI-generated content</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Artificial_intelligence_in_Wikimedia_projects\" title=\"Artificial intelligence in Wikimedia projects\">Artificial intelligence in Wikimedia projects</a> – Use of artificial intelligence to develop Wikipedia and other Wikimedia projects</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Association_for_the_Advancement_of_Artificial_Intelligence\" title=\"Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence\">Association for the Advancement of Artificial Intelligence</a> (AAAI)</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Behavior_selection_algorithm\" title=\"Behavior selection algorithm\">Behavior selection algorithm</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Algorithm that selects actions for intelligent agents</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Business_process_automation\" title=\"Business process automation\">Business process automation</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Automation of business processes</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Case-based_reasoning\" title=\"Case-based reasoning\">Case-based reasoning</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Process of solving new problems based on the solutions of similar past problems</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computational_intelligence\" title=\"Computational intelligence\">Computational intelligence</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Computer system simulating intelligence</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Digital_immortality\" title=\"Digital immortality\">Digital immortality</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Hypothetical concept of storing a personality in digital form</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Emergent_algorithm\" title=\"Emergent algorithm\">Emergent algorithm</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Algorithm exhibiting emergent behavior</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Female_gendering_of_AI_technologies\" title=\"Female gendering of AI technologies\" class=\"mw-redirect\">Female gendering of AI technologies</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Gender biases in digital technology<span style=\"display:none\" class=\"category-annotation-with-redirected-description\">Pages displaying short descriptions of redirect targets</span><link rel=\"mw:PageProp/Category\" href=\"./Category:Pages_displaying_short_descriptions_of_redirect_targets_via_Module:Annotated_link\"/></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Glossary_of_artificial_intelligence\" title=\"Glossary of artificial intelligence\">Glossary of artificial intelligence</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– List of concepts in artificial intelligence</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligence_amplification\" title=\"Intelligence amplification\">Intelligence amplification</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Use of information technology to augment human intelligence</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligent_agent\" title=\"Intelligent agent\">Intelligent agent</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Software agent which acts autonomously</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Intelligent_automation\" title=\"Intelligent automation\">Intelligent automation</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Software process that combines robotic process automation and artificial intelligence</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_computer_books#Artificial_intelligence\" title=\"List of computer books\">List of artificial intelligence books</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_artificial_intelligence_algorithms\" title=\"List of artificial intelligence algorithms\">List of artificial intelligence algorithms</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_artificial_intelligence_companies\" title=\"List of artificial intelligence companies\">List of artificial intelligence companies</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_artificial_intelligence_institutions\" title=\"List of artificial intelligence institutions\">List of artificial intelligence institutions</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_artificial_intelligence_journals\" title=\"List of artificial intelligence journals\">List of artificial intelligence journals</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_artificial_intelligence_projects\" title=\"List of artificial intelligence projects\">List of artificial intelligence projects</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_university_artificial_intelligence_research_centers\" title=\"List of university artificial intelligence research centers\">List of university artificial intelligence research centers</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Lists_of_open-source_artificial_intelligence_software\" title=\"Lists of open-source artificial intelligence software\">Lists of open-source artificial intelligence software</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_proprietary_artificial_intelligence_software\" title=\"List of proprietary artificial intelligence software\">List of proprietary artificial intelligence software</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_robotics_software\" title=\"List of robotics software\">List of robotics software</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mind_uploading\" title=\"Mind uploading\">Mind uploading</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Hypothetical process of digitally emulating a brain</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Organoid_intelligence\" title=\"Organoid intelligence\">Organoid intelligence</a> – Use of brain cells and brain organoids for intelligent computing</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_deep_learning\" title=\"Outline of deep learning\">Outline of deep learning</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Outline_of_machine_learning\" title=\"Outline of machine learning\">Outline of machine learning</a></li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Pseudorandomness\" title=\"Pseudorandomness\">Pseudorandomness</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Appearing random but actually being generated by a deterministic, causal process</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robotic_process_automation\" title=\"Robotic process automation\">Robotic process automation</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Form of business process automation technology</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Last_Day_(novel)\" title=\"The Last Day (novel)\"><i>The Last Day</i></a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– 1967 Welsh science fiction novel</li>\\n<li><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wetware_computer\" title=\"Wetware computer\">Wetware computer</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\">\\xa0</span>– Computer composed of organic material</li></ul>\\n</div>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"69\" id=\"mwDNw\" aria-labelledby=\"Explanatory_notes\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"Explanatory_notes\">Explanatory notes</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1840\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDN0\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Notelist\",\"href\":\"./Template:Notelist\"},\"params\":{},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1327269900\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" about=\"#mwt1841\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Reflist/styles.css\"}}\\'>.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:30em}.mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:25em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-2{column-width:27em}body.skin-vector-2022 .mw-parser-output .reflist-columns-3{column-width:22.5em}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-alpha]{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=upper-roman]{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-alpha]{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-greek]{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output .references[data-mw-group=lower-roman]{list-style-type:lower-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-alpha .references{list-style-type:upper-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-upper-roman .references{list-style-type:upper-roman}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-alpha .references{list-style-type:lower-alpha}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-greek .references{list-style-type:lower-greek}.mw-parser-output div.reflist-liststyle-lower-roman .references{list-style-type:lower-roman}</style></span><div about=\"#mwt1840\" id=\"mwDN4\">\\n<div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/references\" about=\"#mwt1842\" id=\"mwDN8\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"references\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"lower-alpha\",\"responsive\":\"1\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'><ol class=\"mw-references references\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDOA\"><li about=\"#cite_note-Problems_of_AI-2\" id=\"cite_note-Problems_of_AI-2\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"a\"><span rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDOE\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Problems_of_AI_2-0\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDOI\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDOM\">1</span></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Problems_of_AI_2-1\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDOQ\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDOU\">2</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Problems_of_AI-2\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">This list of intelligent traits is based on the topics covered by the major AI textbooks, including: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFRussellNorvig2021\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDOY\">Russell <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDOc\">&amp;</span> Norvig (2021)</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFLugerStubblefield2004\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDOg\">Luger <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDOk\">&amp;</span> Stubblefield (2004)</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFPooleMackworthGoebel1998\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDOo\">Poole, Mackworth <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDOs\">&amp;</span> Goebel (1998)</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFNilsson1998\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDOw\">Nilsson (1998)</a>.</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-Tools_of_AI-3\" id=\"cite_note-Tools_of_AI-3\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"b\"><span rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDO0\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Tools_of_AI_3-0\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDO4\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDO8\">1</span></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-Tools_of_AI_3-1\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" id=\"mwDPA\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDPE\">2</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Tools_of_AI-3\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">This list of tools is based on the topics covered by the major AI textbooks, including: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFRussellNorvig2021\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDPI\">Russell <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDPM\">&amp;</span> Norvig (2021)</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFLugerStubblefield2004\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDPQ\">Luger <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDPU\">&amp;</span> Stubblefield (2004)</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFPooleMackworthGoebel1998\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDPY\">Poole, Mackworth <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDPc\">&amp;</span> Goebel (1998)</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFNilsson1998\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDPg\">Nilsson (1998)</a>.</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-26\" id=\"cite_note-26\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"c\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDPk\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-26\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDPo\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDPs\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-26\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Formal knowledge representations are used in content-based indexing and retrieval,<sup about=\"#mwt64\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESmoliarZhang1994_21-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESmoliarZhang1994\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESmoliarZhang1994-21\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESmoliarZhang1994-21\" id=\"mwDPw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDP0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDP4\">[</span>19<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDP8\">]</span></span></a></sup> scene interpretation,<sup about=\"#mwt66\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTENeumannMöller2008_22-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTENeumannMöller2008\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENeumannMöller2008-22\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTENeumannMöller2008-22\" id=\"mwDQA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDQE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQI\">[</span>20<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQM\">]</span></span></a></sup> clinical decision support,<sup about=\"#mwt68\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEKupermanReichleyBailey2006_23-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEKupermanReichleyBailey2006\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEKupermanReichleyBailey2006-23\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEKupermanReichleyBailey2006-23\" id=\"mwDQQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDQU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQY\">[</span>21<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQc\">]</span></span></a></sup> knowledge discovery (mining \"interesting\" and actionable inferences from large <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Database\" title=\"Database\" id=\"mwDQg\">databases</a>),<sup about=\"#mwt70\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcGarry2005_24-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMcGarry2005\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcGarry2005-24\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcGarry2005-24\" id=\"mwDQk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDQo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQs\">[</span>22<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQw\">]</span></span></a></sup> and other areas.<sup about=\"#mwt72\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBertiniDel_BimboTorniai2006_25-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEBertiniDel BimboTorniai2006\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBertiniDel_BimboTorniai2006-25\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBertiniDel_BimboTorniai2006-25\" id=\"mwDQ0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDQ4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDQ8\">[</span>23<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRA\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-33\" id=\"cite_note-33\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"d\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDRE\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-33\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDRI\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDRM\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-33\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">A complete formal knowledge base needs to represent things such as objects, properties, categories, and relations between objects;<sup about=\"#mwt89\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-28\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-28\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-28\" id=\"mwDRQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDRU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRY\">[</span>25<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRc\">]</span></span></a></sup> situations, events, states, and time;<sup about=\"#mwt94\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-29\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-29\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-29\" id=\"mwDRg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDRk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRo\">[</span>26<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDRs\">]</span></span></a></sup> causes and effects;<sup about=\"#mwt97\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-30\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-30\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-30\" id=\"mwDRw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDR0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDR4\">[</span>27<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDR8\">]</span></span></a></sup> knowledge about knowledge (what we know about what other people know);<sup about=\"#mwt101\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-31\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-31\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-31\" id=\"mwDSA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDSE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDSI\">[</span>28<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDSM\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Default_reasoning\" title=\"Default reasoning\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDSQ\">default reasoning</a> (things humans assume are true until they are told differently and will remain true even when other facts are changing);<sup about=\"#mwt107\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Default_reasoning_32-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Default reasoning\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Default_reasoning-32\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Default_reasoning-32\" id=\"mwDSU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDSY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDSc\">[</span>29<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDSg\">]</span></span></a></sup> and many other aspects and domains of knowledge.</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-37\" id=\"cite_note-37\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"e\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDSk\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-37\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDSo\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDSs\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-37\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Knowledge acquistion is among the reasons that <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Expert_system\" title=\"Expert system\" id=\"mwDSw\">expert systems</a> proved to be inefficient for capturing knowledge.<sup about=\"#mwt122\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTENewquist1994296_35-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTENewquist1994296\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENewquist1994296-35\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTENewquist1994296-35\" id=\"mwDS0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDS4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDS8\">[</span>31<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDTA\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt124\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECrevier1993204–208_36-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTECrevier1993204–208\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECrevier1993204–208-36\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTECrevier1993204–208-36\" id=\"mwDTE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDTI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDTM\">[</span>32<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDTQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-38\" id=\"cite_note-38\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"f\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDTU\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-38\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDTY\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDTc\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-38\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">\"Rational agent\" is general term used in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Economics\" title=\"Economics\" id=\"mwDTg\">economics</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Philosophy\" title=\"Philosophy\" id=\"mwDTk\">philosophy</a> and theoretical artificial intelligence. It can refer to anything that directs its behaviour to accomplish goals, such as a person, an animal, a corporation, a nation, or in the case of AI, a computer program.\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-52\" id=\"cite_note-52\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"g\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDTo\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-52\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDTs\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDTw\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-52\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Turing\" title=\"Alan Turing\" id=\"mwDT0\">Alan Turing</a> discussed the centrality of learning as early as 1950, in his classic paper \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Computing_Machinery_and_Intelligence\" title=\"Computing Machinery and Intelligence\" id=\"mwDT4\">Computing Machinery and Intelligence</a>\".<sup about=\"#mwt163\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTETuring1950_50-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTETuring1950\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTETuring1950-50\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTETuring1950-50\" id=\"mwDT8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDUA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDUE\">[</span>44<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDUI\">]</span></span></a></sup> In 1956, at the original Dartmouth AI summer conference, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Ray_Solomonoff\" title=\"Ray Solomonoff\" id=\"mwDUM\">Ray Solomonoff</a> wrote a report on unsupervised probabilistic machine learning: \"An Inductive Inference Machine\".<sup about=\"#mwt165\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESolomonoff1956_51-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESolomonoff1956\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESolomonoff1956-51\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESolomonoff1956-51\" id=\"mwDUQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDUU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDUY\">[</span>45<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDUc\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-61\" id=\"cite_note-61\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"h\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDUg\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-61\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDUk\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDUo\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-61\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">See <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AI_winter#Machine_translation_and_the_ALPAC_report_of_1966\" title=\"AI winter\" id=\"mwDUs\">AI winter §<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDUw\">\\xa0</span>Machine translation and the ALPAC report of 1966</a>.</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-106\" id=\"cite_note-106\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"i\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDU0\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-106\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDU4\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDU8\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-106\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Compared with symbolic logic, formal Bayesian inference is computationally expensive. For inference to be tractable, most observations must be <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Conditionally_independent\" title=\"Conditionally independent\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDVA\">conditionally independent</a> of one another. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/AdSense\" title=\"AdSense\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDVE\">AdSense</a> uses a Bayesian network with over 300<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDVI\">\\xa0</span>million edges to learn which ads to serve.<sup about=\"#mwt344\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015chpt._6_105-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEDomingos2015chpt. 6\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015chpt._6-105\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015chpt._6-105\" id=\"mwDVM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDVQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDVU\">[</span>97<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDVY\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-109\" id=\"cite_note-109\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"j\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDVc\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-109\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDVg\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDVk\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-109\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Expectation–maximisation, one of the most popular algorithms in machine learning, allows clustering in the presence of unknown <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Latent_variables\" title=\"Latent variables\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDVo\">latent variables</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt350\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015210_108-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEDomingos2015210\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015210-108\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEDomingos2015210-108\" id=\"mwDVs\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDVw\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDV0\">[</span>99<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDV4\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-136\" id=\"cite_note-136\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"k\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDV8\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-136\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDWA\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDWE\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-136\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Some form of deep neural networks (without a specific learning algorithm) were described by:\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Warren_S._McCulloch\" title=\"Warren S. McCulloch\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDWI\">Warren S. McCulloch</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Walter_Pitts\" title=\"Walter Pitts\" id=\"mwDWM\">Walter Pitts</a> (1943);<sup about=\"#mwt436\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117_130-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117-130\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117-130\" id=\"mwDWQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDWU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDWY\">[</span>120<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDWc\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alan_Turing\" title=\"Alan Turing\" id=\"mwDWg\">Alan Turing</a> (1948);<sup about=\"#mwt438\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785_131-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\" id=\"mwDWk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDWo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDWs\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDWw\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Karl_Steinbuch\" title=\"Karl Steinbuch\" id=\"mwDW0\">Karl Steinbuch</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Roger_David_Joseph?action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Roger David Joseph (page does not exist)\" class=\"new\" typeof=\"mw:LocalizedAttrs\" id=\"mwDW4\" data-mw-i18n=\\'{\"title\":{\"lang\":\"x-page\",\"key\":\"red-link-title\",\"params\":[\"Roger David Joseph\"]}}\\'>Roger David Joseph</a> (1961).<sup about=\"#mwt440\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._5_132-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect. 5\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._5-132\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._5-132\" id=\"mwDW8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDXA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXE\">[</span>122<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXI\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nDeep or recurrent networks that learned (or used gradient descent) were developed by:\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Frank_Rosenblatt\" title=\"Frank Rosenblatt\" id=\"mwDXM\">Frank Rosenblatt</a> (1957);<sup about=\"#mwt442\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785_131-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\" id=\"mwDXQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDXU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXY\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXc\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Oliver_Selfridge\" title=\"Oliver Selfridge\" id=\"mwDXg\">Oliver Selfridge</a> (1959);<sup about=\"#mwt444\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._5_132-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect. 5\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._5-132\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._5-132\" id=\"mwDXk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDXo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXs\">[</span>122<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDXw\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Alexey_Ivakhnenko\" title=\"Alexey Ivakhnenko\" id=\"mwDX0\">Alexey Ivakhnenko</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Valentin_Lapa?action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Valentin Lapa (page does not exist)\" class=\"new\" typeof=\"mw:LocalizedAttrs\" id=\"mwDX4\" data-mw-i18n=\\'{\"title\":{\"lang\":\"x-page\",\"key\":\"red-link-title\",\"params\":[\"Valentin Lapa\"]}}\\'>Valentin Lapa</a> (1965);<sup about=\"#mwt446\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._6_133-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect. 6\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._6-133\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._6-133\" id=\"mwDX8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDYA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYE\">[</span>123<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYI\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Kaoru_Nakano?action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" title=\"Kaoru Nakano (page does not exist)\" class=\"new\" typeof=\"mw:LocalizedAttrs\" id=\"mwDYM\" data-mw-i18n=\\'{\"title\":{\"lang\":\"x-page\",\"key\":\"red-link-title\",\"params\":[\"Kaoru Nakano\"]}}\\'>Kaoru Nakano</a> (1971);<sup about=\"#mwt448\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7_134-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect. 7\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7-134\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7-134\" id=\"mwDYQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDYU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYY\">[</span>124<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYc\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Shun-Ichi_Amari\" title=\"Shun-Ichi Amari\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDYg\">Shun-Ichi Amari</a> (1972); <sup about=\"#mwt450\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7_134-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect. 7\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7-134\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7-134\" id=\"mwDYk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDYo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYs\">[</span>124<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDYw\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/John_Joseph_Hopfield\" title=\"John Joseph Hopfield\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDY0\">John Joseph Hopfield</a> (1982).<sup about=\"#mwt452\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7_134-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect. 7\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7-134\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._7-134\" id=\"mwDY4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDY8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZA\">[</span>124<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZE\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nPrecursors to backpropagation were developed by:\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henry_J._Kelley\" title=\"Henry J. Kelley\" id=\"mwDZI\">Henry J. Kelley</a> (1960);<sup about=\"#mwt454\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785_131-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\" id=\"mwDZM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDZQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZU\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZY\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arthur_E._Bryson\" title=\"Arthur E. Bryson\" id=\"mwDZc\">Arthur E. Bryson</a> (1962);<sup about=\"#mwt456\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785_131-3\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\" id=\"mwDZg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDZk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZo\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZs\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_Dreyfus\" title=\"Stuart Dreyfus\" id=\"mwDZw\">Stuart Dreyfus</a> (1962);<sup about=\"#mwt458\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785_131-4\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\" id=\"mwDZ0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDZ4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDZ8\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDaA\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arthur_E._Bryson\" title=\"Arthur E. Bryson\" id=\"mwDaE\">Arthur E. Bryson</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Yu-Chi_Ho\" title=\"Yu-Chi Ho\" id=\"mwDaI\">Yu-Chi Ho</a> (1969).<sup about=\"#mwt460\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785_131-5\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\" id=\"mwDaM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDaQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDaU\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDaY\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\nBackpropagation was independently developed by:\\n<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Seppo_Linnainmaa\" title=\"Seppo Linnainmaa\" id=\"mwDac\">Seppo Linnainmaa</a> (1970);<sup about=\"#mwt462\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._8_135-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect. 8\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._8-135\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESchmidhuber2022sect._8-135\" id=\"mwDag\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDak\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDao\">[</span>125<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDas\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Paul_Werbos\" title=\"Paul Werbos\" id=\"mwDaw\">Paul Werbos</a> (1974).<sup about=\"#mwt464\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785_131-6\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021785-131\" id=\"mwDa0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDa4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDa8\">[</span>121<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbA\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-138\" id=\"cite_note-138\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"l\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDbE\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-138\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDbI\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDbM\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-138\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Geoffrey_Hinton\" title=\"Geoffrey Hinton\" id=\"mwDbQ\">Geoffrey Hinton</a> said, of his work on neural networks in the 1990s, \"our labeled datasets were thousands of times too small. [And] our computers were millions of times too slow.\"<sup about=\"#mwt485\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-137\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-137\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-137\" id=\"mwDbU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDbY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbc\">[</span>126<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDbg\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-262\" id=\"cite_note-262\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"m\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDbk\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-262\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDbo\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDbs\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-262\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">In statistics, a <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bias_(statistics)\" title=\"Bias (statistics)\" id=\"mwDbw\">bias</a> is a systematic error or deviation from the correct value. But in the context of <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Fairness_(machine_learning)\" title=\"Fairness (machine learning)\" id=\"mwDb0\">fairness</a>, it refers to a tendency in favour or against a certain group or individual characteristic, usually in a way that is considered unfair or harmful. A statistically unbiased AI system that produces disparate outcomes for different demographic groups may thus be viewed as biased in the ethical sense.<sup about=\"#mwt931\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-Samuel-2022_261-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"name\":\"Samuel-2022\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-Samuel-2022-261\" id=\"mwDb4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDb8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDcA\">[</span>249<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDcE\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-273\" id=\"cite_note-273\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"n\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDcI\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-273\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDcM\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDcQ\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-273\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Including <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Jon_Kleinberg\" title=\"Jon Kleinberg\" id=\"mwDcU\">Jon Kleinberg</a> (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Cornell_University\" title=\"Cornell University\" id=\"mwDcY\">Cornell University</a>), Sendhil Mullainathan (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/University_of_Chicago\" title=\"University of Chicago\" id=\"mwDcc\">University of Chicago</a>), Cynthia Chouldechova (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Carnegie_Mellon\" title=\"Carnegie Mellon\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDcg\">Carnegie Mellon</a>) and Sam Corbett-Davis (<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stanford\" title=\"Stanford\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDck\">Stanford</a>)<sup about=\"#mwt969\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEChristian202067–70_272-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEChristian202067–70\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202067–70-272\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEChristian202067–70-272\" id=\"mwDco\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDcs\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDcw\">[</span>259<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDc0\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-279\" id=\"cite_note-279\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"o\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDc4\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-279\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDc8\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDdA\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-279\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Moritz Hardt (a director at the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Max_Planck_Institute_for_Intelligent_Systems\" title=\"Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems\" id=\"mwDdE\">Max Planck Institute for Intelligent Systems</a>) argues that machine learning \"is fundamentally the wrong tool for a lot of domains, where you\\'re trying to design interventions and mechanisms that change the world.\"<sup about=\"#mwt986\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-278\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-278\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-278\" id=\"mwDdI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDdM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDdQ\">[</span>264<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDdU\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-288\" id=\"cite_note-288\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"p\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDdY\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-288\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDdc\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDdg\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-288\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">When the law was passed in 2018, it still contained a form of this provision.</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-297\" id=\"cite_note-297\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"q\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDdk\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-297\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDdo\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDds\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-297\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">This is the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/United_Nations\" title=\"United Nations\" id=\"mwDdw\">United Nations</a>\\' definition, and includes things like <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Land_mines\" title=\"Land mines\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDd0\">land mines</a> as well.<sup about=\"#mwt1053\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021989_296-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021989\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021989-296\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig2021989-296\" id=\"mwDd4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDd8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDeA\">[</span>280<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDeE\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-309\" id=\"cite_note-309\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"r\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDeI\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-309\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDeM\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDeQ\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-309\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">See table 4; 9% is both the OECD average and the U.S. average.<sup about=\"#mwt1091\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEArntzGregoryZierahn201633_308-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEArntzGregoryZierahn201633\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEArntzGregoryZierahn201633-308\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEArntzGregoryZierahn201633-308\" id=\"mwDeU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDeY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDec\">[</span>291<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDeg\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-326\" id=\"cite_note-326\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"s\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDek\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-326\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDeo\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDes\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-326\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Sometimes called a \"<a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Robopocalypse\" title=\"Robopocalypse\" id=\"mwDew\">robopocalypse</a>\"<sup about=\"#mwt1153\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211001_325-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211001\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211001-325\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211001-325\" id=\"mwDe0\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDe4\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDe8\">[</span>307<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfA\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-390\" id=\"cite_note-390\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"t\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDfE\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-390\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDfI\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDfM\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-390\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">\"Electronic brain\" was the term used by the press around this time.<sup about=\"#mwt1375\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219_387-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219-387\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20219-387\" id=\"mwDfQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDfU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfY\">[</span>368<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfc\">]</span></span></a></sup><sup about=\"#mwt1379\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-389\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-389\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-389\" id=\"mwDfg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDfk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfo\">[</span>370<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDfs\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-394\" id=\"cite_note-394\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"u\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDfw\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-394\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDf0\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDf4\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-394\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Daniel Crevier wrote, \"the conference is generally recognized as the official birthdate of the new science.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1401\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECrevier199347–49_393-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTECrevier199347–49\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECrevier199347–49-393\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTECrevier199347–49-393\" id=\"mwDf8\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDgA\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgE\">[</span>373<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgI\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwDgM\">Russell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norvig\" title=\"Norvig\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDgQ\">Norvig</a> called the conference \"the inception of artificial intelligence.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1403\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117_130-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117-130\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202117-130\" id=\"mwDgU\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDgY\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgc\">[</span>120<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDgg\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-396\" id=\"cite_note-396\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"v\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDgk\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-396\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDgo\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDgs\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-396\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwDgw\">Russell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norvig\" title=\"Norvig\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDg0\">Norvig</a> wrote \"for the next 20 years the field would be dominated by these people and their students.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1410\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200317_395-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200317\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200317-395\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200317-395\" id=\"mwDg4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDg8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDhA\">[</span>374<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDhE\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-398\" id=\"cite_note-398\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"w\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDhI\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-398\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDhM\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDhQ\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-398\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwDhU\">Russell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norvig\" title=\"Norvig\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDhY\">Norvig</a> wrote, \"it was astonishing whenever a computer did anything kind of smartish\".<sup about=\"#mwt1416\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200318_397-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200318\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200318-397\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig200318-397\" id=\"mwDhc\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDhg\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDhk\">[</span>375<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDho\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-399\" id=\"cite_note-399\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"x\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDhs\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-399\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDhw\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDh0\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-399\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">The programs described are <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Arthur_Samuel_(computer_scientist)\" title=\"Arthur Samuel (computer scientist)\" id=\"mwDh4\">Arthur Samuel</a>\\'s checkers program for the <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/IBM_701\" title=\"IBM 701\" id=\"mwDh8\">IBM 701</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Daniel_Bobrow\" title=\"Daniel Bobrow\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDiA\">Daniel Bobrow</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/STUDENT\" title=\"STUDENT\" id=\"mwDiE\">STUDENT</a>, <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Allen_Newell\" title=\"Allen Newell\" id=\"mwDiI\">Newell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Herbert_A._Simon\" title=\"Herbert A. Simon\" id=\"mwDiM\">Simon</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Logic_Theorist\" title=\"Logic Theorist\" id=\"mwDiQ\">Logic Theorist</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Terry_Winograd\" title=\"Terry Winograd\" id=\"mwDiU\">Terry Winograd</a>\\'s <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/SHRDLU\" title=\"SHRDLU\" id=\"mwDiY\">SHRDLU</a>.\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-404\" id=\"cite_note-404\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"y\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDic\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-404\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDig\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDik\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-404\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwDio\">Russell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norvig\" title=\"Norvig\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDis\">Norvig</a> wrote: \"in almost all cases, these early systems failed on more difficult problems\".<sup about=\"#mwt1439\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202121_403-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202121\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202121-403\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig202121-403\" id=\"mwDiw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDi0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDi4\">[</span>379<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDi8\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-415\" id=\"cite_note-415\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"z\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDjA\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-415\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDjE\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDjI\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-415\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Embodied_mind\" title=\"Embodied mind\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDjM\">Embodied</a> approaches to AI<sup about=\"#mwt1491\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004454–462_411-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004454–462\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004454–462-411\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMcCorduck2004454–462-411\" id=\"mwDjQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDjU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDjY\">[</span>386<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDjc\">]</span></span></a></sup> were championed by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Hans_Moravec\" title=\"Hans Moravec\" id=\"mwDjg\">Hans Moravec</a><sup about=\"#mwt1493\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEMoravec1988_412-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEMoravec1988\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEMoravec1988-412\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEMoravec1988-412\" id=\"mwDjk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDjo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDjs\">[</span>387<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDjw\">]</span></span></a></sup> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rodney_Brooks\" title=\"Rodney Brooks\" id=\"mwDj0\">Rodney Brooks</a><sup about=\"#mwt1495\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooks1990_413-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEBrooks1990\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooks1990-413\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooks1990-413\" id=\"mwDj4\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDj8\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDkA\">[</span>388<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDkE\">]</span></span></a></sup> and went by many names: <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nouvelle_AI\" title=\"Nouvelle AI\" id=\"mwDkI\">Nouvelle AI</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1497\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEBrooks1990_413-1\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEBrooks1990\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooks1990-413\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEBrooks1990-413\" id=\"mwDkM\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDkQ\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDkU\">[</span>388<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDkY\">]</span></span></a></sup> <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Developmental_robotics\" title=\"Developmental robotics\" id=\"mwDkc\">Developmental robotics</a>.<sup about=\"#mwt1503\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-414\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-414\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-414\" id=\"mwDkg\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDkk\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDko\">[</span>389<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDks\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-422\" id=\"cite_note-422\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"aa\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDkw\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-422\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDk0\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDk4\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-422\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Matteo Wong wrote in <i id=\"mwDk8\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/The_Atlantic\" title=\"The Atlantic\" id=\"mwDlA\">The Atlantic</a></i>: \"Whereas for decades, computer-science fields such as natural-language processing, computer vision, and robotics used extremely different methods, now they all use a programming method called \"deep learning\". As a result, their code and approaches have become more similar, and their models are easier to integrate into one another.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1535\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEWong2023_421-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEWong2023\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEWong2023-421\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEWong2023-421\" id=\"mwDlE\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDlI\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDlM\">[</span>395<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDlQ\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-428\" id=\"cite_note-428\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"ab\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDlU\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-428\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDlY\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDlc\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-428\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Jack Clark wrote in <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bloomberg_News\" title=\"Bloomberg News\" id=\"mwDlg\">Bloomberg</a>: \"After a half-decade of quiet breakthroughs in artificial intelligence, 2015 has been a landmark year. Computers are smarter and learning faster than ever\", and noted that the number of software projects that use machine learning at <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Google\" title=\"Google\" id=\"mwDlk\">Google</a> increased from a \"sporadic usage\" in 2012 to more than 2,700 projects in 2015.<sup about=\"#mwt1557\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTEClark2015b_424-2\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTEClark2015b\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTEClark2015b-424\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTEClark2015b-424\" id=\"mwDlo\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDls\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDlw\">[</span>397<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDl0\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-453\" id=\"cite_note-453\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"ac\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDl4\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-453\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDl8\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDmA\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-453\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nils_Nilsson_(researcher)\" title=\"Nils Nilsson (researcher)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDmE\">Nils Nilsson</a> wrote in 1983: \"Simply put, there is wide disagreement in the field about what AI is all about.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1656\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTENilsson198310_452-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTENilsson198310\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTENilsson198310-452\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTENilsson198310-452\" id=\"mwDmI\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDmM\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDmQ\">[</span>424<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDmU\">]</span></span></a></sup></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-459\" id=\"cite_note-459\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"ad\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDmY\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-459\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDmc\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDmg\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-459\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Daniel Crevier wrote that \"time has proven the accuracy and perceptiveness of some of Dreyfus\\'s comments. Had he formulated them less aggressively, constructive actions they suggested might have been taken much earlier.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1669\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTECrevier1993125_458-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTECrevier1993125\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTECrevier1993125-458\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTECrevier1993125-458\" id=\"mwDmk\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDmo\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDms\">[</span>429<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDmw\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-Searle\\'s_strong_AI-473\" id=\"cite_note-Searle\\'s_strong_AI-473\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"ae\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDm0\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-Searle\\'s_strong_AI_473-0\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDm4\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDm8\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-Searle\\'s_strong_AI-473\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\" data-mw-group=\"lower-alpha\">Searle presented this definition of \"Strong AI\" in 1999.<sup about=\"#mwt1734\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESearle1999_470-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESearle1999\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESearle1999-470\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESearle1999-470\" id=\"mwDnA\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDnE\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDnI\">[</span>440<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDnM\">]</span></span></a></sup> Searle\\'s original formulation was \"The appropriately programmed computer really is a mind, in the sense that computers given the right programs can be literally said to understand and have other cognitive states.\"<sup about=\"#mwt1736\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTESearle19801_471-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTESearle19801\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTESearle19801-471\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTESearle19801-471\" id=\"mwDnQ\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDnU\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDnY\">[</span>441<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDnc\">]</span></span></a></sup> Strong AI is defined similarly by <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Stuart_J._Russell\" title=\"Stuart J. Russell\" id=\"mwDng\">Russell</a> and <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Norvig\" title=\"Norvig\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwDnk\">Norvig</a>: \"Strong AI – the assertion that machines that do so are <i id=\"mwDno\">actually</i> consciously thinking (as opposed to <i id=\"mwDns\">simulating</i> thinking).\"<sup about=\"#mwt1738\" class=\"mw-ref reference\" id=\"cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211032_472-0\" rel=\"dc:references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/ref\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"ref\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"name\":\"FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211032\"},\"body\":{\"id\":\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211032-472\"}}\\'><a href=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211032-472\" id=\"mwDnw\"><span class=\"mw-reflink-text\" id=\"mwDn0\"><span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDn4\">[</span>442<span class=\"cite-bracket\" id=\"mwDn8\">]</span></span></a></sup>\\n</span></li>\\n</ol></div></div>\\n\\n</section><section data-mw-section-id=\"70\" id=\"mwDoA\" aria-labelledby=\"References\"><div class=\"mw-heading mw-heading2\"><h2 id=\"References\">References</h2></div>\\n<span class=\"mw-empty-elt\" about=\"#mwt1843\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwDoE\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Reflist\",\"href\":\"./Template:Reflist\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"23em\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1327269900\" about=\"#mwt1844\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Reflist/styles.css\"}}\\'/></span><div class=\"mw-references-wrap mw-references-columns\" style=\"column-width: calc( 0.9 * 23em );\" about=\"#mwt1843\" id=\"mwDoI\"><ol class=\"mw-references references\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/references\" about=\"#mwt1845\" id=\"mwDoM\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"references\",\"attrs\":{\"group\":\"\",\"responsive\":\"0\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"}}\\'><li about=\"#cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\" id=\"cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"1\"><span rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDoQ\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4_1-0\" id=\"mwDoU\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDoY\">1</span></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4_1-1\" id=\"mwDoc\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDog\">2</span></a> <a href=\"#cite_ref-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4_1-2\" id=\"mwDok\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDoo\">3</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-FOOTNOTERussellNorvig20211–4-1\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFRussellNorvig2021\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDos\">Russell <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDow\">&amp;</span> Norvig (2021)</a>, pp.<span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDo0\">\\xa0</span>1–4.</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-4\" id=\"cite_note-4\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"2\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDo4\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-4\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDo8\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDpA\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-4\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\"><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"#CITEREFRussellNorvig2021\" about=\"#mwt21\" typeof=\"mw:Transclusion\" class=\"mw-selflink-fragment\" id=\"mwDpE\" data-mw=\\'{\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"Harvtxt\",\"href\":\"./Template:Harvtxt\"},\"params\":{\"1\":{\"wt\":\"Russell\"},\"2\":{\"wt\":\"Norvig\"},\"3\":{\"wt\":\"2021\"},\"loc\":{\"wt\":\"§1.2\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'>Russell <span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwDpI\">&amp;</span> Norvig (2021</a><span about=\"#mwt21\" id=\"mwDpM\">, §1.2)</span>.</span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-5\" id=\"cite_note-5\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"3\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwDpQ\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-5\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwDpU\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwDpY\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-5\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\"><style data-mw-deduplicate=\"TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" about=\"#mwt23\" id=\"mwDpc\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":