rence-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" about=\"#mwt1132\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwGhs\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"cite book \",\"href\":\"./Template:Cite_book\"},\"params\":{\"last1\":{\"wt\":\"Reeves\"},\"first1\":{\"wt\":\"Byron\"},\"last2\":{\"wt\":\"Nass\"},\"first2\":{\"wt\":\"Clifford\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"The Media Equation: How People Treat Computers, Television, and New Media Like Real People and Places\"},\"publisher\":{\"wt\":\"Cambridge University Press\"},\"location\":{\"wt\":\"New York\"},\"year\":{\"wt\":\"1996\"},\"isbn\":{\"wt\":\"978-1-57586-053-4\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'/><cite id=\"CITEREFReevesNass1996\" class=\"citation book cs1\" about=\"#mwt1132\">Reeves, Byron; Nass, Clifford (1996). <i id=\"mwGhw\">The Media Equation: How People Treat Computers, Television, and New Media Like Real People and Places</i>. New York: Cambridge University Press. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/ISBN_(identifier)\" title=\"ISBN (identifier)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwGh0\">ISBN</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwGh4\">\\xa0</span><a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Special:BookSources/978-1-57586-053-4\" title=\"Special:BookSources/978-1-57586-053-4\" id=\"mwGh8\"><bdi id=\"mwGiA\">978-1-57586-053-4</bdi></a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Abook&amp;rft.genre=book&amp;rft.btitle=The+Media+Equation%3A+How+People+Treat+Computers%2C+Television%2C+and+New+Media+Like+Real+People+and+Places&amp;rft.place=New+York&amp;rft.pub=Cambridge+University+Press&amp;rft.date=1996&amp;rft.isbn=978-1-57586-053-4&amp;rft.aulast=Reeves&amp;rft.aufirst=Byron&amp;rft.au=Nass%2C+Clifford&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AArtificial+intelligence\" class=\"Z3988\" about=\"#mwt1132\" id=\"mwGiE\"></span></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-NassMoon2000-320\" id=\"cite_note-NassMoon2000-320\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"302\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwGiI\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-NassMoon2000_320-0\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwGiM\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwGiQ\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-NassMoon2000-320\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" about=\"#mwt1135\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwGiU\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"cite journal \",\"href\":\"./Template:Cite_journal\"},\"params\":{\"last1\":{\"wt\":\"Nass\"},\"first1\":{\"wt\":\"Clifford\"},\"last2\":{\"wt\":\"Moon\"},\"first2\":{\"wt\":\"Youngme\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"Machines and mindlessness: Social responses to computers\"},\"journal\":{\"wt\":\"Journal of Social Issues\"},\"volume\":{\"wt\":\"56\"},\"issue\":{\"wt\":\"1\"},\"year\":{\"wt\":\"2000\"},\"pages\":{\"wt\":\"81–103\"},\"doi\":{\"wt\":\"10.1111/0022-4537.00153\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'/><cite id=\"CITEREFNassMoon2000\" class=\"citation journal cs1\" about=\"#mwt1135\">Nass, Clifford; Moon, Youngme (2000). \"Machines and mindlessness: Social responses to computers\". <i id=\"mwGiY\">Journal of Social Issues</i>. <b id=\"mwGic\">56</b> (1): <span class=\"nowrap\" id=\"mwGig\">81–</span>103. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwGik\">doi</a>:<a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1111%2F0022-4537.00153\" class=\"external text\" id=\"mwGio\">10.1111/0022-4537.00153</a>.</cite><span title=\"ctx_ver=Z39.88-2004&amp;rft_val_fmt=info%3Aofi%2Ffmt%3Akev%3Amtx%3Ajournal&amp;rft.genre=article&amp;rft.jtitle=Journal+of+Social+Issues&amp;rft.atitle=Machines+and+mindlessness%3A+Social+responses+to+computers&amp;rft.volume=56&amp;rft.issue=1&amp;rft.pages=81-103&amp;rft.date=2000&amp;rft_id=info%3Adoi%2F10.1111%2F0022-4537.00153&amp;rft.aulast=Nass&amp;rft.aufirst=Clifford&amp;rft.au=Moon%2C+Youngme&amp;rfr_id=info%3Asid%2Fen.wikipedia.org%3AArtificial+intelligence\" class=\"Z3988\" about=\"#mwt1135\" id=\"mwGis\"></span></span></li>\\n<li about=\"#cite_note-321\" id=\"cite_note-321\" data-mw-footnote-number=\"303\"><span class=\"mw-cite-backlink\" id=\"mwGiw\"><a href=\"#cite_ref-321\" rel=\"mw:referencedBy\" id=\"mwGi0\"><span class=\"mw-linkback-text\" id=\"mwGi4\">↑</span></a></span> <span id=\"mw-reference-text-cite_note-321\" class=\"mw-reference-text reference-text\"><link rel=\"mw-deduplicated-inline-style\" href=\"mw-data:TemplateStyles:r1333433106\" about=\"#mwt1138\" typeof=\"mw:Extension/templatestyles mw:Transclusion\" id=\"mwGi8\" data-mw=\\'{\"name\":\"templatestyles\",\"attrs\":{\"src\":\"Module:Citation/CS1/styles.css\"},\"body\":{\"extsrc\":\"\"},\"parts\":[{\"template\":{\"target\":{\"wt\":\"cite journal \",\"href\":\"./Template:Cite_journal\"},\"params\":{\"author1\":{\"wt\":\"Salles, Arleen\"},\"author2\":{\"wt\":\"Evers, Kathinka\"},\"author3\":{\"wt\":\"Farisco, Michele\"},\"title\":{\"wt\":\"Anthropomorphism in AI\"},\"journal\":{\"wt\":\"AJOB Neuroscience\"},\"date\":{\"wt\":\"2020\"},\"volume\":{\"wt\":\"2020 Vol 11\"},\"issue\":{\"wt\":\"2\"},\"pages\":{\"wt\":\"88–95\"},\"doi\":{\"wt\":\"10.1080/21507740.2020.1740350\"},\"pmid\":{\"wt\":\"32228388\"},\"url\":{\"wt\":\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/21507740.2020.1740350\"},\"quote\":{\"wt\":\"\\\\\"An additional concern is that socialization with entities that are not truly social, even if designed to offer new tools for enriching users&apos; emotional life and even if beneficial in some specific cases (for example, when enhancing the well-being of those who would otherwise be social outcasts) is not truly meaningful and it can only limitedly replace the richness of human interactions.... Another common objection to anthropomorphism by design is that it is deceptive insofar as it would appear that in order to meet specific, e.g. emotional or social needs, AI must actually \\\\\"fool\\\\\" users by making them believe that they have the capacity to engage emotionally\\\\\"\"}},\"i\":0}}]}\\'/><cite id=\"CITEREFSalles,_ArleenEvers,_KathinkaFarisco,_Michele2020\" class=\"citation journal cs1 cs1-prop-long-vol\" about=\"#mwt1138\">Salles, Arleen; Evers, Kathinka; Farisco, Michele (2020). <a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://www.tandfonline.com/doi/pdf/10.1080/21507740.2020.1740350\" class=\"external text\" id=\"mwGjA\">\"Anthropomorphism in AI\"</a>. <i id=\"mwGjE\">AJOB Neuroscience</i>. 2020 Vol 11 (2): <span class=\"nowrap\" id=\"mwGjI\">88–</span>95. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Doi_(identifier)\" title=\"Doi (identifier)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwGjM\">doi</a>:<a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://doi.org/10.1080%2F21507740.2020.1740350\" class=\"external text\" id=\"mwGjQ\">10.1080/21507740.2020.1740350</a>. <a rel=\"mw:WikiLink\" href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/PMID_(identifier)\" title=\"PMID (identifier)\" class=\"mw-redirect\" id=\"mwGjU\">PMID</a><span typeof=\"mw:Entity\" id=\"mwGjY\">\\xa0</span><a rel=\"mw:ExtLink nofollow\" href=\"https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/32228388\" class=\"external text\" id=\"mwGjc\">32228388</a>. <q id=\"mwGjg\">An additional concern is that socialization with entities that are not truly social, even if designed to offer new tools for enriching users\\' emotional life and even if beneficial in some specific cases (for example, when enhancing the well-being of those who would otherwise be social outcasts) is not truly meaningful and it can only limitedly replace the richness of human interactions.... 